{"_id":"012e25d29a7cadf7","name":"Kaio Healing","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you take a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of <strong>HP</strong> equal to <em>Proficinecy Bonus</em> x 10. You may, as an Action on your turn, place your hand on a creature and heal them any number of <strong>HP</strong> in your pool that you choose.</p>\n<p>You may increase this pool by 5 <strong>HP</strong> for the cost of one <strong>Training Boon.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kaio-healing","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Supreme Kai"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3665,"endLine":3669}}}}
{"_id":"018c719a79fa72cd","name":"Ability score improvement/ Feat","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach <strong>4th Level</strong>, and again at <strong>8th, 12th, 16th,</strong> and <strong>19th Level</strong>, you have 3 points to distribute into your <strong>Ability Scores</strong>. You can't increase an <strong>Ability Score</strong> above your <em>Ability Score Maximum</em> using this feature. Alternatively, you may instead gain a <strong>Feat</strong> for the cost of 2 points.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-ability-score-improvement-feat","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3181,"endLine":3183},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"01ace745ece8494d","name":"Crushing Strength","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your incredible strength places you beyond others in raw might.\nYou can use a d6 in place of your <em>Unarmed Strike's Damage Dice</em>. This die increases as you gain <strong>Bruiser Levels</strong>, as shown on the table above.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-crushing-strength","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2993,"endLine":2995},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"01d381b4e5d79268","name":"Metamorian Fusion Dance","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The fusion method made by the Metamorians. This is considered a rank 2 <em><strong>Technique</strong></em>. You do not have proficiency in this technique when you first learn it. You must wait 1 hour before you may use this technique again.</p>\n<p>As an action on your turn you may initiate the <em>Fusion Dance</em> with a willing character capable of using it within 5 feet of you. Both participants must make Dexterity (Performance) checks to properly do the fusion dance. If both participants roll above a 15 then the fusion is a success. When you fuse you gain the <em>Fusion Tag</em> and add all <strong>Class Features, Racial Features, Trained Features, Customization Options, Techniques/Spells,</strong> and <strong>Transformations</strong> of both participants. <em>Movement Speed</em>, <strong>HP, Stamina,</strong> and <strong>Ki</strong> calculation are directly dependent on the <em>Skill Check</em> results</p>\n<ul>\n<li>For a successful Performance check you succeed in your half of the Fusion Dance:<ul>\n<li>The Fusion gains a +2 <strong>Power Bonus</strong> upon completion</li>\n<li>You add half of your base <em>Movement Speed</em> to the <em>Fusion</em> upon completion</li>\n<li>You add your <strong>Maximum HP, Ki,</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong> to the <em>Fusion</em> upon completion</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For a failed Performance check you misjudged your half of the Fusion Dance:<ul>\n<li>The Fusion gains a -2 <strong>Power Bonus</strong> upon completion</li>\n<li>You add half of your base <em>Movement Speed</em> to the <em>Fusion</em> upon completion</li>\n<li>You add half your <strong>Maximum HP, Ki,</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong> to the <em>Fusion</em> upon completion</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Regardless of the <em>Performance Check</em> successes both fusees must designate 3 of their <strong>Ability Scores</strong>, with no overlap, to be used for the fusion. Anytime you fuse with that individual again using the <em>Fusing Dance</em> you will assume this specific <em>Fusion</em>.</p>\n<p>Fusion requires 3 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong>. The Fusion ends when the fused characters Stamina reaches 0. When the <em>Fusion</em> ends damage taken and <strong>Ki</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong> used is split as evenly as possible and distributed between the fusees.</p>\n<p>In the event that a <em>Metamorian Fusion</em> hits 0 <strong>HP</strong>, they defuse and both participants begin making <em>Death Saving Throws</em></p>\n<h6>Metamorian Equipment</h6>\n<p>When 2 characters fuse using this method, unlike a true fusing of equipment like with the <em>Potara Earrings</em>, a <em>Metamorian Fusion</em> has all <em>Armor</em> replaced with clothes in the Metamorian style. You may choose what <em>Weapons</em> you had prior to the fusion to keep and which get melded into your form for the duration of the <em>Fusion.</em></p>\n<h6>Limitations</h6>\n<p>Characters may only fuse with this method if they are of the same size category and no more than 1 <strong>Character Level</strong> apart.</p>\n<h6>No one's Trained!</h6>\n<p>The <em>Fusion Dance</em> is a unique ability in that anyone of <strong>Ki Rank 2</strong> or higher can use this feature. So long as someone who knows it is present and capable of instructing you for at least 1 hour you may use the fusion dance with Disadvantage for the next 24 hours.</p>\n<p>If the instructor is present for the attempt to instruct you then roll without disadvantage.</p>\n<h6>Self Taught! Kinda....</h6>\n<p>Due to the strange nature of this feature it is possible for 2 people to be instructed on how to use this feature and then have a <strong>Training Arc with a Partner</strong> together to fully learn the feature together for the cost of 2 Training Boons each.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you may have a <strong>Training Arc with a Partner</strong> together with someone that knows the <em>Fusion Dance</em> and gain advantage on <em>Fusion Dances</em> with that person for 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong> each.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"metamorian-fusion-dance","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":2,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Metamoran"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3530,"endLine":3581}}}}
{"_id":"0206eeb275222b0c","name":"Like the Wind","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are taking the <em>Dash Action</em> you are unaffected by <em>Difficult Terrain</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"speedster-like-the-wind","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2227,"endLine":2230},"contentCategory":"subraceFeature","grantedBy":"Speedster"}}}
{"_id":"02d9c032622077f6","name":"Saiyans","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Strength or Dexterity</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You where created with the cells of the prideful warrior race. You gain the saiyans ability to bounce back from near death. Whenever you fail a death saving throw roll a d20 check with a DC starting at 8, increasing by 2 each time you succeed. On a Successful check you gain 1 training boon. You may use this boon immedietly or as soon as you regain conciousness for the chance at a second zenkai boost. You also gain access to the super saiyan transformation up to super saiyan 2.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-saiyans","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1599,"endLine":1603},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"0417100b2527e9bb","name":"Xeno Resistances","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain <em>Resistance</em> against any 1 <em>Damage Type</em> of your choice, this can not be changed later.</p>\n<p>&lt;br&gt;</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alien-xeno-resistances","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1308,"endLine":1313},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Alien"}}}
{"_id":"05d734cce700cffe","name":"Namekian Fusion","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Namekians have the unique ability to assimilate others of their race into themselves to become what is known as a Super Namekian. As an Action you may fuse with one willing Namekian that you can touch.  Once you Fuse with another namekian you gain these benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain the <em>Super Namekian</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> and the ability to learn <em>Namekian Split</em>.</li>\n<li>You learn all <strong>Techniques</strong> and <em>Languages</em> of the assimilated. If the assimilated has more <em>Mastery Ranks</em> in a <strong>Technique</strong> that you know, you gain those <em>Mastery Ranks</em>.</li>\n<li>If they have any <strong>Ability Scores</strong> higher than yours you may add +1 to those <strong>Ability Scores</strong>, this may increase it above your <em>Ability Score Maximum</em>.<ul>\n<li>If none of their <strong>Ability Scores</strong> surpass yours you gain +1 to whichever <strong>Ability Score</strong> was their highest.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>You may only assimilate a number of Namekians equal to your <em>Constitution Modifier</em>.</li>\n<li>You gain the <strong>Fusion Tag</strong> and lose all benefits from this feature that you have gained if you ever lose this Tag, expelling those you have fused with in this manner in the proccess.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-namekian-fusion","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1952,"endLine":1960},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Namekian"}}}
{"_id":"060aa26e2c4c1833","name":"God Ki Creation","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Can never be learned by another master.</strong></p>\n<p>You have been taught to create and harness the energy of the gods. Your <strong>Maximum God Ki</strong> increases by 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"god-ki-creation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; God of Destruction"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3683,"endLine":3686}}}}
{"_id":"067717378a7dc4bb","name":"Superiority: Combat","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one class of <strong>Technique</strong>: <em>Beam, Blast, Barrage, Omni, Weapon, or Melee.</em> You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> when using this type of <strong>Technique</strong>. At <strong>Level 7</strong> this becomes +2 and at <strong>Level 13</strong> you get to pick a second type of <strong>Technique</strong> to gain this bonus as well.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 18</strong> you get an additional +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> that you can place on any class of <strong>Technique</strong>, regardless of if you choose that category previously.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"demon-superiority-combat","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1721,"endLine":1725},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Demon"}}}
{"_id":"080c86cf8acee7f8","name":"Skehmen-jin","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Strength or +1 Dexterity</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You gain the abilities and traits of the slothful Skehmen-jin. You gain their trait of being extremely difficult to kill you gain proficiency in Dexterity Saving throws. If you already have that proficiency you may choose 1 saving throw that you do not already have proficiency in. You also become a perfect being of rest, Whenever you take a short rest you restore full stamina instead of half. Youre demeanor can also change on a dime You gain the ability to, once per long rest, enter an empowered state of “Enraged”. This condition lasts for a number of rounds equal to half your proficiency bonus. Each time you use this feather past the first you gain 2 levels of exhaustion.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-skehmen-jin","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1617,"endLine":1622},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"08205b69d032c039","name":"Skill Expert","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed your proficiency with particular skills, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice.</li>\n<li>Choose one skill in which you have proficiency. You gain expertise with that skill, which means your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make with it. The skill you choose must be one that isn't already benefiting from a feature, such as Expertise, that doubles your proficiency bonus.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"skill-expert","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5422,"endLine":5428},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"0886195b61302998","name":"Namekian Type","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong> a Namekian must designate what type: Warrior Clan, Dragon Clan, or Dark Namekian.</p>\n<h5>Warrior Clan</h5>\n<p>Namekians born for combat that can utilize the monsterous Titan form.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase <em>Dexterity</em> and <em>Strength Scores</em> by 1.</li>\n<li>You gain the <em>Titan Namekian</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</li>\n<li>Warriors Regeneration<ul>\n<li>A Warrior can use his natural energy to repair his body. As an Action you may heal yourself 1 <strong>HP</strong> for every 2 <strong>Ki</strong> you spend.</li>\n<li>As an Action you may regenerate a lost limb for 30 <strong>Ki</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Dragon Clan</h5>\n<p>Those attuned to the spirit of Zalama the dragon god. these namekians are spiritually gifted and some even manage to emulate Zalama himself by creating Dragon Balls.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase <em>Intellegence</em> and <em>Wisdom Scores</em> by 1</li>\n<li>Dragon's Blessing<ul>\n<li>A Dragon Namekian can use his natural energy to repair his body at an alarming rate. As an action you may heal yourself 1 <strong>HP</strong> for every 1 <strong>Ki</strong> you spend.</li>\n<li>As an Action you may regenerate a limb that you have lost for 15 <strong>Ki</strong>.</li>\n<li>A Dragon Namekian is even capable of healing others with a touch. As an action you may heal a creature that you can touch for 1 <strong>HP</strong> for every 2 <strong>Ki</strong> you spend.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Dark Namekian</h5>\n<p>These Namekians are hardier than most and are usually demonized in Namekian Society due to their duller colors and lack of distinct Namekian abilities. Dark Namekians have mastered their own regenerative capability, some say they evolved purely to combat the raging discrimination they once faced.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase <em>Constitution Score</em> by 2</li>\n<li>Demonic Regeneration<ul>\n<li>You may heal yourself as an Action or Bonus Action, 2 <strong>HP</strong> for every 1 <strong>Ki</strong> spent.</li>\n<li>You can use an action and 5 <strong>Ki</strong> to regenerate a lost limb.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-namekian-type","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1966,"endLine":1999},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Namekian"}}}
{"_id":"0a97b60492d6b685","name":"Martial Arts","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your practice of martial arts gives mastery over <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> and <em>Martial Artist Weapons</em>, which are <em>Shortswords</em> and any <em>Simple Melee Weapons</em> without the <em>Heavy</em> or <em>Two-handed Property</em>.</p>\n<p>You gain the following benefits when unarmed or wielding only <em>Martial Artist Weapons</em>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your <em>Unarmed Strikes and Martial Artist Weapons</em> deal damage equal to the <strong>Martial Arts Table</strong> above</li>\n<li>Your <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> and <em>Martial Artist Weapons</em> have the <em>Finesse Property</em> (if they didn’t already), allowing you to use either <em>Dexterity</em> or <em>Strength</em> for <em>Attack</em> and <em>Damage Rolls</em> with them</li>\n<li>When you take the <em>Attack Action</em> with an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> and <em>Martial Artist Weapon</em> on your turn, you may make one <em>Unarmed Strike</em> as a bonus action.</li>\n<li>You may use <em>Dexterity</em> instead of <em>Strength</em> when calculating <em>Attack Roll Bonus</em> and <em>Save DC</em> for <strong>Melee Techniques</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-martial-arts","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2628,"endLine":2636},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"0ac8a01c676b4112","name":"Great Weapon Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned to put the weight of a weapon to your advantage, letting its momentum empower your strikes. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>On your turn, when you score a critical hit with a melee weapon or reduce a creature to 0 hit points with one, you can make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action.</li>\n<li>Before you make a melee attack with a heavy weapon that you are proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll. If the attack hits, you add +10 to the attack's damage.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"great-weapon-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5291,"endLine":5296},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"0ad5585d56ae7e54","name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beginning at <strong>5th Level</strong> you may make an additional attack as part of your <em>Attack Action</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-extra-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3018,"endLine":3021},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"0b2ad58e2cb97896","name":"Back to Basics","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <strong>Combination Form</strong> that you know, it now benefits from all <strong>Heroic Features</strong> of the <strong>Forms</strong> it is comprised of.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"back-to-basics","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6071,"endLine":6073},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"0b6fec048a838621","name":"Technique Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose 1 type of <strong>Technique</strong>: <em>Barrage, Beam, Blast, Melee, Omni, or Weapon</em>; <strong>Techniques</strong> of that type gain 1 <em>Rank of Mastery</em> when you learn them.</p>\n<p>You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> a number of times equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"technique-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6354,"endLine":6357},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"0bf5908093e7d7fc","name":"Time Storage","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The user can hold a maximum number of <em>Time Points</em> equal to half of their <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>, rounded up. <em>Time Points</em> can be recharged at a rate of 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> per <em>Time Point</em>. As an Action you may convert up to as many <strong>Stamina</strong> into Time Points as you can hold.</p>\n<p>Whenever you are under the effects of a <em>Time Skip</em> you may not create <em>Time Points</em> or use another <strong>Time Skip Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-storage","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3469,"endLine":3474}}}}
{"_id":"0d2c864bda03e136","name":"Controlled Crazed","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Purification</em> Transformation</strong>\nYou master your <em>Purified State</em>, now no longer forcing you into the <em>Berserk Condition</em>. Your Alignment Actively shifts 1 step down (Good &gt; Neutral &gt; Evil) while <em>Purification</em> is active.</p>\n<p>Additionally, you deal half your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> on all <strong>Techniques</strong> and <strong>Spells</strong> instead of full <em>Charisma Modifier</em> and this form drains 3 <strong>Stamina</strong> at the end of your turn. You may alternatively choose to lose control to revert to the original version.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"controlled-crazed","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Purification* Transformation","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5863,"endLine":5869},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"0f285d8c4fd08eb7","name":"Nomadic Tendencies","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to generations of lonely upbringing and long lifespans, Chronins gain an additional 1 <strong>Training Boon</strong> when <strong>Training Solo</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronin-nomadic-tendencies","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1678,"endLine":1680},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Chronin"}}}
{"_id":"115d8f146cf4ca4f","name":"Brutal Critical","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beginning at <strong>9th Level</strong>, you can roll one additional weapon damage die when determining the extra damage for a <strong>Critical Hit</strong> a <em>Melee Attack</em> or <strong>Melee/Melee Weapon Technique</strong>.</p>\n<p>This increases to two additional dice at <strong>13th Level</strong> and three additional dice at <strong>17th Level</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-brutal-critical","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3028,"endLine":3031},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"1192a08464c11b59","name":"Destructive Strikes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or <strong>Melee Technique</strong> you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> to give yourself a <em>Static Boost</em> equal to the amount spent for that casting. You may not spend more than half of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>, rounded up, in <strong>Stamina</strong> in this manner for a single attack roll.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"greys-destructive-strikes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1818,"endLine":1820},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Greys"}}}
{"_id":"11eb29872eb379fd","name":"Fighting Initiate","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your martial training has helped you develop a particular style of fighting. As a result, you learn one Fighting Style option of your choice from the Warrior Class. If you already have a style, the one you choose must be different.</p>\n<p>Whenever you reach a level that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace this feat's fighting style with another one from the Warrior Class that you don't have.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"fighting-initiate","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5279,"endLine":5284},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"121030f0307c8f3c","name":"Battery Powered","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have an internal power core that keeps you fueled. You do not suffer negative effects from not eating. You are incapable of regaining <strong>Ki</strong> from a <strong>Technique</strong> or <strong>Item</strong>, instead having a 4 <strong>Ki</strong> per round regen, this increases by 4 again at <strong>Levels 4, 7, 10, 13, 16,</strong> and <strong>19.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"android-battery-powered","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1364,"endLine":1365},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Android"}}}
{"_id":"124b46c8af50431f","name":"Form Fit","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can squeeze through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide, leaving behind all items that can not also fit. You also have Advantage on all <em>Skill Checks</em> you make to initiate or escape a <em>Grapple Check</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"majin-form-fit","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1858,"endLine":1861},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Majin"}}}
{"_id":"13a924f41810bb3e","name":"Destruction","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires God Ki</strong></p>\n<p>You have learned the trick to creating destruction energy. Whenever you cast a <strong>Technique/Spell</strong> you may double the casting cost to change the <em>Damage Type</em> to <em>Destruction Damage</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"destruction","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Requires God Ki","tags":"trained feature; God of Destruction"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3687,"endLine":3690}}}}
{"_id":"13adebd3ea212986","name":"Barrage Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <em>+1 Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Barrage Techniques</strong> and add half of your <em>Dexterity Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em>.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a second time to gain an addition +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> and you may now add your total <em>Dexterity Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em> instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"barrage-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6074,"endLine":6078},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"14467d8234d9cae8","name":"Superiority: Weapon","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are naturally adept at Weapon combat. You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> added to all <em>Martial</em> and <em>Simple Weapon Attacks</em> and <strong>Weapon Techniques</strong>. This increases to +2 at <strong>Level 7</strong>, +3 at <strong>Level 13</strong>, and +4 at <strong>Level 19</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"konatsian-superiority-weapon","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":914,"endLine":916},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Konatsian"}}}
{"_id":"1452736c5fdc8bd8","name":"Namekian Savior","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Fusing with at least 3 Namekians and either Orange or Red-Eyed Namekian</strong>\nYou are the hero the <em>Namekian Book of Prophecy</em> spoke of. You can now use <em>Super Namekian</em> and your <strong>Required Transformation</strong> as a <strong>Combination Transformation</strong> known as <em>Namekian Savior</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-savior","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Fusing with at least 3 Namekians and either Orange or Red-Eyed Namekian","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5878,"endLine":5885},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"14e21b13ec8ede9a","name":"Eureka!","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>*This <strong>Feat</strong> may be taken once per <strong>Ki Rank***\n**Must have the &quot;Gadgets&quot; class feature</strong></p>\n<p>Your Obsessive crafting of weapons and gadgets has sparked an epiphany. You gain 1 branch of magic as if you gained the <em>Gadgets</em> <strong>Class Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"eureka","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5090,"endLine":5096},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"15e9f4860eb9a979","name":"Unarmed Defense","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>1st Level</strong> while wearing no <em>Armor</em> and not wielding a <em>Shield</em>, your <strong>AC</strong> equals 10 + your <em>Dexterity Modifier</em> + your <em>Constitution Modifier</em>+ half of your Proficiency Bonus, rounded up.</p>\n<p>If you are wearing <em>Armor</em>, you use <em>Constitution</em> for <strong>AC</strong> calculation instead of <em>Dexterity</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-unarmed-defense","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2996,"endLine":2999},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"15f578e23e26d828","name":"Combat Superiority","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at <strong>2nd Level</strong>, you learn three <strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong> of your choice. Many <strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong> enhance an attack in some way. You can use only one <strong>Matial Arts Maneuver</strong> per attack. You learn two additional <strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong> of your choice at <strong>7th, 10th,</strong> and <strong>15th Level</strong>. Each time you learn new <strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong>, you can also replace one <strong>Matial Arts Maneuver</strong> you know with a different one.\n<strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong> will be detailed at the end of this chapter.</p>\n<h4>Superiority Dice</h4>\n<p>You have four <em>Superiority Dice</em>, which are d8s. A <em>Superiority Die</em> is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended <em>Superiority Dice</em> when you finish a Short or Long Rest. You gain another <em>Superiority Die</em> at <strong>7th Level</strong> and one more at <strong>15th Level</strong>.</p>\n<h4>Saving Throws</h4>\n<p>Some of your <strong>Matial Arts Maneuvers</strong> require your target to make a saving throw to resist the <strong>Matial Arts Maneuver's</strong> effects. The <em>Saving Throw DC</em> is calculated as follows:\n<strong>Matial Arts Maneuver Save DC</strong> = 8 + your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> + your <em>Strength</em> or <em>Dexterity Modifier</em> (your choice)</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-combat-superiority","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2642,"endLine":2654},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"163bd03ba6b5b4ba","name":"Attack Style","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>11th Level</strong> you choose a single type of <strong>Ki Technique</strong>: <em>Blast, Beam, Barrage</em>, or <em>Omni</em>. <strong>Ki Techniques</strong> of that type have their range doubled and gain one round of <strong>Charge</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-attack-style","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2912,"endLine":2913},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"16a5fe4ac492f2ec","name":"Team  Player","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest you may use the <em>Tag Team Attack</em> <strong>Manuever</strong> without expending <strong>Stamina</strong>.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a second time to make it recharge on a Short or Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"team-player","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6350,"endLine":6353},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"1730e4709136b7f2","name":"Power-Up Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to their adaptive nature Earthlings have a 2nd <strong>Power-Up Slot</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"earthling-power-up-proficiency","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":872,"endLine":884},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Earthling"}}}
{"_id":"17ef471a2dba0dae","name":"Ogre Stamina","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unique biology makes you longer winded than most species. You gain +1 <strong>Stamina</strong> at <strong>Level 1</strong> and everytime you <strong>Level Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ogre-ogre-stamina","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1013,"endLine":1015},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ogre"}}}
{"_id":"18538c2266351ba5","name":"War Caster","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have practiced casting spells in the midst of combat, learning techniques that grant you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You have advantage on Constitution saving throws that you make to maintain your concentration on a spell when you take damage.</li>\n<li>You can perform the somatic components of spells even when you have weapons or a shield in one or both hands.</li>\n<li>When a hostile creature's movement provokes an opportunity attack from you, you can use your reaction to cast a spell at the creature, rather than making an opportunity attack. The spell must have a casting time of 1 action and must target only that creature.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"war-caster","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5482,"endLine":5488},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"191f453d34e553b9","name":"Instant Transmission","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A fantastical ability that allows you to cross vast distances in an instance. As a <em>Bonus Action</em> or <em>Action</em> on your turn, you may spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to teleport to a location that you can see.</p>\n<p>Whenever you successfully locate a target using <em>Sense Ki,</em> you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> to teleport to them, as your Reaction to locating them or as your Action or Bonus Action so long as you can you continue to <em>Sense Ki</em>. You must spend 2 <strong>Stamina</strong> if they are on the same <em>Planet</em>, 3 <strong>Stamina</strong> if they are in the same <em>Solar System</em>, 4 <strong>Stamina</strong> if they are in the same <em>Universe</em>, or 5 <strong>Stamina</strong> if they are in the <em>Other World</em>/<em>Divine Realm</em> of your own <em>Universe</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"instant-transmission","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3424,"endLine":3429}}}}
{"_id":"199e25e3d67bdce2","name":"Big and Burly","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A grey flare's his energy eager to take every shot flying his way, once the barrage ends it's his chance to close the distance and once he did that, the fight was over.</p>\n<p>A young Saiyan roars in excitement, this was the first time he had fought all out in months, too bad none of them could deal any serious damage against him.</p>\n<p>Bruisers are terrors of the battlefield, capable of resisting attacks and dishing out incredible melee damage. Many bruisers become seen as paragons of pure strength.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-big-and-burly","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2946,"endLine":2952},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"1b881c2e410a7b5a","name":"Frozen Fury","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest, when you use a <strong>Technique</strong> of any type you may choose to gain a +3 <em>Static Bonus</em> to that casting.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"arcosian-frozen-fury","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1434,"endLine":1436},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Arcosian"}}}
{"_id":"1c637a5478d5e04d","name":"Natural Innocence","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your soul is bright and shining, even the most evil of Neko Majin radiates joy. You have advantage on all <em>Saving Throws</em> against being <em>Berserk, Charmed, or Frightened</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"neko-majin-natural-innocence","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2042,"endLine":2044},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Neko Majin"}}}
{"_id":"1cfc188983912893","name":"Maximum Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the <em>Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 5</strong> and the <em>Super Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 10</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sateery-maximum-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2086,"endLine":2091},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sateery"}}}
{"_id":"1de396ce4689dfe2","name":"Spirit Control Cloning","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action on your turn, you may create a number of clones up to your <em>Proficieny Bonus</em> for 2 <strong>Stamina</strong> per clone. These clones dissipate as a free action whenever you choose or after 1 minute passes. These clones are extensions of you and share all of your current <strong>Resources, Features, Forms,</strong> and <em>Conditions.</em> At the end of your turn you may have any number of clones move up to your <em>Movement Speed</em> and take a single Action or Bonus Action that you can take.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-control-cloning","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3414,"endLine":3415}}}}
{"_id":"1e031eaad13d2f7e","name":"9 Lives","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are extremely hard to kill, you gain proficiency in <em>Dexterity Saving throws</em>. If you already have that proficiency you may choose 1 <em>Saving Throw</em> that you do not already have proficiency in.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sekhmen-jin-9-lives","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2136,"endLine":2138},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sekhmen-jin"}}}
{"_id":"1e2803fc714c672b","name":"Spirit Burst","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action on your turn you may gain +3 <strong>Power</strong> until the end of your turn. If you do so you can't use this feature again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-burst","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6327,"endLine":6329},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"1e763200cbde9442","name":"Moderately Armored","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have trained to master the use of medium armor and shields, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency with medium armor and shields.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"moderately-armored","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5359,"endLine":5364},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"1fd002856deff812","name":"Magical Weakness","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Ki Damage</em> but have <em>Disadvantage</em> on all <em>Saving Throws</em> from <strong>Spells</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sateery-magical-weakness","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2092,"endLine":2095},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sateery"}}}
{"_id":"201768cbe75734cc","name":"Skilled","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain proficiency in any combination of three skills or tools of your choice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"skilled","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5429,"endLine":5431},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"2039f751251472a4","name":"Mind Over Matter","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>9th Level</strong>, you have learned to use your superior state of mind to push your body beyond it's limitations. When you are at 0 <strong>Stamina</strong> you may spend <strong>Hit Die</strong> in place of any <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-mind-over-matter","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2680,"endLine":2684},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"20a02b15ff349267","name":"Zenkai Boost","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When pushed to near death the saiyan spirit is known to rebel against the threat of death, creating a stronger warrior when they are pushed to near death.</p>\n<p>Whenever you fail a <em>Death Saving Throw</em>, roll a <em>d20 Check</em> with a DC starting at 8, increasing by 2 each time you succeed. On a Success you gain 1 <em>Training Boon</em>. You may use this <em>Training Boon</em> immedietly or as soon as you regain conciousness for the chance at a second <em>Zenkai Boost</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyans-zenkai-boost","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1089,"endLine":1092},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Saiyans"}}}
{"_id":"20d1439279e911cb","name":"Full Assimilation:","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the full strength of a creature within you that you absorb. When you would absorb a creature, you assimilate them entirely into you to gain the entirety of what you did not access. You gain all <strong>Forms</strong> that the creature has. You may only choose one creature to Assimilate within you and you have the <em>Fusion Tag</em> so long as they remain assimilated.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"full-assimilation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5870,"endLine":5871},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"20ebb599a4f35f30","name":"Eagle-Eyed Adaptation","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you see a <strong>Technique</strong> of no more than a single <strong>Ki Rank</strong> higher than you are that you could learn, you may memorize it.</p>\n<p>Until you replace this move you may cast it without gaining your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>. This <strong>Technique</strong> remains memorized until you replace it with a different <strong>Technique</strong>. If you learn the <strong>Technique</strong> that you have memorized it instantly gains 1 <em>Rank of Mastery</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"eagle-eyed-adaptation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6134,"endLine":6139},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"21c26ff37ad1fb9a","name":"Snake Way","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Crossing <em>Snake Way</em> is not easy, factoring multiple aspects, the main two factors being your body’s fortitude and your mind’s will to persevere. You must roll a <strong>DC 15</strong> <em>Constitution Saving Throw</em> and a <strong>DC 10</strong> <em>Charisma Saving Throw</em>. On a failure from either, you end up in HFIL(Hell) as your legs give out from weakness of body or spirit.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"snake-way","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"ordeal","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"ordeal"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3333,"endLine":3335}}}}
{"_id":"2281fd9ce310cba6","name":"Prodigious Learners","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a natural master of replicating what you see.</p>\n<p>You begin the game at <strong>Level 1</strong> with the <em>Eagled-Eyed Adaptation</em> <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> but you may use it a number of times per long rest equal to your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>. You can memorize a number of <strong>Techniques</strong> equal to your <strong>Intellegence Modifier</strong> at a time, replacing one of your choice if you were to exceed your maximum.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"neko-majin-prodigious-learners","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2022,"endLine":2025},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Neko Majin"}}}
{"_id":"2288e9b877cf4709","name":"Alien Brain","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a long living species and as such have a inherently different brain structure. You have advantage on all <em>Intelligence, Charisma, and Wisdom Saving Throws</em> against magic.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"arcosian-alien-brain","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1427,"endLine":1430},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Arcosian"}}}
{"_id":"242353aa0dbf58bb","name":"Blood of Time","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong>, you gain the <em>Time Storage</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> and you can hold 1 additional <em>Time Point</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronin-blood-of-time","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1664,"endLine":1668},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Chronin"}}}
{"_id":"24658954c54a4d6b","name":"Cerealian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Dexterity</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You feel the effect of your keen Cerealian DNA, Once per short rest you gain an extra reaction on your turn. You also gain the tenacity of a cerellian, Once per long rest if you fall to 0 Hit points you instead fall to 1 and you now bear the crimson eyes of a Cerealian, You gain access to the Red-Eye Activation Power Up</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-cerealian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1534,"endLine":1539},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"25c664c3dfed2354","name":"Konastian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 to any Ability Score</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your Konatsian blood has manifested into warrior potential.</p>\n<p>You gain a bonus to Static Bonus with all melee attacks and techniques while wielding a simple or martial weapon that you are proficient with equal to your Ki Rank. You may also use any weapon that gains this benefit in place of an unarmed strike for a melee technique.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-konastian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1561,"endLine":1567},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"26016a78112d83fa","name":"Upgrade Compatibility","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are more than a simple machine. You gain the <em>Construct</em> <strong>Tag</strong> and can not gain the <em>Ki Control</em> <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> through <strong>Training</strong> or <strong>Level Up.</strong></p>\n<p>Additionally you begin with the <em>Arm Missle</em> <strong>Technique</strong> and it's <strong>Ki Rank</strong> is equal to your own.</p>\n<h5>Arm Missile</h5>\n<p><em>Rank ? Melee Technique</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Casting Time:</strong>   1 action</li>\n<li><strong>Range:</strong>          120 feet</li>\n<li><strong>Chargeable?:</strong>          Yes</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong>       Instantaneous</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Fire your forearm off like a rocket before it returns and replaces itself on your arm. Make a combo attack roll against a target in range dealing your unarmed damage die + Xd4 <em>Force Damage</em> where X is your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"android-upgrade-compatibility","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1381,"endLine":1404},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Android"}}}
{"_id":"26dd51ad254da04a","name":"Pulling the Z-Sword","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Lodged and sealed in an indestructable stone collumn, removing the <em>Z-Sword</em> is a herculean task of almost divine proportions. To succeed in removing the sword you must succeed in 3 <strong>DC 20</strong> <em>Athletics Checks</em> or take 1 <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> on a failure as you end up slipping off the blade with skinned hands.\nYou may add half of your current <strong>Power Bonus</strong> to this <em>Athletics Checks</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"pulling-the-z-sword","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"ordeal","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"ordeal"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3336,"endLine":3340}}}}
{"_id":"27438b1a268e8f24","name":"Heavy Armor Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your armor to deflect strikes that would kill others. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>While you are wearing heavy armor, bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage that you take from nonmagical attacks is reduced by 3.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"heavy-armor-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5303,"endLine":5308},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"27524cd078b960bb","name":"Duel-Wielder","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master fighting with two weapons, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain a +1 bonus to AC while you are wielding a separate melee weapon in each hand.</li>\n<li>You can use two-weapon fighting even when the one handed melee weapons you are wielding aren't light.</li>\n<li>You can draw or stow two one-handed weapons when you would normally be able to draw or stow only one.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"duel-wielder","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5258,"endLine":5264},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"276a60a252b21d52","name":"Secret Fighting Poses","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>2nd Level</strong> whenever you would use your <strong>Heroic Inspiration</strong>, you may instead give a number of targets that can see you, equal to your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> minimum of 1, a bonus for the next minute by striking a powerful pose. If you choose the same pose more than once you gain an improved version. Each time you gain this <strong>Feature</strong> you choose one of the following poses:</p>\n<h4>Pose of Valor</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Strength Ability Score and Maximum</em> and +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Melee Attacks Rolls</em> and <em>Unarmed Strikes</em>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Static Bonus increases to +2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Pose of Grace</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Dexterity Ability Score and Maximum</em> and double their <em>Base Fly</em> and <em>Walk Speed</em>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your <em>Movement Speed</em> can not be lowered by any means.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Pose of Vitality</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Constitution Ability Score and Maximum</em> and +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Beam</strong> <strong>Techniques</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Static Bonus</em> increases to +2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Pose of Acuity</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Intelligence Ability Score and Maximum</em> and +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Omni Techniques</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Static Bonus</em> increases to +2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Pose of Clarity</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Wisdom Ability Score and Maximum</em> and +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Blast Techniques</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Static Bonus</em> increases to +2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Pose of Hope</h4>\n<p>Targets gain +2 to their <em>Charisma Ability Score and Maximum</em> and a +1 to all <em>Saving Throws</em>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Saving Throw</em> bonus increases to +2</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-secret-fighting-poses","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3145,"endLine":3178},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"27a148a1e6346e2a","name":"Stitch in Time","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>1 Time Point</em>\nAs an Action on your turn, you may peak into the timestream to see the past of a Person or Object that you are touching.\nThis ability allows you to rewind your or someone else's connection to the flow of time, allowing you to watch echoes of the past to see scenes of the past in perfect clarity. It is up to the <strong>DM</strong> to determine what you see.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"stitch-in-time","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3489,"endLine":3496}}}}
{"_id":"27a6af2e0fca316b","name":"Ceralian Focus","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action on your turn you may spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to gain advantage on all <em>Ranged Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> until the end of your next turn. You may do this a number of times equal to your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> per Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ceralians-ceralian-focus","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":817,"endLine":819},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ceralians"}}}
{"_id":"281b2085730b41ee","name":"Magical Upbringing","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain access to 1 branch of magic of your choice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"konatsian-magical-upbringing","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":908,"endLine":910},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Konatsian"}}}
{"_id":"2bd7f14f8c0da43b","name":"Ki Blast Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>3rd Level</strong> whenever you take the <em>Ki Blast Action</em> you may fire an additional <em>Basic Ki Blast</em> as part of that Action.</p>\n<p>At <strong>9th Level</strong> when you use your Action to take the <em>Attack Action</em> or the <em>Ki Blast Action</em>, you may take the <em>Ki Blast Action</em> as your Bonus Action.</p>\n<p>At <strong>15th Level</strong> whenever you take the <em>Ki Blast Action</em> you may fire an additional <em>Basic Ki Blast</em> as part of that Action.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-ki-blast-proficiency","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2894,"endLine":2899},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"2d520dd86c12314a","name":"Perfected Ultra Instinct","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: 5 ranks of <em>Ultra Instinct Mastery</em> Feat and <em>Mastered Ultra Instinct</em>.</strong>\nYou have stopped considering Ultra Instinct Omen as a <strong>Form</strong>, now considering it truly as part of your base without any of the drawbacks. You may now go into <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> at will. Additionally <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> no longer has a <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"perfected-ultra-instinct","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: 5 ranks of *Ultra Instinct Mastery* Feat and *Mastered Ultra Instinct*.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6017,"endLine":6022},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"2d9b3c985c0873bb","name":"Absorbitive biology","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your body is naturally capable of gaining power from those you can eat. You can eat a creature of medium size only if they are willing, unconcious, paralyzed, or otherwise incapacitated.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You learn all <strong>Techniques</strong>, <strong>Trained Features</strong>, and <em>Languages</em> of the assimilated. If the assimilated has more <em>Mastery Ranks</em> in a <strong>Technique</strong> that you know, you gain those <em>Mastery Ranks</em>.</li>\n<li>If they have any <strong>Ability Scores</strong> higher than yours you may add +1 to those <strong>Ability Scores</strong>, this may increase it above your <em>Ability Score Maximum</em>.<ul>\n<li>If none of their <strong>Ability Scores</strong> surpass yours you gain +1 to whichever <strong>Ability Score</strong> was their highest.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>You gain visual quirks resembling the entities that you assimilated.</li>\n<li>You gain the <strong>Fusion Character Tag</strong> and lose all benefits from this feature that you have gained if you ever lose this <strong>Tag</strong>, coughing up those you have assimilated if it is lost.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You may only gain this benefit a number of times equal to your <em>Constitution Modifier</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sateery-absorbitive-biology","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2096,"endLine":2112},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sateery"}}}
{"_id":"2ed15c54668f0d23","name":"Defensive Aura","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ki forms an invisible barrier around your body, softening impacts and shielding you from energy.</p>\n<p>While wearing no <em>Armor</em> and not wielding a <em>Shield</em>, your <strong>AC</strong> equals 10 + double your <em>Wisdom Modifier</em>+ half of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> (rounded up).</p>\n<p>When you are wearing <em>Armor</em> you may use your <em>Wisdom</em> in place of <em>Dexterity</em> for <strong>AC Calculation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-defensive-aura","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2877,"endLine":2882},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"2f03c1f40e1d18b9","name":"Kami's Lookout","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Ki Rank 2</strong>\nYou have been taught how to place a piece of your soul into an area, pulling it from the ground into your own floating sanctum.</p>\n<p>As an 8 hour <em>Ritual</em> you may meditate, placing your soul into the planet or a structure no larger than an island, causing it to rip from the ground and fly into the sky. While on your <em>Lookout</em>, you have advantage on all <em>Sense Ki Checks</em> you make. At the center of your island resides a spiritual place, from this location you may spend an Action and gain a <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> to teleport you and any creatures you are touching to the <em>Gates of Otherworld</em>.</p>\n<p>You may use this <strong>Trained Feature</strong> so long as you are at the <em>Gates of Otherworld</em> or <em>Yemma's Reception Desk</em> to transport you and any creatures you are touching to your <em>Lookout.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kami-s-lookout","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":2,"requirements":"Requires: Ki Rank 2","tags":"trained feature; Guardian of the Dragon Balls"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3603,"endLine":3610}}}}
{"_id":"3001254dbf77e7ae","name":"Earthling Spirit","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Increase the <em>Ability Score Maximum</em> of one <strong>Ability Score</strong> of your choice by 2. Additionally at an <em>Ability Score Improvement</em>, you gain 4 points to distribute, rather than the usual 3.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"earthling-earthling-spirit","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":863,"endLine":867},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Earthling"}}}
{"_id":"3025d860c545096f","name":"Perfected Divinity","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Divine Combination</strong>\nYou have decided to master the full capabilities of your Super Saiyan God, keeping the ki within your body to enhance all capabilities. You may now apply <em>Super Saiyan Grade 4</em> to the <em>Super Saiyan God</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n<p>When you would end this <strong>Power-Up</strong>, your aura bursts out in a moment of uncontrolled power. You gain +4 <strong>Power Bonus</strong> until the end of your next turn. Afterwards gaining 2 <em>Ranks of Exhaustion</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"perfected-divinity","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Divine Combination","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5549,"endLine":5557},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"30bc64f5c12c3c85","name":"Spirit Power","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> and <strong>Ki Techniques</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3448,"endLine":3450}}}}
{"_id":"3124866b51071d7f","name":"Blood of the Shin-jins","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Radiant Damage</em> as well as Advantage on <em>Spell Saving Throws</em>. Whenever you use the <strong>Block Manuever</strong> your <em>Resistance</em> becomes <em>Immunity</em> and you pass all <em>Spell Saving Throws</em> .</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shinling-blood-of-the-shin-jins","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1239,"endLine":1245},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Shinling"}}}
{"_id":"3155a1cc5e4b440d","name":"DNA Specialization","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Prerequisite: Level 5+</p>\n<p>Pick one race from your Genetic Makeup, you gain the corresponding bonuses listed below. This cannot be changed later:</p>\n<h4>Alien</h4>\n<p>You now only receive 1 level of exhaustion from going past your enraged limit. You also gain the Full Power Transformation.</p>\n<h4>Arcosian</h4>\n<p>You gain access to all Arcosian Transformation/Power Ups and Racial Feats</p>\n<h4>Beastmen</h4>\n<p>You gain the Animal Biology Feature from Beastmen and you may 1/3rd of your proficiency bonus to your AC while not wearing armor</p>\n<h4>Cerealian</h4>\n<p>You gain access to all Cerealian Power-ups and permanently get an additional reaction on your turn.</p>\n<h4>Chronin</h4>\n<p>You gain the ability to turn 1 Stamina into 2 Time Points. And gain access to the Quickened Storage Feat</p>\n<h4>Demon</h4>\n<p>You gain Resistance to 1 <em>Damage Type</em> of your chocie and you gain access to all Demon Feats.</p>\n<h4>Earthling</h4>\n<p>You gain access to all Earthling Power Ups and racial feats</p>\n<h4>Greys</h4>\n<p>Your Ability Score maximum increase by an additional 2 and meditation now gives 10 times your ki rank. You also gain the full power transformation</p>\n<h4>Konastian</h4>\n<p>You gain access to 1 Branch of Magic of your choice as if you gained the Mysticism Feature and you have advantage on saving throws against being charmed.</p>\n<h4>Majin</h4>\n<p>Your unarmed strikes gain an additional 5ft equal to your proficiency bonus/3 rounded down. You regeneration now becomes 1 Ki for 1 HP.</p>\n<h4>Mashin-jin</h4>\n<p>You gain access to all Mashin-jin Transformations and Power Ups and gain access to racial feats. You gain the Infernal tag.</p>\n<h4>Namekian</h4>\n<p>You gain access to all Namekian Transformations and Power Ups and Racial Feats</p>\n<h4>Neko Majin</h4>\n<p>You may now copy a number of abilities equal to your Intelligence Modifier and you gain the <strong>Mystical Mimicry</strong> Feature from Neko Majin. You additionally gain access to all Neko majin Feats</p>\n<h4>Ogre</h4>\n<p>Increase your maximum stamina by an amount equal to your level and you gain an additional +1 stamina every time you level up from this point.</p>\n<h4>Sateery</h4>\n<p>You gain the Energy Thief feature and gain the Full Power Transformation</p>\n<h4>Saiyan</h4>\n<p>You grow a saiyan Tail. choose between Berserker Saiyan or Universe 7 Saiyan you gain access to all the transformations of the chosen archetype. You also gain access to saiyan racial feats.</p>\n<h4>Shinling</h4>\n<p>You gain the Celestial tag and gain access to Racial Feats</p>\n<h4>Skehmen-jin</h4>\n<p>You can now enrage once per short rest. You also gain the ability to change any damage you deal into fire damage.</p>\n<h4>Yardratian</h4>\n<p>You gain an additional spirit control feature at rank 2 and rank 4, if you are already past or at these ranks you gain them at this time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dna-specialization","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisite: Level 5+","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5919,"endLine":5989},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"317109fa224563e4","name":"Predator or Prey","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Choose 1</strong></p>\n<h5>Predator</h5>\n<p>You have advantage on <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> and <em>Weapon Attack Rolls</em> against a creature if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the creature you are targeting.</p>\n<h5>Prey</h5>\n<p>You can take the <strong>Dash, Dodge, or Disengage Actions</strong> as a Bonus Action on your turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beastmen-predator-or-prey","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":766,"endLine":772},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Beastmen"}}}
{"_id":"32268e7e17a75d50","name":"Ki Flow","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Can't be taken by Androids or Cyborgs</strong></p>\n<p>Your energy constantly flows throughout your body. You gain (your <strong>Character Level</strong> + 2) <strong>Ki</strong> at the end of your turn if you did not spend <strong>Ki</strong> that turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ki-flow","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6205,"endLine":6208},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"34101aeb15546225","name":"Weight Acclimation","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Can be taken a number of times equal to Ranks in the &quot;Weight Training&quot; feat.</strong></p>\n<p>You have fully acclimated your body to the heightened weight of your training and can treat it as your standard gravity.</p>\n<p>Whenever you are not under the <em>Heavy Weight Condition</em> you benefit from the <em>Light Weight Condition</em> equal to the amount of times you have taken this <strong>Feat</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"weight-acclimation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5108,"endLine":5115},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"34e00c74c9b25cdb","name":"Self Taught! Kinda....","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to the strange nature of this feature it is possible for 2 people to be instructed on how to use this feature and then have a <strong>Training Arc with a Partner</strong> together to fully learn the feature together for the cost of 2 Training Boons each.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you may have a <strong>Training Arc with a Partner</strong> together with someone that knows the <em>Fusion Dance</em> and gain advantage on <em>Fusion Dances</em> with that person for 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong> each.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"self-taught-kinda","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Metamoran"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3565,"endLine":3581}}}}
{"_id":"3538b75b97728dcc","name":"Beam Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <em>+1 Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Beam Techniques</strong> and add half of your <em>Constitution Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em>.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a second time to gain an addition +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> and you may now add your total <em>Constitution Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em> instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beam-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6079,"endLine":6083},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"35722ae85f28cb63","name":"Bolster allies","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action choose a number of creatures equal to or less than your <em>Charisma Modifier</em>, within 120 feet who can see or hear you. They gain 1d8 + your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> + your <strong>Hero</strong> level in <strong>Temporary HP</strong>. These last for 1 hour. You must finish a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-bolster-allies","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3120,"endLine":3122},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"35877ae5db835104","name":"Grappler","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've developed the skills necessary to hold your own in close-quarters grappling. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You have advantage on attack rolls against a creature you are grappling.</li>\n<li>You can use your action to try to pin a creature grappled by you. To do so, make another grapple check. If you succeed, you and the creature are both restrained until the grapple ends.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"grappler","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5285,"endLine":5290},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"36a8c50eec4ee2ec","name":"Self Conscious","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Prerequisites: 20+ Wisdom</strong></p>\n<p>You master a state of calmness and control of your ki that exceeds what most individuals are normally able to gain, you gain the <em>No-Ego</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"self-conscious","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisites: 20+ Wisdom","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5126,"endLine":5130},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"39a6bf49a3103f01","name":"Sky Dancing","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You immediately gain 1 rank of the <em>Ki Flight</em> <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>. This can raise you above the normal maximum for <em>Ki Flight.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sky-dancing","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Crane School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3371,"endLine":3373}}}}
{"_id":"3ab3fc186f4369f3","name":"Magical Stretch","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your putty-like body gives you <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing,</em> and <em>Slashing Damage</em>. Your <em>Unarmed Strikes/Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <strong>Melee/Melee Weapon Techniques</strong> all gain an additional 5 feet of the <em>Reach Property</em> equal to a third of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>, rounded up.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"majin-magical-stretch","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1862,"endLine":1864},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Majin"}}}
{"_id":"3ae72a79c94475ad","name":"Spirit Restoration","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your mastery of <em>Spirit Control</em>  to stimulate the body's healing process through ki. As an Action you may touch yourself or another creature, you and/or the creature being healed may spend <strong>Ki</strong> to restore 2 <strong>HP</strong> per <strong>Ki</strong> spent collectively.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-restoration","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3451,"endLine":3461}}}}
{"_id":"3b55e25eca8cd391","name":"Android/Cyborg","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As opposed to DNA, the specific cybernetic parts were applied to yourbody, enhancing your bodies capability. You gain 1 Rank of <em>Light Weight</em>. If you absorb a creature that has the Cyborg Subrace, you must choose between the Main Race or the Cyborg Subrace.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-android-cyborg","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1520,"endLine":1523},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"3b64dceeec9504f8","name":"Supercharged Ki Blast","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your <em>Basic Ki Blast's</em> <em>Damage Die</em> is increased by 1 stage. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken up to 3 times.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"supercharged-ki-blast","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6339,"endLine":6341},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"3c160ec1d89f1b48","name":"Emperial Wrath","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires &quot;Hubris of Midus&quot; Feat.</strong>\nHistory is written by the powerful. It's time to change the books.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Obsidian Form</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"emperial-wrath","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires \"Hubris of Midus\" Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5795,"endLine":5801},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"3c1e6d2363043c43","name":"Dungeon Delver","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Alert to the hidden traps and secret doors found in many dungeons, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to detect the presence of secret doors.</li>\n<li>You have advantage on saving throws made to avoid or resist traps.</li>\n<li>You have resistance to the damage dealt by traps.</li>\n<li>Travelling at a fast pace doesn't impose the normal -5 penalty on your passive Wisdom (Perception) score.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dungeon-delver","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5265,"endLine":5272},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"3cf5447e0fba3207","name":"Savage Attacker","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you roll damage for a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice and use either total.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"savage-attacker","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5395,"endLine":5398},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"3dcc3403d1a7eccf","name":"Sharpshooter","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You <em>Basic Ki Blast</em> has it’s Damage Die increased by 2 steps (1d4&gt;1d6&gt;1d8&gt;1d10&gt;1d12&gt;2d6&gt;2d8&gt;etc) and it's range is doubled. Each time your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> increases, increase the range by an additional 30/90 feet.</p>\n<p>This does not effect <strong>Techniques</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ceralians-sharpshooter","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":824,"endLine":827},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ceralians"}}}
{"_id":"3e006345a1a95044","name":"Heroic Feature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Gain 2 features from the <strong>Heroic Features List</strong>. Every time you get this <strong>Class Feature</strong> after the first time, you gain 1 additional <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-heroic-feature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2883,"endLine":2888},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"3e072ffb26b75532","name":"Divine Talent","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong> you add the <em>Kaio-Ken</em> <strong>Forms</strong> to your <strong>Learnable Technique List</strong>, but <em>Kaio-Ken!</em> and <em>Kaio-Ken x4!</em> become <strong>Ki Rank 2</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shinling-divine-talent","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1261,"endLine":1263},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Shinling"}}}
{"_id":"3e786ee112fcea9f","name":"Solid Guard","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use the <em>Block</em> <strong>Manuever</strong>, you may spend twice as much <strong>Stamina</strong> to take 1/4 damage instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"solid-guard","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6333,"endLine":6338},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"3f952f75bf80e023","name":"Small but Legendary","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong> you gain a single <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>. This does not count as gaining a <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> as a <strong>Class Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"neko-majin-small-but-legendary","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2045,"endLine":2053},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Neko Majin"}}}
{"_id":"40764c0e357e7f71","name":"Legendary Mentality","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Berserker Super Saiyan 3</em> and <em>Legendary Power</em> Feat.</strong>\nYou learn to master your Super Saiyan 3 state to the point where your muscles calm down and control the level of output that is shown. You gain access to the <em>Controlled Super Saiyan 3</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"legendary-mentality","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Berserker Super Saiyan 3* and *Legendary Power* Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5740,"endLine":5744},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"431188534c6ab72c","name":"Ki Enhanced Abilities","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to supercharge your attacks with your ki making your attacks hit with unearthly force. Wearing <em>Armor</em> does not affect this <strong>Feature</strong>. You gain the following benefits when unarmed:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can use a d4 in place of your <em>Unarmed Strike's Damage Die</em>. This die increases as you gain <strong>Blaster Levels</strong>, as shown on the table above. You may use <em>Wisdom</em> as your <em>Modifier</em> for <em>Unarmed Strikes</em>.</li>\n<li>Your <em>Basic Ki Blast Damage Die</em> increases as you gain <strong>Blaster Levels</strong>, as shown on the table above.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-ki-enhanced-abilities","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2872,"endLine":2876},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"434d3e927a51c4ee","name":"Crane Style Disciple","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The <strong>AC Bonus</strong> from the <em>Crane Style</em> <strong>Stance</strong> is increaesd by 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"crane-style-disciple","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Crane School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3365,"endLine":3367}}}}
{"_id":"44b22c206a943e71","name":"Milk Run","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The essence of the <em>Milk Run</em> is simple, your task is to deliver all of the milk in to the population of an island in a single day on foot. By spending 1 day you may attempt 3 consecutive <strong>DC 15</strong> <em>Athletics Checks</em> to succeed this task.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"milk-run","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"ordeal","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"ordeal"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3327,"endLine":3329}}}}
{"_id":"452e60efaa9c2498","name":"Saiyan Ascension","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6</em>\nSuper Saiyan, the ultimate power of the Saiyan race, many don’t have the skill to take it “even further beyond”.</p>\n<p>This feat can only be taken after <em>Super Saiyan 1</em> is unlocked. This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken twice, the first time granting you <em>Super Saiyan 2</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>, the second time giving you <em>Super Saiyan 3</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyan-ascension","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5507,"endLine":5519},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"4533c49525d38fbb","name":"Spirit Amplification","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use your Action for <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> or <strong>Ki Techniques</strong>, you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> to give yourself a <em>Static Bonus</em> equal to the <strong>Stamina</strong> spent, max of 10.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-amplification","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3438,"endLine":3440}}}}
{"_id":"46174cefa67caaf9","name":"Know Your Enemy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at <strong>7th Level</strong>, if you spend at least 1 Minute observing or interacting with another creature outside combat, you can learn certain information about its capabilities compared to your own. The DM tells you if the creature is your equal, superior, or inferior in regard to two of the following characteristics of your choice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Strength Ability Score</em></li>\n<li><em>Dexterity Ability Score</em></li>\n<li><em>Constitution Ability Score</em></li>\n<li><strong>AC</strong></li>\n<li>Current <strong>HP</strong></li>\n<li>Total <strong>Class Levels</strong>, if any</li>\n<li><strong>Martial Artist Class Levels</strong>, if any</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-know-your-enemy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2669,"endLine":2679},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"4698f13c5f06c341","name":"Super Saiyan God Evolution","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Divine Combination</strong>\nYou have pushed <em>Super Saiyan God</em> to its limit and broken them. You now gain the <em>Super Saiyan God Evolution</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"super-saiyan-god-evolution","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Divine Combination","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5534,"endLine":5540},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"4776cc1e55024597","name":"Tavern Brawler","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Accustomed to the rough-and-tumble fighting using whatever weapons happen to be at hand, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Consititution score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You are proficient with improvised weapons.</li>\n<li>Your unarmed strike damage die is increased by 1 step. (1d4&gt;1d6&gt;1d8&gt;1d10&gt;1d12&gt;2d6&gt;2d8&gt;etc)</li>\n<li>When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike or an improvised weapon on your turn, you can use a bonus action to attempt to grapple the target.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"tavern-brawler","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5455,"endLine":5462},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"48762a775809b99c","name":"Dark Saiyan","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Level 10+</strong>\nYou accept the evil within your heart, unleashing it and manifesting it within your aura and the evil within your entire being.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Dark Energy</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dark-saiyan","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Level 10+","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5693,"endLine":5699},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"489efa010d138965","name":"Observant","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Quick to notice details of your environment, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>If you can see a creature's mouth while it is speaking a language you understand, you can interpret what it's saying by reading its lips.</li>\n<li>You have a +5 bonus to your passive Wisdom (Perception) and passive Intelligence (Investigation) scores.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"observant","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5365,"endLine":5375},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"48e5d1bd7990d387","name":"Ultimate Form","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Ki Rank 3</strong></p>\n<p>You may choose 1 <strong>Transformation</strong> and 1 <strong>Power-Up</strong> that you have access to, these become a new <strong>Combination Transformation</strong> with a name unique to you. This new <strong>Combinatation Form</strong> retains all activation requirements as the <strong>Forms</strong> that make it up.\nThe <strong>Forms</strong> you pick can not both have the <strong>Godly Tag</strong> or already be a <strong>Combination Form</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ultimate-form","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Ki Rank 3","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5196,"endLine":5204},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"49612b10c0f1afe1","name":"Telekenetic","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to move things with your mind, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You learn the <em>mage hand</em> cantrip. You can cast it without verbal or somatic components, and you can make the spectral hand invisible. If you already know this spell, its range increases by 30 feet when you cast it. Its spellcasting ability is the ability increased by this feat.</li>\n<li>As a bonus action, you can try to telekinetically shove one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. When you do so, the target must succeed on a Strength saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + the ability modifier of the score increased by this feat) or be moved 5 feet toward or away from you. A creature can willingly fail this save.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"telekenetic","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5463,"endLine":5471},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"49c6b8c54013f61b","name":"Phycic Prowess","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to use your energy as an extension of your body. You may make <em>Grapple Checks</em> instead of dealing damage with your <em>Basic Ki Blast.</em> To maintain the <em>Grapple</em> on a target you must maintain <em>Concentration</em> and use <em>Spirit</em> instead of <em>Athletics</em> when making contested <em>Grapple Checks</em> with the target.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"phycic-prowess","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Crane School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3374,"endLine":3379}}}}
{"_id":"4a2b5c1b44740da2","name":"Unique Physiology","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Creature tag is Monstrosity and your Ki Signiture appears as a strange amalgamation of Signatures. Creatures have advantage on perception checks to find your Ki when you are not actively concealing it.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-unique-physiology","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1474,"endLine":1477},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"4a433e83b1b32069","name":"Redirect Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature misses you with an attack with an attack roll, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> as a reaction to cause that attack to hit one creature of your choice, other than the attacker, that you can see within 5 feet of you.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"redirect-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6316,"endLine":6318},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"4b6212f1a7a3c7e0","name":"Unarmored Defense","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While wearing no <em>Armor</em> and not wielding a <em>Shield</em>, your <strong>AC</strong> equals 10 + your <em>Dexterity Modifier</em> + your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-unarmored-defense","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2637,"endLine":2641},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"4bcafeb2c360d1dc","name":"Animal Biology","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>You must choose 1</strong></p>\n<p>Your animal nature has resulted in you taking the distinct form of a family of animals, granting you certain features.</p>\n<h5>Mammalian</h5>\n<p>You have a set of powerful claws. Your <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> can deal <em>Slashing Damage</em>.</p>\n<h5>Fish</h5>\n<p>You are capable of breathing air as well as underwater. You also gain a 30 foot <em>Swim Speed</em> that increases by 15 feet each time your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> increases.</p>\n<h5>Avian</h5>\n<p>You are a master of arial combat. You gain a 30 foot <em>Fly Speed.</em> You may only use this <em>Fly Speed</em> while you are not wielding a <em>Weapon</em> in your hand. Your <strong>AC</strong> increases while in the air by one third of your <em>Proficiency Modifier</em>, rounded down.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beastmen-animal-biology","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":773,"endLine":791},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Beastmen"}}}
{"_id":"4e3af5551820a7a2","name":"He’s Fast!","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may take the <em>Dash Action</em> as a Bonus Action and gain an additional 15 feet of <em>Movement Speed</em> while <em>Dashing.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hes-fast","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6153,"endLine":6155},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"4f919899e05a62a3","name":"There’s No Holding Back","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest, If you activate a <strong>Form</strong> before taking any other Actions in combat, gain +2 to all <strong>Ability Scores</strong> until the end of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"theres-no-holding-back","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6362,"endLine":6366},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"518f01e642c984a1","name":"Magical Shape-Shifters","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Years of hiding have made Neko Majins a master of hiding their true self.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level</strong> 1 you know the <em>Disguise Self</em> and <em>Alter Self</em> <strong>Spells</strong> as if through the <em>Mysticism</em> <strong>Class Feature</strong> except their duration becomes 8 hours.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level</strong> 10 you also gain the <em>Polymorph</em> <strong>Spell</strong> as if through the <em>Mysticism</em> <strong>Class Feature</strong>.\nThese <strong>Spells</strong> can only target yourself.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"neko-majin-magical-shape-shifters","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2026,"endLine":2034},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Neko Majin"}}}
{"_id":"51d6c0d2d63b8c76","name":"Dark Energy Awakening","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the <em>Dark Energy</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong> and do not need to make <em>Berserk Saving Throws.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dark-energy-awakening","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5852,"endLine":5853},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"52b01461c90b0e62","name":"Reckless Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can throw aside all concern for defense to attack with fierce desperation. When you make your first attack on Your Turn, you can decide to <em>Attack Recklessly</em>. Doing so gives you Advantage on all Melee Attack rolls until the start of your next turn, but Attack Rolls against you have Advantage until your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"reckless-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6313,"endLine":6315},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"532e2d0d8aae8815","name":"Super Saiyan","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The golden form of legend. At <strong>Level 5</strong> and beyond, the first time you enter the <em>Enraged</em> condition you turn <em>Super Saiyan 1</em> and can access it from that point on.</p>\n<p>You also have access to learning the <em>Super Saiyan Grades</em> <strong>Power-ups</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyans-super-saiyan","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1093,"endLine":1097},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Saiyans"}}}
{"_id":"5486efaa465354ee","name":"The Weight of Heaven and HFIL","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You carry on your shoulders the metaphysical weight of the realms as a curse, this however has only served to strengthen you.. You gain the <strong>Infernal Tag</strong> and at <strong>Levels 5, 10, 15, and 20</strong> you gain the <em>Weight Training</em> <strong>Feat.</strong> If you already have the <em>Weight Training</em> <strong>Feat</strong> to its maximum, than you gain the <em>Weight Acclimation</em> <strong>Feat</strong> instead.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"demon-the-weight-of-heaven-and-hfil","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1726,"endLine":1728},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Demon"}}}
{"_id":"548f9673a65d76c1","name":"Alien Ability","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <em>Damage Type</em> from the list below, this can not be changed later. You gain the option to change the <em>Damage Type</em> of your <strong>Techniques/Spells</strong>, <em>Unarmed Strikes</em>, and <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> to this <em>Damage Type</em>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fire</li>\n<li>Cold</li>\n<li>Lightning</li>\n<li>Thunder</li>\n<li>Force</li>\n<li>Psychic</li>\n<li>Poison</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alien-alien-ability","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1314,"endLine":1324},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Alien"}}}
{"_id":"54ba07931d787936","name":"Quickened Storage","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your storage speed is even faster then before. You gain the option to turn <strong>Stamina</strong> into <strong>Time Points</strong> as a Bonus Action.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken a second time to gain the option to do this as a Reaction on your turn. Taking this Feat does not remove your ability to store time points as an Action or Bonus Action if you have that capability already.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"quickened-storage","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5846,"endLine":5850},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"55f998016a926153","name":"Removed From Time","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>3 Time Points</em>\nThe user can remove himself from the prime material plane, temporarily allowing attacks to pass right through you. You are still visible and can still be seen and heard.</p>\n<p>As a Reaction on your turn whenever you are subject to an <em>Attack Roll</em> or forced to make a <em>Saving Throw</em>, you may cause all effects to miss you until the start of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"removed-from-time","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3502,"endLine":3508}}}}
{"_id":"56cb3c6bb643d835","name":"Cat Nap","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Sleep is good, especially for you. Once per day, when you take a Short Rest you restore full <strong>Stamina</strong> instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sekhmen-jin-cat-nap","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2154,"endLine":2165},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sekhmen-jin"}}}
{"_id":"57aca92c6733bb1e","name":"Alien Skill","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <strong>Technique</strong> every time you <strong>Level-Up</strong> to 20 and 2 <strong>Techniques</strong> every level beyond. You also gain 1 additional <em>Training Boon</em> each time you have a <strong>Training Arc</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alien-alien-skill","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1325,"endLine":1327},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Alien"}}}
{"_id":"581a765232667770","name":"Ki Reserve","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>2nd Level</strong> once per Long Rest as a Bonus Action you regain 2d12 + <em>Wisdom Modifier</em> <strong>Ki</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>7th Level</strong> it recharges on a Short Rest.\nAt <strong>13th Level</strong> you recover 4d12 + <em>Wisdom Modifier</em> <strong>Ki</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-ki-reserve","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2889,"endLine":2893},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"58e60982ec69e585","name":"Shinling","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Cannot be taken with Mashin-Jin DNA</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>+1 Wisdom</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This rare divine DNA grants you a taste of godhood, You gain access to the Kaioken power up. You also can empower an attack with divine energy, when you deal damage you may use a bonus action to change its damage type to radiant. You also gain resistance to radiant damage.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-shinling","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1609,"endLine":1616},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"5946a4c8c5f99936","name":"Legendary Divinity","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Legendary Power</em> Feat, <em>Super Saiyan God</em>, and <em>Full Power Super Saiyan</em>.</strong>\nYou have mixed Super Saiyan with Super Saiyan God but it's different than others, your hair elongates and your aura shines green with divine energy. You can use <em>Super Saiyan God</em> as a <strong>Power-Up</strong> with <em>Full Power Super Saiyan</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"legendary-divinity","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Legendary Power* Feat, *Super Saiyan God*, and *Full Power Super Saiyan*.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5755,"endLine":5761},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5997e56e41712453","name":"Energy of the Divine Realm","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Action to take the <em>Attack Action</em> or use a <strong>Technique</strong>, you may also expend your Bonus Action to empower it with divine energy. Change the <em>Damage Type</em> of the attack you are using to <em>Radiant Damage</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shinling-energy-of-the-divine-realm","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1264,"endLine":1275},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Shinling"}}}
{"_id":"5a271ba8c3a6ac44","name":"Chronin","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Dexterity</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With the blood of the Adapting Chronins you gain their innate ability to control time and gain access to Chronal Manipulation. The chronins are able to adapt quickly and learn as they fight Whenever you are hit with a critical hit roll a d20 check with a DC starting at 12, increasing by 2 each time you succeed. On a Successful check you gain 1 training boon. These boons must be used immediately at the start of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-chronin","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1540,"endLine":1544},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"5a5a7a35c5a66d48","name":"Combat Awareness","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Thanks to your keen observation skills in combat. You have <em>Advantage</em> on all <em>Skill Checks</em> made to determine what an opponent's move is and how it works. You may also do <em>Insight, Investigation,</em> or <em>Perception Skill Checks</em> during combat as a Bonus Action.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"combat-awareness","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6106,"endLine":6109},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"5b18dc6646c9a127","name":"Beyond SSGSS 2","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Beyond SSGSS</em> and <em>Super Saiyan 3***\nYou have the ability to use *Super Saiyan 3 and Super Saiyan God</em> as a **Combination Transformation</strong>. This <strong>Combination Form</strong> is known as <em>Super Saiyan God Super Saiyan 3</em> or shortened to <em>Super Saiyan Blue 3.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beyond-ssgss-2","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Beyond SSGSS* and *Super Saiyan 3","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5663,"endLine":5677},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5b40c6b06ad20cee","name":"Time Thief","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The ability to store time is just that, an ability. For you however it is a part of your very DNA and you've become even better at the act.</p>\n<p>You gain 2 <strong>Time Points</strong> per <strong>Stamina</strong> spent instead of 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-thief","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5841,"endLine":5845},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5bab286def296792","name":"Super Stamina","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you may ignore the first <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em>. You still die at 10 <em>Ranks of Exhaustion</em>.</p>\n<p>You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> more than once, letting you ignore an additional <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> each time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"super-stamina","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6342,"endLine":6346},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"5bf46b9320c82d2c","name":"Golden Monkey Artistey King","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Super Saiyan 3</em> and <em>Golden Great Ape</em> Feat.</strong>\nYou no longer need to make control checks for using <em>Super Saiyan 2</em> while using <em>Great Ape</em>. While using <em>Great Ape</em> you may now use <em>Super Saiyan 3</em> but make <em>Berserk Checks</em> at disadvantage while it is active.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"golden-monkey-artistey-king","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Super Saiyan 3* and *Golden Great Ape* Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5642,"endLine":5656},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5c3f53abfc246b58","name":"Lightly Armored","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have trained to master the use of light armor, gaining the following benefits.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency with light armor.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"lightly-armored","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5319,"endLine":5324},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5d1cc3d4c5e16805","name":"No one's Trained!","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The <em>Fusion Dance</em> is a unique ability in that anyone of <strong>Ki Rank 2</strong> or higher can use this feature. So long as someone who knows it is present and capable of instructing you for at least 1 hour you may use the fusion dance with Disadvantage for the next 24 hours.</p>\n<p>If the instructor is present for the attempt to instruct you then roll without disadvantage.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"no-one-s-trained","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":2,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Metamoran"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3558,"endLine":3564}}}}
{"_id":"5dd3b3a911bf76f5","name":"Survivor","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You attain the pinnacle of resilience in battle. At the start of each of your turns, you regain <strong>HP</strong> equal to 5 + your <em>Constitution Modifier</em> if you have less than half of your <strong>Maximum HP</strong> left. You don't gain this benefit if you have 0 <strong>HP</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"survivor","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6347,"endLine":6349},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"5e1166de0a954865","name":"Demonic energy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to the strange energy flowing through you, creatures without <strong>God Ki</strong> treat your <em>Passive Ki Stealth</em> and <em>Ki Stealth Checks</em> as 5 higher than it would actually be.</p>\n<p>You gain the <strong>Fiend Tag</strong> and count as a <em>Kai</em> for the purpose of features such as the <em>Potara Earrings</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mashin-jin-demonic-energy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":969,"endLine":974},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Mashin-jin"}}}
{"_id":"5e8a5a16bf5c57e5","name":"Athlete","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have undergone extensive physical training to gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>When you are prone, standing up uses only 5 feet of your movement.</li>\n<li>Climbing doesn't cost you extra movement.</li>\n<li>You can make a running long jump or a running high jump after moving only 5 feet on foot, rather than 10 feet.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"athlete","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5220,"endLine":5229},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5ed0b885be9b6573","name":"Kai-Kai","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>For 7 <strong>Stamina</strong> you may cast the <em>Teleportation</em> <strong>Spell</strong> with Advantage on your <em>Destination Roll</em>. This may move you between the <em>Other World</em>, <em>Mortal Realm</em>, and <em>Land of the Kais</em> but not between <em>Universes</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kai-kai","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Supreme Kai"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3662,"endLine":3664}}}}
{"_id":"5f09bb967b771980","name":"Monkey Artistey King","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Limit Breaker</strong>\nYou may use <em>Super Saiyan God</em> and <em>Super Saiyan 4</em> as a <strong>Combination Transformation</strong> known as <em>Super Saiyan 4 Limit Breaker.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"monkey-artistey-king","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Limit Breaker","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5606,"endLine":5627},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"5f7cfa909861d607","name":"Heroic Feature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Gain 2 features from the <strong>Heroic Features List</strong>. Every time you get this <strong>Class Feature</strong> after the first time, you gain 1 additional <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-heroic-feature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3012,"endLine":3013},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"5f91e240c7dd1db8","name":"Adaptability","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your race survives on it's ability to learn and adapt to threats. Whenever you are hit with a <em>Critical Hit</em>, roll a <em>d20 Check</em> with a DC starting at 12, increasing by 2 each time you succeed. On a successful check you gain 1 <strong>Training Boon</strong>. These <strong>Training Boons</strong> must be used immediately or at the start of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronin-adaptability","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1674,"endLine":1677},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Chronin"}}}
{"_id":"5f963aa8d5e98938","name":"Magical Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all <em>Intelligence, Charisma</em>, and <em>Wisdom Saving Throws</em> against magic.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"majin-magical-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1865,"endLine":1867},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Majin"}}}
{"_id":"5fddfb6b1f3a623c","name":"Animal Reflexes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your animal nature gives you senses and reaction time. You gain a bonus to your <strong>AC</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beastmen-animal-reflexes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":757,"endLine":758},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Beastmen"}}}
{"_id":"6021d7a7208ffc69","name":"Saiyan Genetics","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Saiyan genes vary slightly the mix of Saiyans following the tournament of power. Regardless of your choice, you are eligeble for <em>Super Saiyan God</em> <strong>Form</strong> and it's ritual. You gain access to <em>Saiyan</em> <strong>Feats</strong> and you must choose your bloodline from the following list:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Universe 7 &quot;The Kaleidoscope of Transformations&quot;</li>\n<li>Universe 6 &quot;Masters of Super Saiyan&quot;</li>\n<li>Mutant Saiyan &quot;Explosive Power&quot;</li>\n<li>Ancient Saiyan &quot;Power of Legends&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Universe 7</h5>\n<p>You gain access to <em>Saiyan</em> <strong>Feats</strong> with the <strong>U7 Tag</strong> and <strong>Feats</strong> in the <em>Universe 7 Saiyan</em> section. You also gain the <em>Saiyan Pride</em> and <em>Saiyan Tail</em> <strong>Features</strong>:\nRuthless and battle hungry, Universe 7 Saiyans lived many years as planet conquerors and soldiers with the help of their tail and the mighty great ape transformation.</p>\n<h6>Saiyan Tail</h6>\n<p>Long enough to be wrapped around one's waist. It cannot lift anything over 10 pounds, and is susceptible to pain.</p>\n<p>If your tail is ever severed it will regrow after 1d4 weeks, so long as you are <strong>Level 5</strong> or below. A creature may attempt to make a special <em>Grapple Check</em> against your tail as an Action, having Disadvantage on the check, <em>Restraining</em> the Saiyan on a Success.</p>\n<p>While you have your Tail you may use <strong>Great Ape</strong> <em><strong>Forms</strong></em>.</p>\n<h6>Saiyan Pride</h6>\n<p>Due to your indomitable spirit and pride you have advantage on saves against being <em>Charmed</em> or <em>Frightened</em>. You can not be put to sleep by magical means.</p>\n<h5>Universe 6</h5>\n<p>You gain access to <em>Saiyan</em> <strong>Feats</strong> with the <strong>U6 Tag</strong> and <strong>Feats</strong> in the <em>Universe 6 Saiyan</em> section. You also gain the <em>Super Saiyan Superiority</em> <strong>Feature</strong>:\nOtherwise known as <em>Tail-less Saiyans</em>, these are an alternate, or perhaps even future, evolution to the <em>Universe 7 Saiyans</em>. These Saiyans eventually lost their tails, replacing them with much higher <em>S-Cells</em> numbers. This change resulted in stronger, though slower to obtain, <em>Super Saiyan</em> <strong>Forms.</strong></p>\n<h6>Super Saiyan Superiority</h6>\n<p>Saiyans in Universe 6 got to live a much more peaceful lifestyle, this peace and happiness evolved the saiyans into having higher S-cell counts than Universe 7 Saiyan.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you have the <strong>Super Saiyan</strong> feature you unlock <em>Super Saiyan</em> at <strong>Level 8 or above</strong> whenever you first become <em>Enraged</em>.</li>\n<li>Any <strong>Form</strong> with <em>&quot;Super Saiyan&quot;</em> in its name, except for <em>Super Saiyan God</em> and <em>Super Saiyan Grades</em>, takes 1 less <strong>Stamina</strong> per round to maintain to a minimum of 1 <strong>Stamina</strong>.</li>\n<li>Any <strong>Form</strong> with <em>&quot;Super Saiyan&quot;</em> in its name, except <em>Super Saiyan God</em> and <em>Super Saiyan Grades</em>, gains an additional +1 <strong>Power Bonus</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Mutant</h5>\n<p>You gain access to <em>Saiyan</em> <strong>Feats</strong> with the <strong>Mutant Tag</strong> and <strong>Feats</strong> in the <em>Mutant Saiyan</em> section. You gain the <em>S-Cell Overload</em> <strong>Feature</strong> and your choice of one of the following <strong>Features</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>(a) <em>Uncontrollable Saiyan Power</em> <strong>or</strong> (b) <em>Unstoppable Force</em>\nSaiyans that were born with a genetic mutation and produce incredible amounts of S-cells, unfortunately, many can't control this power.</li>\n</ul>\n<h6>S-Cell Overload</h6>\n<p>If you have the <em>Super Saiyan</em> <em><strong>Racial Feature</strong></em> you gain the <em>Mutant Saiyan</em> <strong>Forms</strong> instead.</p>\n<h6>Uncontrollable Saiyan Power</h6>\n<p>You possess an overly powerful <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Form</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain the <em>Saiyan Tail</em> <strong>Feature</strong> from <em>Universe 7 Saiyans</em>.</li>\n<li>You automatically fail all checks to control the <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong> but gain an additional +1 Power while in a <strong>Oozaru</strong> <em>family</em> <em><strong>Form</strong></em>.</li>\n<li>If <em>Ozaru Fury</em> is used in Conjunction with a <em>&quot;Berserk Super Saiyan&quot;</em> <em><strong>Form</strong></em> you have disadvantage on your <em>Berserk</em> saving throw.</li>\n<li>Whenever you have the <em>Enraged</em> condition you automatically fail all <em>Berserk</em> Saving Throws.</li>\n</ul>\n<h6>Unstoppable Force</h6>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain an additional +1 <strong>Stamina</strong> at <strong>Level</strong> 1 and everytime you level up.</li>\n<li>Whenever you have the <em>Enraged</em> condition you automatically fail all <em>Berserk</em> Saving Throws.</li>\n<li>You can not gain any <strong>Forms</strong> from the <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Family</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Ancient</h5>\n<p>You gain access to <em>Saiyan</em> <strong>Feats</strong> with the <strong>Ancient Tag</strong> and feats in the <em>Ancient Saiyan</em> section. You gain the <em>Ancient Power</em>, <em>Prehensile Tail</em>, and <em>Nose For Battle</em> <strong>Features</strong>:\nSaiyans from ancient times before the development of the <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Form</strong>.</p>\n<h6>Ancient Power</h6>\n<p>If you have the <em>Super Saiyan</em> <em><strong>Racial Feature</strong></em> you gain the <em>Ancient Saiyan</em> <strong>Forms</strong> instead.</p>\n<h6>Prehensile Tail</h6>\n<p>You have a tail identical to <em>&quot;Saiyan Tail&quot;</em> but without the weakness to grappling and the <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n<h6>Nose For Battle</h6>\n<p>Saiyans in ancient times were blessed with the ability to &quot;sniff out&quot; strong foes. Due to their lack of understanding of true Ki capabilities, this was done in a much more true sense. You can sniff out creatures with a Power Level that are not <em>Concealing</em> their Ki.</p>\n<p>As an Action on your turn, make a <em>Wisdom (Perception) Check</em> at Advantage to <em>Sense Ki</em> at a <strong>Continental Scale</strong>. You have an inate sense of the location and <strong>Power Level</strong> of any creature you sense with this method so long as you hold <em>Concentration</em> and they remain on the same Continent as you, or the equivalent distance.\nYou may use this <strong>Feature</strong> at any time and it is not effected by <strong>Ki Exhaustion</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyans-saiyan-genetics","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1098,"endLine":1213},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Saiyans"}}}
{"_id":"60624178966557bb","name":"Kai Sorcery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain access to 2 options from the <em>Metamagic</em> <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>. This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken twice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kai-sorcery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5810,"endLine":5813},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"60b0fc6d17ac7eb5","name":"Martial Arts Devotee","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are devoted to the ways of the fist and nothing else. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> deal +2 Damage.</li>\n<li>Your <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> deal -2 Damage, minimum 1.</li>\n<li>You take -1 damage from all <em>Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing Damage</em>.</li>\n<li>You take +1 Damage from all <strong>Ki Techniques and Spells.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-arts-devotee","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6213,"endLine":6220},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"60ec0c5f44597c9a","name":"Egotistical Lust","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Ultra Ego</strong>\nWhen you would take damage, you may spend your Reaction to store the damage within. Until the end of your next turn, you write down the amount of damage you've taken. The next time you would deal damage, you may add the damage that you've accumulated onto the damage you deal.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"egotistical-lust","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Ultra Ego","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6040,"endLine":6044},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"611557bdf39d0e2c","name":"Maximum Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the <em>Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 5</strong> and the <em>Super Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 10</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"greys-maximum-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1812,"endLine":1817},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Greys"}}}
{"_id":"615d7975333115f1","name":"Durable","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Hardy and resilient, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>When you roll a Hit Die to regain hit points, the minimum number of hit points you regain from the roll equals twice your Constitution modifier (minimum of 2).</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"durable","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5273,"endLine":5278},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"61677a932c563cf1","name":"Weapon Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have practiced extensively with a variety of weapons, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency with four weapons of your choice. Each one must be a simple or a martial weapon.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"weapon-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"You gain proficiency with four weapons of your choice. Each one must be a simple or a martial weapon.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5489,"endLine":5495},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"6169bd935d23182d","name":"General Upgrade","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hardware or software has been improved. Gain 4 points to distribute to your Ability Scores or gain an Android <strong>Power-Up</strong>. This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken once per <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"general-upgrade","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5804,"endLine":5807},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"62779c52c3d5b1df","name":"Powerful Energy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You <em>Basic Ki Blast</em> has it's <em>Damage Die</em> increased by 1 step. (1d4&gt;1d6&gt;1d8&gt;1d10&gt;1d12&gt;2d6&gt;2d8&gt;etc)</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"yardratian-powerful-energy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2196,"endLine":2198},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Yardratian"}}}
{"_id":"627ebd0a49a76e3f","name":"Directed Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may now add half of your <strong>Power Bonus</strong> to <em>Athletics</em> and <em>Acrobatics Skill Checks</em>. You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> a second time to add your entire <strong>Power Bonus</strong> instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"directed-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6120,"endLine":6122},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"628dc9b93e019d12","name":"Arcosian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Intellegence</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With the DNA of the unstoppable Arcosians your body hardens with natural armor gaining +1 bonus to AC. You also gain access to the gates of power transformations up to 4th form</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-arcosian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1524,"endLine":1528},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"62def8655c40f51a","name":"Spirit Calm","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a 1d4 bonus to all <em>Charm</em> and <em>Berserk Saving Throws</em>. You may <em>Master</em> this feature like a <em><strong>Technique</strong></em> once at <strong>Ki Rank 2, 3,</strong> and <strong>4</strong> increasing the Die size by 1 step each time.</p>\n<p>When this <strong>Trained Feature</strong> has 3 <em>Ranks of Mastery</em>, you may end the <em>Charmed</em> or <em>Berserk Conditions</em> on yourself as a Reaction a number of times equal to your Wisdom Modifier per Long Rest, minimum of 1 time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-calm","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":2,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3441,"endLine":3445}}}}
{"_id":"632fd138dc67180b","name":"Big-Gete Features","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<h5>Metal Wire Construction</h5>\n<p>You have the ability to stitch your body back together with your control of the micromachines making up your body. As an Action on your turn you may spend <strong>Ki</strong> to heal yourself, 1 <strong>HP</strong> for every 2 <strong>Ki</strong> spent.</p>\n<p>Additionally you gain the ability to unravel your form temporarily to attempt to grapple a target. As an Action on your turn you may make an unarmed strike against a target in melee range, dealing 0 damage and <em>Grappling</em> the target on a hit. You may grapple targets 1 <em>Size Category</em> larger than usual in this way.</p>\n<h5>Big Gete Star Cloning</h5>\n<p>As an Action on your turn you may spend <strong>Hit Die</strong> to create lesser copies of yourself. Each clone costs 2 <strong>Hit Dice</strong> that you can not regain until the clone is killed or dispelled as an Action on your turn. Clones have the following traits and features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You may create a maximum number of clones equal to half your Proficiency Bonus, rounded down.</li>\n<li>All clones have your <em>Ability Score and Class Features</em> with half your Proficiency Bonus rounded down.</li>\n<li>Each Clone has HP equal to the maximum amount of a single <strong>Hit Die</strong> spent in the creation, taking the higher leveled option in the event of <em>Multi-Classing.</em><ul>\n<li>For Example: a Mystic/Bruiser (lvl 6/4) would use their Mystic <strong>Hit Die</strong> due to having more levels in that class.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Clones use <em>your</em> <strong>Ki</strong> for <strong>Techniques</strong> and <strong>Features</strong> and have no access to <strong>Stamina</strong>.</li>\n<li>Clones have thier turn immedietly following yours in initiative but only have a Single Action per turn to <strong>Cast a Technique</strong> or take the <strong>Attack, Dash, Disengage, or Dodge Actions</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Draining Grapple</h5>\n<p>Whenever you have a target <em>Grappled</em> you may use your Bonus Action to drain 1d4 <strong>Stamina</strong> from the target.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"cyborg-big-gete-features","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2310,"endLine":2331},"contentCategory":"subraceVariant","grantedBy":"Cyborg"}}}
{"_id":"633f5030760ab974","name":"Metamorian Equipment","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When 2 characters fuse using this method, unlike a true fusing of equipment like with the <em>Potara Earrings</em>, a <em>Metamorian Fusion</em> has all <em>Armor</em> replaced with clothes in the Metamorian style. You may choose what <em>Weapons</em> you had prior to the fusion to keep and which get melded into your form for the duration of the <em>Fusion.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"metamorian-equipment","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Metamoran"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3553,"endLine":3554}}}}
{"_id":"63f8b047544d6add","name":"Slasher","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned where to cut to have the greatest results, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>Once per turn when you hit a creature with an attack that deals slashing damage, you can reduce the speed of the target by 10 feet until the start of your next turn.</li>\n<li>When you score a critical hit that deals slashing damage to a creature, you grievously wound it. Until the start of your next turn, the target has disadvantage on all attack rolls.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"slasher","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5439,"endLine":5447},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"6579e7f4ec08b2be","name":"Superiority: Combat","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one class of <strong>Technique</strong>: <em>Beam, Blast, Barrage, Omni, Weapon, or Melee.</em> You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> when using this type of <strong>Technique</strong>. At <strong>Level 7</strong> this becomes +2 and at <strong>Level 13</strong> you get to pick a second type of <strong>Technique</strong> to gain this bonus as well.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 18</strong> you get an additional +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> that you can place on any class of <strong>Technique</strong>, regardless of if you choose that category previously.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyans-superiority-combat","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1085,"endLine":1088},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Saiyans"}}}
{"_id":"65efd825eb4c38fa","name":"Heroic Inspiration","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can inspire others through stirring words or music. As a Bonus Action on your turn, choose one creature other than yourself within 60 feet of you who can hear you. That creature gains one <strong>Heroic Inspiration Die</strong>, a d6.</p>\n<p>Once within the next 10 minutes, the creature can roll the die and add the number rolled to one <em>Ability Check, Attack Roll,</em> or <em>Saving Throw</em> they make. The creature can wait until after it rolls the d20 to decide to use the <strong>Heroic Inspiration Die</strong>, but must decide before the DM says whether the roll succeeds or fails. Once the <strong>Heroic Inspiration Die</strong> is rolled, it is lost. A creature can have only one (set of in the case of 2d6) <strong>Heroic Inspiration Die</strong> at a time.</p>\n<p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your <em>Charisma Modifier</em>, minimum of once. You regain any expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>\n<p>Your <strong>Heroic Inspiration Die</strong> changes when you reach certain <strong>Hero</strong> levels in this class as shown in the <strong>Heroic Presence Table</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-heroic-inspiration","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3127,"endLine":3144},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"67028b2452043200","name":"Fist of the God King","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While perhaps arrogantly named, the Kaio-Ken is an incredibly powerful ability that quickly and forcibly multiplies the user's abilities while tearing the body apart with the backlash.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Kaio-Ken!</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"fist-of-the-god-king","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; North Kaio"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3631,"endLine":3635}}}}
{"_id":"687ba58ec086e72f","name":"Dragon Ball Improvement","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Dragon Ball Creation</strong>\nYou have learned the ancient rite to improve your <em>Set of Dragon Balls</em>. As an hour long <em>Ritual</em>, you may increase the <em>Wish Count</em> by 1 or halve the <em>Recharge Time</em> of your <em>Set of Dragon Balls.</em>\n<strong>This Trained Feature can only be learned once.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dragon-ball-improvement","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Requires: Dragon Ball Creation","tags":"trained feature; Guardian of the Dragon Balls"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3594,"endLine":3602}}}}
{"_id":"6983c8d1fa46918d","name":"Korrin's Tower","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Before you stands a tower ascending to the heavens and your job is to climb to the top and meet this land's guardian.  By spending 1 day you may attempt 5 consecutive <strong>DC 15</strong> <em>Athletics Checks</em>  to succeed this task.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"korrin-s-tower","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"ordeal","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"ordeal"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3330,"endLine":3332}}}}
{"_id":"69d4ddd11281f0e4","name":"Spirit Bomb","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>&quot;Give me strength, from the forests, and rushing brooks and streams. For people everywhere who can't protect themselves... for the animals of the wild, and for life it's self. Give me strength for them. Thank you.&quot;</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Spirit Bomb</em> <strong>Technique</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-bomb","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; North Kaio"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3636,"endLine":3658}}}}
{"_id":"6a1c3a99aacd32ae","name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beginning at <strong>5th Level</strong>, and again at <strong>13th</strong> and <strong>20th Level</strong>, you may make an additional attack as part of your <em>Attack Action</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-extra-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2665,"endLine":2668},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"6ad11859758056bf","name":"Tough","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by an amount equal to twice your level when you gain this feat. Whenever you gain a level thereafter, your hit point maximum increases by an additional 2 hit points.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"tough","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5479,"endLine":5481},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"6ae72278df6e28fd","name":"Namekian Biology","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Namekians do not eat and survive only off of water. Due to this liquid nature namekians are able to stretch thier limbs for combat and utility purposes.</p>\n<p>Your <em>Unarmed Strikes</em>, <em>Melee Weapon Attacks</em> and <strong>Melee/Melee Weapon Techniques</strong> gain 5 feet of the <em>Reach Property</em> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>. When you make a <em>Grapple Check</em> you count as 1 <em>Size Category</em> larger for each rank of <em>Reach Property</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-namekian-biology","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1932,"endLine":1936},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Namekian"}}}
{"_id":"6b1bbc8cd9968688","name":"Spell Slinger","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may replace a number of <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or <em>Basic Ki Blast</em> attack done as part of the <em>Attack Action/Ki Blast Action</em>, to a max equal to your <em>Spell Casting Modifier</em>, with a <strong>Cantrip</strong> that you know.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spell-slinger","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6324,"endLine":6326},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"6b7974f807747642","name":"Rigorous Dicipline","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Yardratians are famous for their training methods and determination. You gain a <strong>Technique</strong> every time you <strong>Level-Up</strong> to 20 and 2 <strong>Techniques</strong> every level beyond. You also gain 1 additional <em>Training Boon</em> each time you have a <strong>Training Arc</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"yardratian-rigorous-dicipline","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2190,"endLine":2193},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Yardratian"}}}
{"_id":"6bd6db6caa2a06db","name":"Blood of Sesa","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one feature from the <em>Esoteric Arts</em> <strong>Class Feature.</strong></p>\n<p>This feat can be taken twice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blood-of-sesa","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5825,"endLine":5830},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"6bd8b0d74e8cedd6","name":"Masters of Spirit","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have spent your life in tune with your own spirit and due to this you can manipulate it with little effort.</p>\n<p>You gain the option to reduce the casting time of any <em>Spirit Control</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> you use by 1 step.</p>\n<p>(Action&gt;Bonus Action&gt;Reaction)</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"yardratian-masters-of-spirit","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2199,"endLine":2216},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Yardratian"}}}
{"_id":"6c0c2ecdcca2dc38","name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beginning at <strong>5th Level</strong>, you can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the <em>Attack Action</em> on your turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-extra-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2902,"endLine":2904},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"6cf89efd87e48b7c","name":"Complete Conversion","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: a Racial Form currently copied by Mystical Mimicry</strong>\nYou have taken the leap and partially converted your DNA into that of another race. You permanently keep the <strong>Racial Form</strong> you have copied as well as any lower forms in its <strong>Family.</strong> This <strong>Form</strong> now counts as your own and not part of <strong>Mystical Mimicry.</strong></p>\n<p>You may now take <strong>Feats</strong> as if you were that <strong>Race</strong> to gain additional <strong>Forms</strong> in that <strong>Family.</strong>\n<strong>This Feat can never be taken again.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"complete-conversion","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: a Racial Form currently copied by Mystical Mimicry","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5887,"endLine":5894},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"6e0070be673ef353","name":"Hellish Resistance","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to 1 <em>Damage Type</em> of your choice, this can not be changed later.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"demon-hellish-resistance","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1729,"endLine":1731},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Demon"}}}
{"_id":"6e89675545b6ac71","name":"Blast Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <em>+1 Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Blast Techniques</strong> and add half of your <em>Wisdom Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em>.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a second time to gain an addition +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> and you may now add your total <em>Wisdom Modifier</em> to their <em>Damage Rolls</em> instead of half.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blast-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6084,"endLine":6092},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"6fe4375a5b798292","name":"Medium Armor Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have practiced moving in medium armor to gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wearing medium armor doesn't impose disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</li>\n<li>When you wear medium armor, you can add 3, rather than 2, to your AC if you have a Dexterity of 16 or higher.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"medium-armor-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5345,"endLine":5350},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"7041f9d02520fdc5","name":"Limitations","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Characters may only fuse with this method if they are of the same size category and no more than 1 <strong>Character Level</strong> apart.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"limitations","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Metamoran"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3555,"endLine":3557}}}}
{"_id":"70722110089e9ad7","name":"Realm of the Gods","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Super Saiyan God</strong> and <strong>Super Saiyan 1/Controlled Super Saiyan 1/Legendary Super Saiyan</strong>\nYou have learned to mix Super Saiyan with the energy of the gods and unlocked a new divine level of power. You can use <em>Super Saiyan God</em> as a <strong>Power-Up</strong> while your required <strong>Transformation</strong> listed above is active.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"realm-of-the-gods","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Super Saiyan God** and **Super Saiyan 1/Controlled Super Saiyan 1/Legendary Super Saiyan","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5520,"endLine":5526},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"70b2406d67372419","name":"Heavy strikes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your <em>Unarmed Strike Damage Die</em> is increased by 1 step as long as the <em>Attack Roll</em> is made using <strong>Strength</strong>. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken up to 3 times.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"heavy-strikes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6156,"endLine":6158},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"71a9104dd2e1e715","name":"Size Manipulation","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may cast the Enlarge/Reduce Spell on <strong>yourself</strong> as a Bonus Action on your turn. This <strong>Spell</strong> is cast as if through the <em>Mysticism</em> <strong>Class Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"size-manipulation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3435,"endLine":3437}}}}
{"_id":"725bd5c5243a03b7","name":"Demonic Bloodline","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You hold the blood of the great old one Sesa and have access to <em>Mashin-jin</em> <strong>Forms</strong> as laid out in the <em><strong>Forms Chapter</strong></em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mashin-jin-demonic-bloodline","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":975,"endLine":977},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Mashin-jin"}}}
{"_id":"729b64aaa122dec7","name":"Ultra Instinct Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: *Complete Ultra Instinct***\nThis **Feat</strong> can be taken 5 times granting the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The first time you take this <strong>Feat</strong>, you can now use <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> as a <strong>Power-Up</strong></li>\n<li>The second time you would pick this <strong>Feat</strong>, you would reduce the <strong>Stamina Cost</strong> of <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> by 1</li>\n<li>The third time you would pick this <strong>Feat</strong>, you can now use <em>Complete Ultra Instinct</em> as a <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</li>\n<li>The fourth time you would pick this <strong>Feat</strong>, you reduce the <strong>Stamina Cost</strong> of <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> and <em>Complete Ultra Instinct</em> by 1.</li>\n<li>The fifth time you would pick this <strong>Feat</strong>, you can now use <em>Mastered Ultra Instinct</em> as a <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do not gain these benefits before you have access to the effected <strong>Forms</strong> without activation restrictions.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ultra-instinct-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Complete Ultra Instinct","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6004,"endLine":6016},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"72ab221ff81a07b9","name":"Saiyan Elite","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Saiyan Tail</em> Racial Feature</strong>\nA high-class Saiyan is able to control their abilities and weaknesses, unlike the standard low class.</p>\n<p>You automatically pass checks to control the <em>Great Ape</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong> while not in a <strong>Super Saiyan Family Form</strong> and your <em>Saiyan Tail</em> <strong>Racial Feature</strong> no longer enforces <em>Restrained</em> when <em>Grappled</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyan-elite","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Saiyan Tail* Racial Feature","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5630,"endLine":5636},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"733f213099167a59","name":"Telepathy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Namekians can speak telepathically to anyone within a mile that they know well. This range is increased to 10 miles at <strong>Level 5</strong>, Continent-wide at <strong>Level 10</strong>, Planet-wide at <strong>Level 15</strong>, and Galaxy-wide at <strong>Level 20</strong>.</p>\n<p>If you can <strong>Sense Ki</strong> you can use this feature on any creature who's ki you can sense.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-telepathy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1937,"endLine":1951},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Namekian"}}}
{"_id":"740cc8d5c878b3ca","name":"Range Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <strong>Ki Technique</strong> type from Beam, Blast, Barrage or Omni. All <strong>Techniques</strong> with that type have their Range inxreased by 50%.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> came taken a second time, to either increase the range of the chosen type by another 50% or to choose another type of <strong>Ki Technique</strong> to gain the benefit instead.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"range-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6308,"endLine":6312},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"74f48f5db583df0f","name":"Chef","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Time and effort spent mastering the culinary arts has paid off. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Constitution or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency with cook’s utensils if you don’t already have it.</li>\n<li>As part of a short rest, you can cook special food, provided you have ingredients and cook's utensils on hand. You can prepare enough of this food for a number of creatures equal to 4 + your proficiency bonus. At the end of the short rest, any creature who eats the food and spends one or more Hit Dice to regain hit points regains an extra 1d8 hit points.</li>\n<li>With one hour of work or when you finish a long rest, you can cook a number of treats equal to your proficiency bonus. These special treats last 8 hours after being made. A creature can use a bonus action to eat one of those treats to gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chef","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5230,"endLine":5237},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"759b50637d364f83","name":"Ogre's Endurance","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action on your turn, you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> to gain Xd12 <strong>Temporary HP</strong> where X is equal to the <strong>Stamina</strong> spent. This <strong>Temporary HP</strong> disappears after 1 hour or whenever you gain another source of <strong>Temporary HP</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ogre-ogre-s-endurance","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1016,"endLine":1021},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ogre"}}}
{"_id":"762d04814d9be9c0","name":"Unyielding Stamina","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your reserves of stamina are deeper than most. Increase your <strong>Stamina</strong> by an amount equal to your <em>Character Level</em> and gain +1 <strong>Stamina</strong> every time you <em>Level-Up</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"unyielding-stamina","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5085,"endLine":5089},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"762d426952993cc7","name":"Muscular Durability","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your body is unnaturally durable. You gain a bonus to your <strong>AC</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ogre-muscular-durability","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1010,"endLine":1012},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ogre"}}}
{"_id":"77335ec9573ec1ea","name":"Ki Empowered Muscules","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you may gain a <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> to gain the <em>Empowered Condtion</em> for a number of rounds equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ki-empowered-muscules","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6199,"endLine":6204},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"780e08562a0bdb8d","name":"Master of Many","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to their wide range in variety amongst your race, you gain a free proficiency in any <em>Skill</em> or any <em>Tool</em> of their choice. You gain an additional <em>Skill</em> of your choice at levels 7 and 13. If you choose a <em>Skill</em> you already have proficiency in you gain <em>Expertise</em> in it.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"earthling-master-of-many","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":868,"endLine":871},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Earthling"}}}
{"_id":"78bcda42d285550e","name":"Earthling:","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 to any Ability Score</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Having Human DNA gives you their innate ability to learn and adapt. You gain proficiency in 2 Skills of your choice or Expertise in 1 skill. You also gain access to the super earthling transformation.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-earthling","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1550,"endLine":1555},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"79a0edb0353739d8","name":"Sharpshooter","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered ranged weapons and can make shots that others find impossible. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Attacking at long range doesn't impose disadvantage on your ranged weapon attack rolls.</li>\n<li>Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover.</li>\n<li>Before you make an attack with a ranged weapon that you are proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll. If that attack hits, you add +10 to the attack's damage.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sharpshooter","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5406,"endLine":5412},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"7ad1339f7771b807","name":"Legendary Control","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Full Power Super Saiyan</em> and <em>Legendary Power</em> Feat.</strong>\nYou channel the level of power to a point where you have gained a full control of the output of your full strength. You can master <em>Controlled Super Saiyan</em> as if it was a <strong>Technique</strong> to learn the <strong>Legendary Grades Power-Ups</strong> to use alongside it.</p>\n<p>When you learn the <em>Legendary Grade 4</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>, you may begin mastering <em>Super Saiyan Full Power</em> as well to gain the same benefit.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"legendary-control","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Full Power Super Saiyan* and *Legendary Power* Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5745,"endLine":5754},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"7b193c533cc51040","name":"Blood of the Great Ape","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/Ancient/Mutant, lv 3+</em>\nA Saiyan alpha in ancient times was said to be a Great Ape as a man. You are a new one.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Oozaru's Fury</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blood-of-the-great-ape","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5578,"endLine":5584},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"7c1868ee2a33b81f","name":"Energy of the Demon Realm","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Action to take the <em>Attack Action</em> or use a <strong>Technique</strong>, you may also expend your Bonus Action to empower it with demonic energy. Change the <em>Damage Type</em> of the attack you are using to <em>Necrotic Damage</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mashin-jin-energy-of-the-demon-realm","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":978,"endLine":989},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Mashin-jin"}}}
{"_id":"7c6df2f5a3a3d377","name":"Training Boons","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>&quot;Even a low-class warrior can surpass an elite. With enough hard work.&quot;</em> These words have echoed throughout history and inspired the greatest warriors of history.\nTraining Boons are bonus gained from <strong>Training Arcs</strong>, <strong>Ordeals</strong>, as well as <em><strong>Racial Features</strong></em> like <em>Zenkai Boost</em> and <em>Pure Progress</em>. These bonuses can boost your character in-between level-ups and can provide much needed time to master abilities and unlock <em><strong>Forms</strong></em> or other methods of empowerment.\nFor 1 <strong>Training Boon</strong> you may gain 1 of the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gain an additional <strong>Hit Die</strong> and <strong>Maximum HP</strong> as if you gained a <strong>Level</strong> based on your most recent <strong>Class Level</strong>.</li>\n<li>Gain <strong>Ki</strong> as if you gained a <strong>Level</strong> based on your most recent <strong>Class Level</strong>.</li>\n<li>Maximum <strong>Stamina</strong> increases by 2.</li>\n<li>Increase your <em>Base Walk Speed</em> by 5 feet</li>\n<li>Gain 1 <em>Rank of Mastery</em> to put in one of your <strong>Techniques</strong>.</li>\n<li>Learn a <strong>Technique</strong> of your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> that you qualify for.<ul>\n<li>You may not trade this <strong>Technique</strong> out on later <em>Level-Ups</em> or <strong>Training Arcs</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Gain proficiency in a <em>Skill</em> or <em>Toolkit</em> of your choice.\nFor 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong> you may gain 1 of the following:</li>\n<li>You may gain a <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> or a <strong>Feat</strong>.</li>\n<li>Increase an <strong>Ability Score</strong> by 2 or two <strong>Ability Scores</strong> by 1.</li>\n<li>Learn a <strong>Technique</strong> of a single <strong>Ki Rank</strong> higher than you currently are.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Gaining Additional Boons</h3>\n<h4>Optional Rule: Training Boon Exchanges</h4>\n<p>Whenever you gain an <strong>Ability Score Improvement</strong> you may replace the amount of points you may allocate into an equal amount of <strong>Training Boons</strong>.</p>\n<p>You may also replace gaining a <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> upon <strong>Level Up</strong> with gaining 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong>.</p>\n<h4>Downtime</h4>\n<p>When dealing with smaller units of <em>Downtime</em>, 10 weeks of <em>Downtime</em> equates to 1 <strong>Training Boon</strong>.  This time does not need to be consecutive.</p>\n<h4>Extreme Conditions</h4>\n<p>If you have a <strong>Training Arc</strong> under conditions such as extreme gravity or harsh enviroments such as a desert planet like <em>Vampa</em> you gain an additional <strong>Training Boon</strong> upon completion.</p>\n<h4>Time Chambers</h4>\n<p>Chambers of time dialation that stretch the passing of time into incredible lengths and comes in multiple variations. Each <em>Time Chamber</em> has a different amount of time covered and bonuses gained.</p>\n<p>You may spend a total of 1 year <em>Inside of a Time Chamber</em> per <strong>Ki Rank</strong> or immedietly roll on the <strong>Indefinite Madness Table</strong> from mental fatigue. You gain an additional year after you obtain <strong>God Ki.</strong></p>\n<h5>Galactic Patrol</h5>\n<p>You may enter this desert like chamber to experience 3 days in the time of 1. Training in this chamber allows for a <strong>Training Arc</strong> in 2 months.</p>\n<h5>Kami's Lookout</h5>\n<p>This massive white expanse is filled with heightened gravity and chaotic weather. A single day in the outside world is 1 year inside this <em>Time Chamber</em>. You also benefit from <em>Extreme Conditions</em> for each <strong>Training Arc</strong> spent in this Chamber.</p>\n<p>Due to the nature of this chamber it is incredibly taxing on the mind of the users, for each <strong>Training Arc</strong> you wish to attempt you must make 3 DC 15 <em>Saving Throws</em> using either your <em>Intellegence, Wisdom,</em> or <em>Charisma Score</em> (your choice) or roll on the <a href=\"https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Madness#content\">Indefinite Madness Table</a>. If you are in the <em>Time Chamber</em> with at least 1 other person you have Advantage on this roll.</p>\n<p>If you fail this roll you may choose to exit the <em>Time Chamber</em> early instead of rolling on the <em>Madness Table</em>, gaining only 1 <strong>Training Boon</strong> for each successful <em>Saving Throw</em> before you failed, spending 2 months in the chamber for each success.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"training-boons","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"boon","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"training boon options"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3259,"endLine":3322}}}}
{"_id":"7ceb56774983299b","name":"Self Indulgence","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Can be taken twice</strong>\nYou are becoming Destruction incarnate. You gain the <em>Ultra Ego</em> <strong>Form</strong>. If you take this <strong>Feat</strong> a second time you gain the <em>Burning Ultra Ego</em> <strong>Form.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"self-indulgence","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6045,"endLine":6051},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"7d421ffbbd5be128","name":"Corrupted Blood of the Shin-jins","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Fire</em> and <em>Necrotic Damage</em> as well as Advantage on <em>Spell Saving Throws</em>. Whenever you use the <strong>Block Manuever</strong> your <em>Resistance</em> becomes <em>Immunity</em> and you pass all <em>Spell Saving Throws</em> for the duration.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mashin-jin-corrupted-blood-of-the-shin-jins","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":951,"endLine":959},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Mashin-jin"}}}
{"_id":"7f49b7106ded8669","name":"Time Skip","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>1 Time Point</em>\nThe user’s first steps to chrono mastery, the user stops time for brief moments. As a Bonus Action on your turn or as a <strong>Clash</strong> to any <strong>Technique</strong> you may spend <em>Time Points</em> to give all creatures but you the <em>Frozen in Time Condition</em> as well as grant you additional <em>Movement Speed</em> and <em>Action Economy</em>.</p>\n<p>If used as a <strong>Clash</strong>, the other <strong>Technique</strong> finishes its casting at the end of <em>Time Skip</em> unless you damage them or otherwise hender their ability to cast. You gain the following <em>Movement Speed</em> and <em>Action Economy</em> based on the amount of <em>Time Points</em> you spend:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>1 <em>Time Point</em>: 1 Bonus Action &amp; 10 Feet of Movement</li>\n<li>2 <em>Time Points</em>: 1  Action &amp; 20 Feet of Movement</li>\n<li>3 <em>Time Points</em>: 1 Action and 1 Bonus Action &amp; 30 Feet of Movement</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Alternatively you may expend 3 <em>Time Points</em> at the start of your turn to end the <em>Frozen in Time Condition</em> on yourself.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-skip","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3477,"endLine":3488}}}}
{"_id":"807155371085d56f","name":"Dragon Soul","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You pull from your warrior spirit to empower you.\nOn your turn, you can activate your <em>Dragon Soul</em> as a Bonus Action.</p>\n<p>While active, you gain the following benefits if you aren't wearing <em>Heavy Armor</em>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You have Advantage on <em>Strength Checks</em> and <em>Strength Saving</em> Throws.</li>\n<li>When you make a <em>Melee Weapon Attack/Unarmed Attack</em> using <strong>Strength</strong> or a <strong>Melee Technique</strong>, you gain a +2 <em>Static Bonus</em>. This bonus increases as you level.</li>\n<li>You have <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing,</em> and <em>Slashing Damage</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your <em>Dragon Soul</em> lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you are knocked <em>Unconscious</em> or if your turn ends and you haven't attacked a hostile creature since your last turn or taken damage since then. You can also end your <em>Dragon Soul</em> as a free action at any time.</p>\n<p>You may activate <em>Dragon Soul</em> a number of times per long rest as shown on the <strong>Dragon Soul Table</strong> above,  you may activate it again past your maximum and gain a <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> when it ends.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-dragon-soul","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3000,"endLine":3011},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"80755899e9959f19","name":"Improved Critical","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Attack Rolls made from your <em>Attack Action</em>'and <em>Ki Blast Action</em> have their <em>Critical Threat Range</em> increased by 1. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a second time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"improved-critical","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6171,"endLine":6174},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"82724b6d46ba6dc8","name":"Yardratian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Wisdom</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your Yardratian DNA has manifested as a natural spirit contol. At level 1 you gain 1 Spirit Control Feature of your choice. You also gain an additional feature at Ki Rank 3.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-yardratian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1623,"endLine":1638},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"835eb1eeb245c947","name":"I’m Putting It All Into This","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Reaction when you roll damage for a <strong>Technique,</strong> you may expend up to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> in <strong>Hit Die</strong> to add the amount rolled to the <em>Damage Roll.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"im-putting-it-all-into-this","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6168,"endLine":6170},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"8360f2d684ebd5ed","name":"Mashin-jin","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Cannot be taken with Shinling DNA</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>+1 Constitution</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You have the blood of demons in you. You gain access to Mahshin-jin power ups\nAnd resistance to fire and necrotic damage. You can also empower an attack with demonic energy, when you deal damage you may use a bonus action to change its damage type to necrotic.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-mashin-jin","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1573,"endLine":1581},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"836edbe07b8dd645","name":"Training With A Partner","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>“Together, we form a necessary paradox; not a senseless contradiction.”</em>\nTraining with an adequate partner means training with another character within 3 <strong>Character Levels</strong> of your current <strong>Character Level</strong>. If the other character is more than 3 levels below you, you benefit as if you were <em>Solo Training</em> and they act as if <em>Training with a Master</em>.</p>\n<p>When training with a partner you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain 4 <strong>Training Boons</strong>, gaining an additional one for each 2 additional training partners.<ul>\n<li>Any 2 people in a <strong>Training Arc</strong> together like this may partner together and each expend <strong>Training Boons</strong> as listed below to teach something from one partner to the other:<ul>\n<li>1 <strong>Training Boon</strong>: 1 <strong>Technique</strong> that they fit the <em>Requirements</em> for.</li>\n<li>2 <strong>Training Boons</strong>: 1 Mortal <strong>Trained Feature</strong></li>\n<li>3 <strong>Training Boons</strong>: 1 Alien <strong>Trained Feature</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"training-with-a-partner","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"arc","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":26,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"training arc"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3231,"endLine":3244}}}}
{"_id":"83d1da74999852bc","name":"Action Surge","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional Action on top of your regular Action and a possible Bonus\naction. Once you use this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>, you must finish a Short or Long rest before you can use it again.</p>\n<p>This Action must be used to take the <em>Attack Action</em>, <em>Ki Blast Action</em>, cast a <strong>Spell</strong> or <strong>Technique</strong>, use an item, or take the <em>Dash, Dodge</em>, or <em>Disengage Action</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"action-surge","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"This Action must be used to take the *Attack Action*, *Ki Blast Action*, cast a **Spell** or **Technique**, use an item, or take the *Dash, Dodge*, or *Disengage Action*.","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6059,"endLine":6064},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"8431d713321eff04","name":"Mafuba","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The ancient method of sealing evil passed throughout the generations. You gain the <em>Evil Containment Wave</em> <strong>Technique.</strong></p>\n<h6>Evil Containment Wave</h6>\n<h2><em>Special Rank Technique</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Casting Cost:</strong>  5 <strong>Hit Die</strong>, this can reduce you below zero <strong>Hit Die</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Casting Time:</strong>  1 Action</li>\n<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> 1 Jar (or any other sealable container) and 1 Sealing Tag that cost 10,000 Zeni each</li>\n<li><strong>Casting Time:</strong> 1 Action</li>\n<li><strong>Range:</strong>  30 Feet</li>\n<li><strong>Chargeable?:</strong>          No</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong>          Instantaneous</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong>  Omni</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You use an empty bottle and seal a creature within range that you can see. The target of this <strong>Technique</strong> must make a <em>Constitution Saving Throw</em>, with advantage during <strong>Combat</strong>. Creatures who fail are immediately sealed within the jar and can only be let free if a creature spends an Action to unseal them.</p>\n<p>While in the <em>Jar</em>, a creature gains the <em>Paralyzed Condition</em>, even if they would be immune to it. They do not age, do need to eat, breathe, or sleep. The <em>Jar</em> has 1 <strong>Hit Point</strong> and has an <strong>AC</strong> of 5. If the <em>Jar</em> is within a creature's inventory, the <em>Jar</em> cannot be targeted.\n<strong>Hit Die</strong> expended to cast this <strong>Technique</strong> can never be recovered. You die at the completion of this <strong>Technique</strong> if your <strong>Hit Die</strong> would hit Zero or below.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mafuba","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Prerequisites:** 1 Jar (or any other sealable container) and 1 Sealing Tag that cost 10,000 Zeni each","tags":"trained feature; Turtle School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3382,"endLine":3402}}}}
{"_id":"84a5e9d34e35b736","name":"Omni Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a <em>+1 Static Bonus</em> to <strong>Omni Techniques</strong> and add half of your Int mod to damage rolls.</p>\n<p>Can be taken twice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"omni-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6277,"endLine":6281},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"84e8754abe0fed52","name":"True Body","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires Fourth Form</strong>\nYou have finally removed the limiters on your body and taken on your true form.</p>\n<p>You always appear to be in your Final Form, though you don’t gain the full benefits of the <strong>Transformation</strong>. You may no longer use the <em>Second, Third, or Fourth Form</em> <strong>Transformations</strong> but gain 2 <em>Ranks of the Light-Weight Condition</em>. You also gain +5 to <strong>Stamina</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"true-body","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires Fourth Form","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5781,"endLine":5787},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"8604ec47d2e9eaca","name":"Tri-Wielder","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Prerequisite: Duel-Wielder</em></p>\n<p>You master fighting with three weapons by holding one in your mouth, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your Duel-Wielding bonus to <strong>AC</strong> increases to +2.</li>\n<li>You can hold an additional offhand weapon with another appendage or with your mouth, and it doesn't have to be light. You can't make attacks with it.</li>\n<li>Choose one one-handed weapon you are proficienct with held in either hand during your turn, you may combine attacks made with that weapon with your third weapon to increase the chosen weapon's damage dice by one stage for the remainder of your turn. For example, a d4 damage die made with the weapon would become a d6 to hit, a d6 would become a d8, a d8 would become a d10, and a d10 would become a d12. The maximum the damage dice can increase to is a d12.</li>\n<li>You can draw or stow three one-handed weapons when you would normally be able to draw or stow only two.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"tri-wielder","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisite: Duel-Wielder","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5116,"endLine":5125},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"863efc50d0b89834","name":"Chronal Mastery","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>5 Time Points</em>\nThe user has complete mastery over time itself. As an Action you may touch 1 creature, completely reverse the last round of combat for the target. This reverses death, expended <strong>Resources</strong> such as <strong>HP, Ki,</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong>, as well as limited use <strong>Features</strong>.</p>\n<p>If used outside of combat the effect's scope increases to up to 1 minute.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronal-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3515,"endLine":3528}}}}
{"_id":"8741802a4fb480b5","name":"Battle Cry","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Ogres have a natural ability to inspire anger and aggression from those near them.</p>\n<p>You gain the following <strong>Omni Technique</strong> and it's rank matches your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>:</p>\n<h5>Battle Cry</h5>\n<p><em>Rank X Omni Technique</em></p>\n<p><strong>Cost:</strong>   1 Stamina\n<strong>Casting Time:</strong>   1 Bonus Action\n<strong>Range:</strong>          30 Feet\n<strong>Duration:</strong>       Special</p>\n<p>You attempt to compel a creature into a duel. One creature that you can see within range must make a <em>Wisdom Saving Throw</em>. On a failed save, the creature is drawn to you, compelled by your aggressive demand. For the duration, it has Disadvantage on <em>Attack Rolls</em> against creatures other than you, and must make a <em>Wisdom Saving Throw</em> each time it attempts to move to a space that is more than 30 feet away from you; if it succeeds on this <em>Saving Throw</em>, this <strong>Technique</strong> doesn’t restrict the target’s movement for that turn.</p>\n<p>The effects ends if you attack any unaffected creature, if you cast a <strong>Spell/Technique</strong> that targets a hostile creature other than a target, or if you end your turn more than 30 feet away from a target.</p>\n<p>For each additional <strong>Stamina</strong> you spend you may force an additional target in your range to make the <em>Saving Throw</em> as well, to a maximum number of targets equal to your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ogre-battle-cry","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1026,"endLine":1054},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ogre"}}}
{"_id":"8759f4560b4c3993","name":"God Ki Creation","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Can never be learned by another master.</strong></p>\n<p>You have been taught to create and harness the energy of the gods. Your <strong>Maximum God Ki</strong> increases by 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"god-ki-creation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Angel"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3704,"endLine":3707}}}}
{"_id":"87985d6e4827a856","name":"I’ll Take It!!!","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are so tought that you can shrug off danger instead of flee from it. If a <strong>Technique/Spell</strong> asks you to make a <em>Dexterity Saving Throw</em>, you can replace it with a <em>Constitution Saving Throw</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ill-take-it","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6165,"endLine":6167},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"87b05a7c6db33b94","name":"Hubris of Midus","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires &quot;True Body&quot; Feat.</strong>\nYou are the shining light this universe needs, only you have the power to change the fate of history.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Golden Form</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hubris-of-midus","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires \"True Body\" Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5788,"endLine":5794},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"8890779ff1927833","name":"Hyper Focus","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to put your whole body behind a <strong>Power-Up</strong>, allowing you to activate it in your <strong>Transformation Slot</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hyper-focus","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6159,"endLine":6161},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"8b63b2e54916cf86","name":"Overload Proof","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Increase your <strong>Power Overload Threshold</strong> by one. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken a number of times equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"overload-proof","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6282,"endLine":6284},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"8bc726aae79b3a0f","name":"Neko Majin","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Charisma</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your DNA is made up of a mystical species known for their copycat capabilities. you gain the <em>Eagled-Eyed Adaptation</em> <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> but you may use it a number of times per long rest equal to your Proficiency Bonus. You can memorize a number of <strong>Techniques</strong> equal to half your <strong>Intelligence Modifier</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-neko-majin","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1587,"endLine":1591},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"8c60aebfacf2e9e2","name":"Mage Slayer","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have practiced techniques in melee combat against spellcasters, gaining the following benefits.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When a creature within 5 feet of you casts a spell, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature.</li>\n<li>When you damage a creature that is concentrating on a spell, that creature has disadvantage on the saving throw it makes to maintain its concentration.</li>\n<li>You have advantage on saving throws against spells cast by creatures within 5 feet of you.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mage-slayer","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5335,"endLine":5344},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"8d3ec40d4c1933ee","name":"Sentinel","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered techniques to take advantage of every drop in any enemy's guard, gaining the following benefits.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you hit a creature with an opportunity attack, the creature's speed becomes 0 for the rest of the turn.</li>\n<li>Creatures provoke opportunity attacks from you even if they take the Disengage action before leaving your reach.</li>\n<li>When a creature makes an attack against a target other than you (and that target doesn't have this feat), you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against the attacking creature.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sentinel","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5399,"endLine":5405},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"8de1457e71f3207e","name":"Steadfast Strikes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you roll a 1 on a <em>Damage Die</em>, you may reroll it and then take the second roll instead. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> has 3 Charges, restored after a Short or Long Rest. If this is taken again the charges increase to 5.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"steadfast-strikes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6330,"endLine":6332},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"8e6f256e3675181f","name":"Unifying Presence","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>6th Level</strong> your unifying presence enhances the party’s ability to resist all manner of external attacks. As a Reaction to you or a creature that you can see making a <em>Saving Throw</em>, a number creatures of your choice (including yourself) up to your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> may add your charisma bonus to that <em>Saving Throw</em>. You can use this <strong>Feature</strong> after the rolls are made but not after the results are said. You must wait until you finish a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-unifying-presence","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3187,"endLine":3190},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"8eb9a71d586945de","name":"Predatory Combat","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your predatory nature shines when in combat. Your <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> can deal <em>Slashing Damage</em> and have their <em>Unarmed Strike Damage Die</em> increased by 1 step.</p>\n<p>On your turn if you take the <em>Attack Action</em>, <em>Ki Blast Action</em> or use a <strong>Technique</strong> that deals damage before you move or take any other action you gain +1 Power until the start of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sekhmen-jin-predatory-combat","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2139,"endLine":2144},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sekhmen-jin"}}}
{"_id":"8f7c045b51cce17f","name":"Hellish Fortitude","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have improved durability due to your unnatural body. All <strong>Hit Die</strong> you gain are increased by 1 step.</p>\n<p>(1d6&gt;1d8&gt;1d10&gt;1d12&gt;2d6)</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"demon-hellish-fortitude","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1732,"endLine":1745},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Demon"}}}
{"_id":"8f8d698926b1b3bd","name":"Blue Evolved","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Super Saiyan God Evolution</strong>\nYou may now use <em>Super Saiyan God Evolution</em> instead of <em>Super Saiyan God</em> for the <em>Super Saiyan Blue</em> <strong>Combination Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blue-evolved","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Super Saiyan God Evolution","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5541,"endLine":5548},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"90002af870b721dc","name":"Neo-Mutant Features (WIP)","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<h5>Liquid Metal Form</h5>\n<p>As an Action on your turn while you are making contact with metal outside of your own body you may sink into it, gaining a 60 foot movement speed while you are in this form. While in this form you can not be seen and you have <em>Advantage</em> on <em>Ki Stealth Checks</em> while submerged in the material.</p>\n<p>While in this form you still take damage if your space is attacked. You may not cast <strong>Techniques/Spells</strong> or make <em>Attack Rolls</em> while in this form.</p>\n<p>While in this state you may &quot;swim&quot; through all connected metal as well as see through the material to it's closest available line of sight. You may not use your Action or Bonus Actions to do anything except remove yourself from the metal or take the <em>Dash Action</em>.</p>\n<h5>Shape Form</h5>\n<p>As a Bonus Action on your turn you may spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> and convert your <em>Unarmed Strike</em> into a <em>Melee Weapon</em> of your choice until you change it's shape again as another Bonus Action.</p>\n<p>Returning to your original form does not require spending <strong>Stamina</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Weapon Attacks Rolls</em> and <strong>Techniques</strong> made with weapons made by this feature gain a <em>Static Bonus</em> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Superiority: Combat</h5>\n<p>Choose one class of <strong>Technique</strong>: <em>Beam, Blast, Barrage, Omni, Weapon, or Melee.</em> You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> when using this type of <strong>Technique</strong>. At <strong>Level 7</strong> this becomes +2 and at <strong>Level 13</strong> you get to pick a second type of <strong>Technique</strong> to gain this bonus as well.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 18</strong> you get an additional +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> that you can place on any class of <strong>Technique</strong>, regardless of if you choose that category previously.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"cyborg-neo-mutant-features-wip","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2332,"endLine":2357},"contentCategory":"subraceVariant","grantedBy":"Cyborg"}}}
{"_id":"9087e07a6599c7e9","name":"Beastmen","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 to any Ability Score</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Having DNA of animals within your body, you learn to become more animalistic. You gain the <strong>Predator or Prey</strong> feature from Beastmen and you may now comprehend with beasts.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-beastmen","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1529,"endLine":1533},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"90dc43a2e3dc82a0","name":"Maximum Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the <em>Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 5</strong> and the <em>Super Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> at <strong>Level 10</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alien-maximum-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1328,"endLine":1330},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Alien"}}}
{"_id":"91fd49c86d9fcecf","name":"Technique of the Gods","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires God Ki</strong></p>\n<p>You have learned to fight without thinking, the truest mark of divinity. You gain the <em>Ultra Instinct Omen</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"technique-of-the-gods","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Requires God Ki","tags":"trained feature; Angel"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3708,"endLine":3711}}}}
{"_id":"92c75ad75c9290bb","name":"Kaio-ken Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Kaio-ken!</strong>\nReduce the HP cost of all <em>Kaio-Ken</em> <strong>Forms</strong> by 1 (minimum 1).</p>\n<p>This <strong>Feat</strong> may be taken a number of times equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kaio-ken-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Kaio-ken!","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5997,"endLine":6002},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"934ab4b09d032a84","name":"Turtle School Spirit","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to put your entire spirit into an attack. Once per Long Rest you may grant yourself Advantage on a <strong>Clash</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"turtle-school-spirit","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Turtle School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3403,"endLine":3405}}}}
{"_id":"93554a3e197b42c1","name":"Natural Talent","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an <em>Ability Score Improvement</em> at <strong>level 1</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"earthling-natural-talent","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":859,"endLine":860},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Earthling"}}}
{"_id":"9369581db4f2e2b8","name":"Alert","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Always on the lookout for danger, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can't be surprised while you are conscious.</li>\n<li>You gain a +5 bonus to initiative.</li>\n<li>Other creatures don't gain advantage on attack rolls against you as a result of being unseen by you.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alert","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5213,"endLine":5219},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"93e88f32f25884a5","name":"Magic Blood","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have advantage on <em>Saving Throws</em> against being <em>Charmed</em>, and magic can't put you to sleep or <em>Enrage</em> you.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"konatsian-magic-blood","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":911,"endLine":913},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Konatsian"}}}
{"_id":"9484b8bf0fcb2ad2","name":"Weapon Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <em>Weapon</em> that you are proficient with, you may now increase the <em>Damage Die</em> you deal with these weapons by 1 step.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"weapon-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6379,"endLine":6381},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"9498dd181533f3d4","name":"Spellbook of Mekikabura","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain 3 <strong>Spells</strong> equal to or below 5th level and can cast them as if through <em>Mysticism</em> <strong>Class Feature.</strong></p>\n<p>This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken twice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spellbook-of-mekikabura","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5831,"endLine":5837},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"94a8390d945340e4","name":"Namekian Armada","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Fusing with at least 2 Namekians</strong>\nYou carry with you the might of Planet Namek. You can now use <em>Super Namekian</em> and <em>Namekian Split</em> as a <strong>Combination Transformation</strong> known as <em>Namekian Hero</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-armada","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Fusing with at least 2 Namekians","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5873,"endLine":5877},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"954976c9658feeba","name":"Flight","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> repeatedly to gain a 15 foot <em>Flight Speed</em> or increase your current <em>Flight Speed</em> by 15 feet.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"flight","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6150,"endLine":6152},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"957e66a7533812ce","name":"Space Knights","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to your upbringing on the fringes of the ancient and modern worlds has left you with a very unique set of skills. You gain proficiency in <em>Martial Weapons</em> and the <em>Technology Skill</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"konatsian-space-knights","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":904,"endLine":907},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Konatsian"}}}
{"_id":"95c33194278068bc","name":"Beyond SSGSS","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Divine Combination Feat</em> and <em>Super Saiyan 2***\nYou have the ability to use *Super Saiyan 2 and Super Saiyan God</em> as a **Combination Transformation</strong>. This <strong>Combination Form</strong> is known as <em>Super Saiyan God Super Saiyan 2</em> or shortened to <em>Super Saiyan Blue 2.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beyond-ssgss","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Divine Combination Feat* and *Super Saiyan 2","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5659,"endLine":5662},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"95d17780fbeaf174","name":"Magical Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have access to 1 branch of magic of your choice as if through the <em>Mysticism</em> <em><strong>Class Feature</strong></em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sateery-magical-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2076,"endLine":2078},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sateery"}}}
{"_id":"975e42037539ba02","name":"Ki Growth Training","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You increase your <strong>Maximum Ki</strong> by 1, whenever you gain a level thereafter, your <strong>Maximum Ki</strong> increases by 1. You may pick this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> multiple times, up to an amount equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>, gaining a +1 to your <strong>maximum ki points</strong> when you pick this feature and gaining a +1 to your <strong>Maximum Ki</strong> every level afterwards.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ki-growth-training","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6209,"endLine":6212},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"97840466a40056f9","name":"Tenacity","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you would hit 0 <strong>HP</strong> you instead drop to 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ceralians-tenacity","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":820,"endLine":823},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ceralians"}}}
{"_id":"979c4822ada44e4d","name":"Energy Thief","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you may radiate a 10 foot radius of Stamina draining energy. This radius increases by 10 feet each time your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> increases. This <strong>Feature</strong> requires concentration to maintain and cost at least 20 <strong>Ki</strong>.</p>\n<p>Whenever a creature enters this space or begin/ends it's turn in the radius you absorb 1 Stamina per 20 ki spent to maintain this feature.</p>\n<p>All <strong>Stamina</strong> gained in this way over your maximum becomes <strong>Temporary Stamina</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sateery-energy-thief","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2079,"endLine":2085},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sateery"}}}
{"_id":"97b11522f805fda1","name":"Keen Mind","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a mind that can track time, direction, and detail with uncanny precision. You gain the following benefits.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You always know which way is north.</li>\n<li>You always know the number of hours left before the next sunrise or sunset.</li>\n<li>You can accurately recall anything you have seen or heard within the past month.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"keen-mind","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5309,"endLine":5318},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"9a475e42d5bef2cb","name":"Spell Sniper","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned techniques to enhance your attacks with certain kinds of spells, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you cast a spell that requires you to make an attack roll, the spell's range is doubled.</li>\n<li>Your ranged spell attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover.</li>\n<li>You learn one cantrip that requires an attack roll. Your spellcasting modifier for this cantrip is either Charisma or Intellegence which you choose when you gain this Feat</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spell-sniper","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"When you cast a spell that requires you to make an attack roll, the spell's range is doubled.; You learn one cantrip that requires an attack roll. Your spellcasting modifier for this cantrip is either Charisma or Intellegence which you choose when you gain this Feat","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5448,"endLine":5454},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"9a5f20aa4414d7df","name":"Fighting Adaptability","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Prerequisites: 20+ Constitution</strong></p>\n<p>Your fighting grows in the middle of battle, allowing you to adapt and even match the strongest opponent there. You gain the <em>Pure-Progress</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"fighting-adaptability","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisites: 20+ Constitution","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5131,"endLine":5134},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"9b217ccdc6828f81","name":"Block Breaker","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at <strong>7th Level</strong>, once per Long Rest, when a target attempts to <strong>Block</strong> a <em>Melee Attack</em> or <strong>Melee/Melee Weapon Technique</strong> you may expend your reaction to power through, negating their <strong>Block</strong>.</p>\n<p>You gain an additional use of this <strong>Feature</strong> at <strong>11th Level</strong> and it recharges on a Short Rest at 15th Level.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-block-breaker","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3022,"endLine":3027},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"9cb156813ff1bee8","name":"Mobile","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are exceptionally speedy and agile. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your speed increases by 10 feet.</li>\n<li>When you use the Dash action, difficult terrain doesn't cost you extra movement on that turn.</li>\n<li>When you make a melee attack against a creature, you don't provoke opportunity attacks from that creature for the rest of the turn, whether you hit or not.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mobile","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5351,"endLine":5358},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"9ce65d3cb0dcd0d8","name":"Wrestling Control","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Berserker Super Saiyan***\nYou have learned to draw less power from your seemingly endless reservoir so you can remain in control. Shrinking to barely larger than your standard frames you gain bright green pupils and hair and have control of your mind once again. You gain the *Controlled Super Saiyan</em> **Transformation.</strong></p>\n<p>**This Feat must be obtained through <em>Training Boons</em> or by completing an *Ordeal***</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"wrestling-control","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Berserker Super Saiyan; This Feat must be obtained through *Training Boons* or by completing an *Ordeal","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5726,"endLine":5732},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"9f5f141d0cace287","name":"Kai Versatility","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain 3 <strong>Spells</strong> equal to or below 5th level and can cast them as if through <em>Mysticism</em> <strong>Class Feature.</strong></p>\n<p>This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken twice.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"kai-versatility","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5814,"endLine":5822},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"a059295a06af898a","name":"Magical Power Advancement","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken a number of times equal to half of your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>, rounded up.</em>\n<strong>Requires- Mysticism: Burst</strong></p>\n<p>You have pushed your magical capabilities beyond their maximum. Increase the <em>Spell Level</em> that you can learn for the <em>Mysticism: Burst</em> <strong>Class Feature</strong> by 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"magical-power-advancement","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires- Mysticism: Burst","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5135,"endLine":5141},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"a0c5409874a60f09","name":"Raw Talent","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Greys find themselves regularly surpassing the limitations of other races. A single <em>Ability Score Maximum</em> of your choice is increased by 4.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"greys-raw-talent","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1806,"endLine":1808},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Greys"}}}
{"_id":"a10036ae7e0c5741","name":"Defensive Duelist","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Prerequisite: Dexterity 13 or higher</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you are wielding a finesse weapon with which you are proficient and another creature hits you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction to add your proficiency bonus to your AC for that attack, potentially causing the attack to miss you.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"defensive-duelist","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisite: Dexterity 13 or higher","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5253,"endLine":5257},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"a2fafb3437b0fccf","name":"Divine Legacy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You slowly unlock the full power of the <em>Divine Realm</em>. You gain access to <em>Shin-jin</em> <strong>Feats</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>1st Level</strong>, you know the <em>Sacred Flame</em> <strong>Cantrip</strong>. When you reach <strong>3rd Level</strong>, you gain the <em>Prayer of Healing</em> <strong>Spell</strong>. When you reach <strong>5th Level</strong>, you gain the <em>Mass Healing Word</em> <strong>Spell</strong>. These <strong>Spells</strong> are cast through the <strong>Mysticism Feature</strong> but can not be casted at a higher <strong>Spell Level.</strong></p>\n<p>At <strong>10th Level</strong> you may cast these spells at a higher <strong>Spell Level</strong> as if through the <strong>Mysticism Feature</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>15th Level</strong> you may add any 3 <strong>Spells</strong>  of 5th level or below to this feature that deal <em>Radiant Damage</em>, grants <strong>HP</strong> or <strong>Temporary HP</strong>, or otherwise restores or heals a target.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shinling-divine-legacy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1246,"endLine":1255},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Shinling"}}}
{"_id":"a34a6740091824f0","name":"Alien Battle Instincts","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Short or Long Rest, you can enter the <em>Enraged Condition</em> as a Bonus Action on your turn. Each time you use this after the first you gain 1 <strong>Rank of Exhaustion</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"alien-alien-battle-instincts","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1331,"endLine":1342},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Alien"}}}
{"_id":"a3d80eb42f2c457e","name":"Signature  Move","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>10th Level</strong> you may take a Long Rest to familiarize yourself with a specific <strong>Technique</strong> for constant use. Choose a <strong>Ki Technique</strong> that has a <em>Saving Throw</em> or an <em>Attack Roll</em>, you gain a <em>Static Bonus</em> to that <strong>Technique</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.\nYou may take a Long Rest and change your Signature Move.</p>\n<p>At <strong>17th Level</strong> you may designate 2 additional <strong>Techniques</strong> to gain this benefit.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-signature-move","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2905,"endLine":2911},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"a543bde0f5267ced","name":"Next Evolution","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: <em>Super Saiyan 2, Legendary Super Saiyan, or Controlled Super Saiyan</em> and <em>True Saiyan Rage</em> Feat</strong>\nYou learn to mix Super Saiyan and your Ozaru's Power into your base form, manifesting it into a new form. You gain the <em>Super Saiyan 4</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"next-evolution","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Super Saiyan 2, Legendary Super Saiyan, or Controlled Super Saiyan* and *True Saiyan Rage* Feat","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5592,"endLine":5598},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"a553a305c8c7467f","name":"Namekian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Wisdom</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The DNA of the noble Namekians flows through you. You gain their elastic limbs, Your Unarmed Strikes gains the reach property. Namekians are also known to regrow their own limbs. As an action you may spend 2 ki to heal 1 hit points and 30 ki points to regrow a lost limb.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-namekian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1582,"endLine":1586},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"a56046f1260b8cdd","name":"Superiority: Ki Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one class of <strong>Ki Technique</strong>: <em>Beam, Blast, Barrage</em>, or <em>Omni</em>. You gain +1 to <em>Static Bonus</em> when using this type of <strong>Ki Technique</strong>. At <strong>Level 7</strong> this becomes +2 and at <strong>Level 13</strong> you get to pick a second type of <strong>Ki Technique</strong> to gain this bonus.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 18</strong> you get an +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> that you can place on any class of <strong>Ki Technique</strong>, regardless of if you choose that category previously.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"yardratian-superiority-ki-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2184,"endLine":2189},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Yardratian"}}}
{"_id":"a644dfc2f1620469","name":"I won't give up!","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you are reduced to zero <strong>HP</strong> you may use your Reaction and roll any amount of your <strong>Hit Die</strong> and heal that amount.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"i-won-t-give-up","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6162,"endLine":6164},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"a681611fc8fbf27a","name":"Diagnostics and Soft Reset","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Android you do not need to sleep and can not be forced to fall asleep by any means.</p>\n<p>To benefit from a <em>Long Rest</em> you must instead go into a repair mode where your systems fix themself. You may do light activity during this 4 hour rest period, alternatively you may benefit from a Short Rest in 10 minutes.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"android-diagnostics-and-soft-reset","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1373,"endLine":1377},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Android"}}}
{"_id":"a69e73cace178743","name":"Divine Energy","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the <strong>Celestial Tag</strong> and all creatures without the <strong>Celestial</strong> or <strong>Infernal Tag</strong> or access to <strong>God Ki</strong> treat your <em>Passive Ki Stealth</em> and <em>Ki Stealth Checks</em> as 5 higher than it would actually be.</p>\n<p>You also count as a <strong>Supreme Kai</strong> for sake of the <em>Potara Earrings</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"divine-energy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Supreme Kai"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3670,"endLine":3681}}}}
{"_id":"a7b50cc1eeeb9585","name":"Hard Work","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>What they lack in flashy transformation earthlings make up for with an endless drive for greatness. You gain a <strong>Technique</strong> every time you <strong>Level-Up</strong> to 20 and 2 <strong>Techniques</strong> every level beyond. You also gain 1 additional <em>Training Boon</em> each time you have a <strong>Training Arc</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"earthling-hard-work","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":861,"endLine":862},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Earthling"}}}
{"_id":"aa56f3a704f27a9c","name":"Third Eye Awakening","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have become enlighnted in a way that has physically awakened a third eye on your forehead. You gain the following benefits.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your <strong>Power Bonus</strong> also boosts your <em>Perception</em> and <em>Sense Ki Skill Checks</em> as your third eye is sharpened alongside your body.</li>\n<li>Your <em>Critical Threat Range</em> is increased by 1.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"third-eye-awakening","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5896,"endLine":5902},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"aab26d2e90bb4818","name":"Heroic Features","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Gain 2 features from the <strong>Heroic Features List</strong>. Every time you get this <strong>Class Feature</strong> after the first time, you gain 1 additional <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-heroic-features","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2659,"endLine":2660},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"aacd9c65be4a31ca","name":"Extra attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beginning at <strong>5th Level</strong>, and again at <strong>11th</strong> and <strong>17th Level</strong>, you may make an additional attack as part of your <em>Attack Action</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-extra-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3184,"endLine":3186},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"ab189aade372c438","name":"Time Skip Features","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain access to these <strong>Features</strong> whenever you reach the <strong>Time Point Cost</strong> for that feature.</p>\n<h6>Time Skip</h6>\n<p><em>1 Time Point</em>\nThe user’s first steps to chrono mastery, the user stops time for brief moments. As a Bonus Action on your turn or as a <strong>Clash</strong> to any <strong>Technique</strong> you may spend <em>Time Points</em> to give all creatures but you the <em>Frozen in Time Condition</em> as well as grant you additional <em>Movement Speed</em> and <em>Action Economy</em>.</p>\n<p>If used as a <strong>Clash</strong>, the other <strong>Technique</strong> finishes its casting at the end of <em>Time Skip</em> unless you damage them or otherwise hender their ability to cast. You gain the following <em>Movement Speed</em> and <em>Action Economy</em> based on the amount of <em>Time Points</em> you spend:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>1 <em>Time Point</em>: 1 Bonus Action &amp; 10 Feet of Movement</li>\n<li>2 <em>Time Points</em>: 1  Action &amp; 20 Feet of Movement</li>\n<li>3 <em>Time Points</em>: 1 Action and 1 Bonus Action &amp; 30 Feet of Movement</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Alternatively you may expend 3 <em>Time Points</em> at the start of your turn to end the <em>Frozen in Time Condition</em> on yourself.</p>\n<h6>Stitch in Time</h6>\n<p><em>1 Time Point</em>\nAs an Action on your turn, you may peak into the timestream to see the past of a Person or Object that you are touching.\nThis ability allows you to rewind your or someone else's connection to the flow of time, allowing you to watch echoes of the past to see scenes of the past in perfect clarity. It is up to the <strong>DM</strong> to determine what you see.</p>\n<h6>Time Blink</h6>\n<p><em>2 Time Points</em>\nWhenever you would use your Movement for your turn you may spend your Reaction to vanish from the timestream momentarily.  You do not provoke <em>Attacks of Opprotunity</em> until the end of your turn.</p>\n<h6>Removed From Time</h6>\n<p><em>3 Time Points</em>\nThe user can remove himself from the prime material plane, temporarily allowing attacks to pass right through you. You are still visible and can still be seen and heard.</p>\n<p>As a Reaction on your turn whenever you are subject to an <em>Attack Roll</em> or forced to make a <em>Saving Throw</em>, you may cause all effects to miss you until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<h6>Time Cage</h6>\n<p><em>3 Time Points</em>\nChoose 1 creature or object within 60 feet. They must make a <em>Charisma Saving Throw</em> against your <strong>Omni Save DC</strong> or gain the <em>Frozen in Time</em> <strong>Condition</strong> until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<h6>Chronal Mastery</h6>\n<p><em>5 Time Points</em>\nThe user has complete mastery over time itself. As an Action you may touch 1 creature, completely reverse the last round of combat for the target. This reverses death, expended <strong>Resources</strong> such as <strong>HP, Ki,</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong>, as well as limited use <strong>Features</strong>.</p>\n<p>If used outside of combat the effect's scope increases to up to 1 minute.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-skip-features","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3475,"endLine":3528}}}}
{"_id":"ab50543627d2a606","name":"Demon","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 to any Ability Score</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your DNA is made up of entities of negative emotions, drawing powers from those who come from Other World. You gain a Demonic Ability of your choice from the Demon Race.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-demon","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1545,"endLine":1549},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"ac0ab5f161e3110e","name":"Powered-Up To The Limit","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional <strong>Power-Up Slot.</strong> <strong>Forms</strong> using this slot cost +2 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong>.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken an additional 2 times to reduce the additional <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong> by 1 each time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"powered-up-to-the-limit","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6291,"endLine":6297},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"ac1e34c601848728","name":"Hyper Reflexes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your brain is evolved to take on more information than others. You have 2 Reactions per round.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ceralians-hyper-reflexes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":830,"endLine":840},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ceralians"}}}
{"_id":"ac599d63d4960ea3","name":"Crusher","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are practiced in the art of crushing your enemies, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack that deals bludgeoning damage, you can move it 5 feet to an unoccupied space, provided the target is no more than one size larger than you.</li>\n<li>When you score a critical hit that deals bludgeoning damage to a creature, attack rolls against that creature are made with advantage until the start of your next turn.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"crusher","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5245,"endLine":5252},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"acc08a507ca9b7c5","name":"Brutal Critical","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can roll one additional <em>Damage Die</em> when determining the extra damage for a <strong>Critical Hit</strong> with a <em>Melee Attack Roll</em> or a <strong>Melee/Melee Weapon Technique</strong>.\nThis <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken up to three times.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"brutal-critical","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6093,"endLine":6098},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"acccefec9a0fd18b","name":"Power-Up Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <strong>Form</strong> you know, reduce the <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong> by 1, minimum of 1, while it is active in your <em>Power-Up Slot</em>.</p>\n<p>You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> no more than 3 times per <strong>Form</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"power-up-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6298,"endLine":6301},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"ace359079b3b84e8","name":"High-Speed Reactions","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Manuevers</strong> require 1 less <strong>Stamina</strong> to use, to a minimum of 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronin-high-speed-reactions","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1669,"endLine":1673},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Chronin"}}}
{"_id":"b016e75aef5d4977","name":"Heroic Features","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Gain 2 features from the <strong>Heroic Features List</strong>. Every time you get this <strong>Class Feature</strong> after the first time, you gain 1 additional <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-heroic-features","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3179,"endLine":3180},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"b0ceb21f8a4b0469","name":"Training to Wield the Z-Sword","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Attuning</strong> to the <em>Z-Sword</em> is an <strong>Ordeal</strong> by itself. This 8 hour <em>Ritual</em> leaves you with 1 <em>Rank of Exhaustion.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"training-to-wield-the-z-sword","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"ordeal","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"ordeal"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3341,"endLine":3352}}}}
{"_id":"b1a4827e9aa36f67","name":"Ki Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>20th Level</strong> once per Long Rest, when you hit enter <em>Ki Exhaustion</em> you may instead choose to regain half of your <strong>Maximum Ki</strong> as <strong>Temporary Ki</strong>. This <strong>Temporary Ki</strong> lasts for 1 minute of combat before dispelling. You may not gain <strong>Temporary Ki</strong> in any way while this <strong>Feature</strong> is ongoing.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blaster-ki-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2914,"endLine":2918},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Blaster"}}}
{"_id":"b205a09cfe5e471f","name":"Heavily Armored","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have trained to master the use of heavy armor, gaining the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency with heavy armor.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"heavily-armored","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5297,"endLine":5302},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"b3bd8fe1ab038f8a","name":"Combative Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest, you may initiate a <strong>Clash</strong> without spending <strong>Stamina</strong> or <strong>Ki</strong>. This becomes once per Short Rest at <strong>level 10</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"greys-combative-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1809,"endLine":1811},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Greys"}}}
{"_id":"b3ef5ae1e731710a","name":"Infernal Legacy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You slowly unlock the full power of the <em>Demon Realm</em>. You gain access to <em>Mashin-jin</em> <strong>Feats</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>1st Level</strong>, you know the <em>Thaumaturgy</em> <strong>Cantrip</strong>. When you reach <strong>3rd Level</strong>, you gain the <em>Hellish Rebuke</em> <strong>Spell</strong>. When you reach <strong>5th Level</strong>, you gain the <em>Fireball</em> <strong>Spell</strong>. These <strong>Spells</strong> are cast through the <strong>Mysticism Feature</strong> but can not be casted at a higher <strong>Spell Level.</strong></p>\n<p>At <strong>10th Level</strong> you may cast these spells at a higher <strong>Spell Level</strong> as if through the <strong>Mysticism Feature</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>15th Level</strong> you may add any 3 <strong>Spells</strong> that deal damage of 5th level or below to this feature.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"mashin-jin-infernal-legacy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":960,"endLine":968},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Mashin-jin"}}}
{"_id":"b50419d2e8688d1e","name":"Plot Armor","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest, when you are subject to a <em>Critical Hit</em> you may treat it as if it was not a <em>Critical Hit.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"plot-armor","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6285,"endLine":6288},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"b59e4d8d858191b8","name":"Assassin Techniques","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A number of times equal to your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> you may replace the <em>Damage Type</em> of a <strong>Technique</strong> to <em>Ki Damage.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"assassin-techniques","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Crane School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3368,"endLine":3370}}}}
{"_id":"b5a1cb039d677752","name":"Ki Control","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have gained an intimate knowledge of how to sense ki around you and hide your own from detection.</p>\n<h4>Sense Ki</h4>\n<p>As an Action on your turn, you may feel outwards for living creatures or creatures with a <em>Power Level</em> that are not <em>Concealing</em> their <em>Ki</em> or are an <em>Android</em>, <em>Cyborg</em>, or otherwise a <em>Construct</em>.</p>\n<p>Make a <em>Wisdom (Perception) Check</em> at a range listed below based on your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>. You have an inate sense of the location and <em>Power Level</em> of any creature you sense with this method so long as you hold <em>Concentration</em> and they are within your range.</p>\n<p>Creatures have a unique <em>Ki Signature</em> that you are capable of recognizing when felt at a later time. You may be able to feel similarities between the <em>Ki Signatures</em> of family members and particularly powerful individuals can even make their <em>Alignment</em> known upon sensing their <em>Ki Signature.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>At rank 1 you have a range of your current Continent</li>\n<li>At rank 2 you have a range of your current Planet</li>\n<li>At rank 3 you have a range of your current Solar System</li>\n<li>At rank 4 you have a range of your current Galaxy</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Conceal Ki</h4>\n<p>As an Action on your turn you may attempt to pool together all of your energy so that it can not be sensed. Make a <em>Wisdom (Ki Control) Check</em> to supress your <em>Power Level</em> and set a <strong>DC</strong> for any <em>Sense Ki Checks</em> against you. You may also lower your <em>Power Level</em> to any number below your current <em>Power Level</em>. These effects last so long as you hold <em>Concentration</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ki-control","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6178,"endLine":6198},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"b5bc6924dd869c18","name":"True Saiyan Rage","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/Mutant/Ancient</em></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites: <em>Oozaru's Fury</em>, Level 7+</strong>\nYou push your Ikari state to a further state, unleashing it into a level that causes your muscles to bulk up to a similar state that the Oozaru gives you. You gain the <em>&quot;Wrath of the Saiyans&quot;</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"true-saiyan-rage","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisites: *Oozaru's Fury*, Level 7+","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5585,"endLine":5591},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"b5cbbb78707cedb0","name":"Double Weapon Technique","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are fighting with two weapons, you may make an additional weapon attack with your offhand weapon when casting a Weapon Technique</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"double-weapon-technique","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6123,"endLine":6126},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"b651d30909c7a053","name":"Exoskeleton","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to your bone-like exoskeleton, you gain a bonus to your <strong>AC</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"arcosian-exoskeleton","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1431,"endLine":1433},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Arcosian"}}}
{"_id":"b65ba078d6975f70","name":"Egotistical Strength","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Complete Ultra Ego</strong>\nWhen you would transform into any <strong>Form</strong> that has: <em>Ultra Ego</em> in its name, it has its <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong> reduced by 1, minimum of 1. Additionally, you gain an additional <em>Destruction Die</em> at the end of your turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"egotistical-strength","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Complete Ultra Ego","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6024,"endLine":6028},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"b68017cbbfb87785","name":"Biotic Blueprint","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The design philosophy of your creation differs from scientist to scientist. Are you a complete being that has had traits hand picked from the races of the universe or are you perhaps an imperfect being that must absorb more beings to become the perfect life form.</p>\n<h5>Incomplete Creation:</h5>\n<p>Your journey is to become the ultimate lifeform. You Start with 2 Genetic Makeup features.</p>\n<p>You’ve been designed to improve you have the ability to absorb other life forms including other androids through a tail or an intergrated weapon within your body called <strong>Life Drain</strong> to make an unarmed strike. You decrease the damage step by 1 when dealing damage using <strong>Life Drain</strong> but you may choose to deal damage to their hit poitns or ki points. Dealing damage in this way gives you an amount of ki points equal to the damage dealt.</p>\n<p>Beyond absorbing them, you may additionally gain their skills and abilities by fulling intergrating them within you. You may target a creature using <strong>Life Drain</strong>. If you would bring a creature down to 0 hit points by a <strong>Life Drain</strong> attack, you may choose to absorb them into you. You may alternatively target a creature that is willing <strong>and not charmed</strong>, you may automatically absorb the creature as an action.</p>\n<p>You may integrate a number of creatures equal to half of your Constitution Modifier. When you would absorb a creature from <strong>Life Drain</strong>, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>You gain the benefit of an additional Genetic Makeup of the race you had absorbed. You do not gain the additional bonus to your Ability Score.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>You learn all techniques and languages of the assimilated, this will not improve a move you have if you already have it to a higher degree of mastery but if they have an improved version you do get it.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>If they have any ability scores higher than yours you may add +1 to those scores, this may increase it above a Ability Score maximum.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If none of their Ability Scores surpass yours you gain +1 to whichever Ability Score was their highest.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><p>You gain the <em>Fusion Tag</em> when you absorb a creature this way</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Artificial Warrior:</h5>\n<p>You are a warrior that had its genetic makeup cherry picked, You gain 3 Genetic Makeup features. You may pick the DNA Specialization Feat two additional times, ignoring all limitation</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-biotic-blueprint","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1478,"endLine":1511},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"b6b1d355438eda87","name":"Computer Eyes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your eyes are mechanical, granting you +3 on any <em>Perception Checks</em> involving sight. As an Action on your turn, you can see in high detail up to 1 mile so long as you hold <em>Concentration</em>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 10</strong> gain a new an improved scanner. This functions as true sight as long as the creature is not undead, has been dead for 5 hours, or is obscured by an external extreme temperature. This <strong>Feature</strong> can be activated and deactivated as an Action and it can be activated for a total of 1 hour per Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"android-computer-eyes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1366,"endLine":1372},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Android"}}}
{"_id":"b8316c41ca51ab08","name":"Just like base","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires:<em>Super Saiyan Grade 4</em> Power-Up</strong>\nYour mastery of the Super Saiyan form has led you down a path few can ever reach. Your Super Saiyan form has become your base body and rage and unrest are no longer required to use it.</p>\n<p>You always appear to be in the <em>Super Saiyan</em> <strong>Form</strong>, though you are not actually <strong>Transformed</strong>. You may no longer use the <em>Super Saiyan 1</em> <strong>Transformation</strong> or the <em>Grades 2-4</em> <strong>Power-Ups</strong> alongside it. You gain 1 <em>Rank of the Light-Weight Condition</em> so long as you are concious. Your <strong>Stamina</strong> also permanently increases by 2.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"just-like-base","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires:*Super Saiyan Grade 4* Power-Up","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5498,"endLine":5506},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"b8932ae72cfa1851","name":"Signature Move","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>13th Level</strong> you may take a Long Rest to familiarize yourself with a specific <strong>Technique</strong> for constant use. Choose a <strong>Ki Technique</strong> that has a <em>Saving Throw</em> or an <em>Attack Roll</em>, you gain a <em>Static Bonus</em> to that <strong>Technique</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n<p>You may take a Long Rest and change your <em>Signature Move</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-signature-move","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3191,"endLine":3204},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"b8bd43a68f07344e","name":"Alien","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 to any Ability Score</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You were created with extra terrestrial DNA. You gain resistances to a damage type of your choice, Youre are also granted access to the full power transformation at Level 5 and Once per long rest, you can enter the Enraged Condition as a bonus action on your turn. Each time you use this past the first you gain 2 level of exhaustion.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-alien","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1515,"endLine":1519},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"b8dd5dda3829bf47","name":"Piercer","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have achieved a penetrating precision in combat, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack that deals piercing damage, you can re-roll one of the attack’s damage dice, and you must use the new roll.</li>\n<li>When you score a critical hit that deals piercing damage to a creature, you can roll one additional damage die when determining the extra piercing damage the target takes.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"piercer","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5376,"endLine":5382},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"b97b5f1b6f4627da","name":"Second Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have become so attuned to a <strong>Transformation</strong> you may use it in a <strong>Power-Up Slot</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"second-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6319,"endLine":6320},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"b9839826ac28259b","name":"Aggressive Aura","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your aura has become so powerful that it pushes away attacks. Your <strong>AC</strong> increases by 1.</p>\n<p>This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken an amount of times equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"aggressive-aura","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6065,"endLine":6070},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"ba2aeb38a2409bb5","name":"Burning Soul","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to their supposed connection or perhaps some other strange genetic trait, Sekhmen-jin can choose to turn any <em>Ki Damage</em> they deal into <em>Fire Damage</em>. At <strong>Level 10</strong> this ignores <em>Resistance</em> and treats <em>Immunity</em> as <em>Resistance</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sekhmen-jin-burning-soul","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2145,"endLine":2148},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sekhmen-jin"}}}
{"_id":"ba6455ddb3a2bfaa","name":"Majin Regenerate","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your body is capable of reconstructing itself. As an Action you can heal yourself an amount equal to Ki points spent. You can spend <strong>Ki</strong> when you would hit 0 <strong>HP</strong> equal to the amount of <em>Damage</em> that would put you below 1, to instead drop to 1 <strong>HP</strong>.</p>\n<p>At <strong>Level 5</strong>, so long as you are not under the effects of <em>Ki Exhaustion,</em> you may spend a Bonus Action to regenerate a lost limb.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"majin-majin-regenerate","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1868,"endLine":1881},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Majin"}}}
{"_id":"bb92b3f3301c00e4","name":"Clash Instigator","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest you may initiate a <strong>Clash</strong> without expending <strong>Stamina</strong>.</p>\n<p>Taking this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> a second time makes it recharge on a Short Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"clash-instigator","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6099,"endLine":6105},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"bcaa35b475780a69","name":"Spirit Conversion","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you may artificially create <strong>Stamina</strong> for 15 <strong>Ki</strong> per <strong>Stamina</strong> that you create.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"spirit-conversion","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3446,"endLine":3447}}}}
{"_id":"bccd74ad815d0183","name":"True Namekian Split","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Namekians have the ability to permenantly split themselves into 2 diametricly opposed people.\nAt an action on your turn, you may split into 2. <strong>Class Levels, HP, KI,</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong> are split as evenly as possible amoung the now 2 unique entities.</p>\n<p>If these two entities were to fuse through Namekian Fusion then both characters are fully added together when one is assimilated.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"namekian-true-namekian-split","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1961,"endLine":1965},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Namekian"}}}
{"_id":"bd0c46947fb6678b","name":"Final dregs","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you reach Zero <strong>Stamina</strong> you gain 5 <strong>Temporary Stamina</strong> for 1 Minute. This <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> can be taken up to 3 times, increasing the amount to 10 and then 15.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"final-dregs","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6143,"endLine":6147},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"bdabb4da255da5ca","name":"Great Awakening","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires God Ki</strong></p>\n<p>If your <strong>Race</strong> has more than one <strong>God Form</strong> available you may gain one that you did <strong>not</strong> gain when you obtained <strong>God Ki.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"great-awakening","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Requires God Ki","tags":"trained feature; Angel"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3712,"endLine":3729}}}}
{"_id":"be78c8528025fbe7","name":"Battle Jacket Crafter","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Requires: Technology Skill</em>\nYou are a master at modifying armor, allowing you to add mechanical enhancements  to them. You may spend 8 hours and 50% of an armor's total <em>Zeni Cost</em> in supplies to permanently add a single effect to a piece of <em>Light Armor</em>. Each time a modification is added you add the expended Zeni to the armor's cost.</p>\n<p>This feat can be taken again twice allowing you to modify <em>Medium Armor</em> as well as add  an additional modification on <em>Light Armor</em>, and then allowing you to modify <em>Heavy Armor</em> as well as add an <em>additional</em> modification on <em>Light and Medium Armor</em>.</p>\n<p>Modifications that have limited uses recharge at dawn.\nModification options include:</p>\n<h5>Adrenaline Injector</h5>\n<p>*Requires: <strong>Battery Pack Class Feature***\nYou can now use your **Battery Pack Class Feature</strong> as if it were <strong>Stamina</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Buster Plates</h5>\n<p>You have installed new armor plating to reduce impacts. You may reduce all <em>Bludgeoning, Slashing, and Piercing Damage</em> by an amount equal to your <em>Intellegence Modifier.</em></p>\n<h5>Combat Systems</h5>\n<p>You gain one rank of the <em>Light-Weight Condition.</em></p>\n<h5>Defensive AI</h5>\n<p>You have developed an artifical intellegence that is design to help get you out of dange in combat. A number of times per day equal to half of your <em>Intellegence Modifier</em> per day you may use <strong>Wild Sense</strong> without expending <em><strong>Stamina</strong></em>.</p>\n<h5>Deflectors</h5>\n<p>You have installed new energy shields to dispel attacks. You may reduce all <em>Fire, Cold, Lightning, Radiant, and Ki Damage</em> by an amount equal to your <em>Intellegence Modifier.</em></p>\n<h5>Energy Overload</h5>\n<p>As an action on your turn you may enter the <em>Super-Charged Condition</em> for a number of rounds equal to your <em>Intellegence Modifier.</em></p>\n<h5>Enviroment Suit</h5>\n<p>You can breathe in space or underwater for a number of hours per day equal to your <em>Intellegence Modifier.</em></p>\n<h5>Light Weight Polymer</h5>\n<p>This modification allows you to reconstitute the armor with new materials. You may reduce the classification of a set of <em>Medium or Heavy Armor</em> by 1 step.</p>\n<p>(Heavy &gt; Medium &gt; Light)\nStrength Requirements for this armor also drop by 3, minimum 10.</p>\n<h5>Scanners</h5>\n<p>You have made a <strong>Rank 2 Scouter</strong> a part of the equipment. This scouter does not explode if it scans above it's rank.</p>\n<p>You may take this a second time to upgrade the scouter to <strong>Rank 4.</strong></p>\n<h5>Shields</h5>\n<p>You have developed energy shields that can protect you. A number of times per day equal to half of your <em>Intellegence Modifier</em> per day you may <strong>Block</strong> without expending <em><strong>Stamina</strong></em>.</p>\n<h5>Strength Augmenters</h5>\n<p>As an action on your turn you may enter the <em>Empowered Condition</em> for a number of rounds equal to your <em>Intellegence Modifier.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"battle-jacket-crafter","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Technology Skill; Requires: **Battery Pack Class Feature","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5142,"endLine":5195},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"bf2495022c075029","name":"Actor","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Skilled at mimicry and dramatics, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of your Current ability score maximum.</li>\n<li>You have an advantage on Charisma (Deception) and Charisma (Performance) checks when trying to pass yourself off as a different person.</li>\n<li>You can mimic the speech of another person or the sounds made by other creatures. You must have heard the person speaking, or heard the creature make the sound, for at least 1 minute. A successful Wisdom (Insight) check contested by your Charisma (Deception) check allows a listener to determine that the effect is faked.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"actor","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5207,"endLine":5212},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"bf93423cbfe904dc","name":"Weight Training","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>*This <strong>Feat</strong> may be taken once per **Ki Rank***</p>\n<p>Due to your determined weight and gravity training you are able to ignore the negatives of 1 rank of the <em>Heavy Weight Condition</em>, though you still have the condition. Each time you take this <strong>Feat</strong> you may ignore 1 additional rank of the condition.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"weight-training","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5102,"endLine":5107},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"bfffeb1e4ab13dc9","name":"Shield Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use shields not just for protection but also for offense. You gain the following benefits while you are wielding a shield:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you take the Attack action on your turn, you can use a bonus action to try to shove a creature within 5 feet of you with your shield.</li>\n<li>If you aren't incapacitated, you can add your shield's AC bonus to any Dexterity saving throw you make against a spell or other harmful effect that targets only you.</li>\n<li>If you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, you can use your reaction to take no damage if you succeed on the saving throw, interposing your shield between yourself and the source of the effect.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shield-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5413,"endLine":5421},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"c03c3ac652b3ba78","name":"Super Fighting Heroes","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A purple alien walks before his men eying each of them before their upcoming battle. &quot;Alright men, prepare yourself to engage and steel your hearts!&quot; The captain strikes an excentric pose that seems to encourage his team before leading them into yet another successful mission.</p>\n<p>Heroes are leaders that have learned that the only way to success is through your team. Leading with the ability to buff their allies and inspire them to greater heights, heroes are always welcome on a battlefield.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-super-fighting-heroes","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3073,"endLine":3078},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"c0a1ecedb32bf4d4","name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may attack an additional time as part of the <em>Attack Action</em>. You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> an amount of times equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"extra-attack","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6113,"endLine":6116},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"c0bef7a02fe24ada","name":"Eager Fighter","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You’re always ready to fight! Gain +3 to <em>Initiative</em>, and activating a <strong>Transformation</strong> now only takes a Bonus Action.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"eager-fighter","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6127,"endLine":6133},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"c1640faea80dd0f7","name":"Meditative State","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action on your turn, you may enter a special meditation stance to regain 10x your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> in <strong>Ki</strong>. You may extend this meditation into your Bonus Action to gain an additional 50% of that amount.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"greys-meditative-state","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1821,"endLine":1830},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Greys"}}}
{"_id":"c1910a15b08b4a73","name":"Majin","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Constitution</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The blood of the mystical majin courses through your veins, your body becomes elastic and has the consistency of rubber, your unarmed strikes gain the reach property. Along with this your body has been engineered to repair itself, as an action you may spend ki to heal at a 2:1 ratio. With your malleable body you also gain the ability to squeeze into a space at least 1 inch wide.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-majin","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1568,"endLine":1572},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"c7d9b1ad4517f598","name":"Metamoran Fusion Expert","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Fusion is even stronger than before! Designate a <em>Metamorian Fusion</em> that you have become, you gain 50 <strong>Fusion HP</strong> and <strong>Fusion Ki</strong> for the Duration of that fusion. This <strong>Fusion HP and Ki</strong> are treated as normal <strong>HP and Ki</strong> but are not calculated on the fusees when the <em>Metamorian Fusion</em> ends.</p>\n<p>You automatically pass any <em>Skill Checks</em> to fuse into the designated <em>Fusion</em>. This <strong>Feat</strong> can be taken multiple times but can not be used on the same fusion.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"metamoran-fusion-expert","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5991,"endLine":5996},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"c8297501329e6984","name":"Indomitable","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can reroll a <em>Saving Throw</em> that you fail with a bonus to the roll equal to your <strong>Character Level</strong>. If you do so, you must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"indomitable","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6175,"endLine":6177},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"c9b62976e404fdc7","name":"Heroic Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong> you gain a single <strong>Heroic Feature</strong>. This does not count as gaining a <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> as a <strong>Class Feature</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"konatsian-heroic-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":917,"endLine":929},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Konatsian"}}}
{"_id":"cacc4697e7f1685e","name":"Advanced Demonic Bloodline","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain 1 <strong>Feature</strong> from the <em>Demonic Ability</em> <strong>Racial Feature</strong> that you do not already have.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"advanced-demonic-bloodline","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5854,"endLine":5861},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"cbfe23cd3527f147","name":"Lucky","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have inexplicable luck that seems to kick in at just the right moment.</p>\n<p>You have 3 luck points. Whenever you make an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, you can spend one luck point to roll an additional d20. You can choose to spend one of your luck points after you roll the die, but before the outcome is determined. You choose which of the d20s is used for the attack roll, ability check, or saving throw.</p>\n<p>You can also spend one luck point when an attack roll is made against you. Roll a d20 and then choose whether the attack uses the attacker's roll or yours.</p>\n<p>If more than one creature spends a luck point to influence the outcome of a roll, the points cancel each other out; no additional dice are rolled.</p>\n<p>You regain your expended luck points when you finish a long rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"lucky","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5325,"endLine":5334},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"cc7a20ce9ddf62d1","name":"Red Eyes Of The Ceralian","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Ceralians are born with a strange quirk, a single hyper-evolved red eye. You gain access to the <em>Red Eye</em> <strong>Forms</strong> as laid out in the <strong>Forms Chapter</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ceralians-red-eyes-of-the-ceralian","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":828,"endLine":829},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ceralians"}}}
{"_id":"ce16a4fe9a16ddd1","name":"Slow Fall","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may use your reaction to reduce any <em>Fall Damage</em> you take by 5x your <strong>Character Level.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"slow-fall","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6321,"endLine":6323},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"cef90d0255e641e7","name":"Modular Stamina Engine","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>They actually did it, they made a perfect generator! You regain 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> at the start of every round. You may take the <em>General Upgrade</em> <strong>Feat</strong> and use every point to increase this bonus by 1 a single time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"android-modular-stamina-engine","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1378,"endLine":1380},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Android"}}}
{"_id":"d1fa059087160791","name":"Energy Reserve","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long or Short Rest, you can use an Action and regain 4d12 + your <em>Constitution Modifier</em> <strong>Ki.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"energy-reserve","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6140,"endLine":6142},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"d21997dc25bbc352","name":"Unarmored Movement","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at <strong>2nd Level</strong>, your speed increases by 10 feet while you are not wearing armor or wielding a shield. This bonus increases when you reach certain Martial Artist levels, as shown in the Martial Artist table.</p>\n<p>Additionally, you gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling during the move.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-unarmored-movement","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2655,"endLine":2658},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"d27eacddb59dad38","name":"Primal Legend","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Full Power Super Saiyan</em> and *Super Saiyan 4.***\nUsing your full-power and Super Saiyan 4 has become second nature and can maintain without a second slot. You may use Super Saiyan-Full Power and Super Saiyan 4 as a **Combination Transformation</strong> known as <em>Super Saiyan 4 Full Power</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"primal-legend","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Full Power Super Saiyan* and *Super Saiyan 4.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5762,"endLine":5779},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"d362bbc86adc7549","name":"Superiority: Awakening","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to awaken your internal potential, be it physical or spiritual. You gain 1 of the following:</p>\n<h4>Superiority: Ki</h4>\n<p>Choose one class of <em><strong>Techniques</strong></em>: Beam, Blast, Barrage, or Omni. You gain a +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> when using this type of <strong>Ki Technique</strong>. At <strong>Level 7</strong> this becomes a +2 <em>Static Bonus</em> and at <strong>Level 13</strong> you get to pick a second available type of <strong>Technique</strong> to gain this bonus. At <strong>Level 18</strong> you get a +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> that you can place on any available type of <strong>Technique</strong>, regardless of if you choose that category previously.</p>\n<h4>Superiority: Melee/Weapons</h4>\n<p>Choose one class of <em><strong>Techniques</strong></em>: Melee or Weapons. You gain a +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> added to all <em>Attack Rolls</em> and <em><strong>Techniques</strong></em> of that type. This increases to +2 at <strong>Level 7</strong>, +3 at <strong>Level 13</strong>, and +4 at <strong>Level 19</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"superiority-awakening","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5903,"endLine":5912},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"d3a8f2476a06714d","name":"Sateery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Wisdom or +1 Charisma</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The DNA of the mysterious Sateery race grants you access to one branch of magic. You also gain resistance to ki damage but have disadvantage to all spell saving throws.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-sateery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1604,"endLine":1608},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"d3d910414ce73636","name":"The Secret of the Self-indulgent","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires God Ki</strong></p>\n<p>You have begun the true undertaking of becoming a God of Destruction. You gain the <em>Ultra Ego Omen</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"the-secret-of-the-self-indulgent","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Requires God Ki","tags":"trained feature; God of Destruction"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3691,"endLine":3702}}}}
{"_id":"d3e283834f15e3dd","name":"Telepathy","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have been taught to reach outward to communicate telepathically. You may now communicate telepathically with any creature that you can sense through <em>Sense Ki.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"telepathy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Guardian of the Dragon Balls"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3613,"endLine":3627}}}}
{"_id":"d5e79435eb5cbdaa","name":"Majin Absorption","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 10</strong>, Majins have  access to the legendary power of Majin Buu himself.  Candy Beam is added to your <strong>Learnable Technique List</strong>, and it's <strong>Ki Rank</strong> matches your own, and you can benefit from its second ability.</p>\n<h5>Candy Beam</h5>\n<p><em>Rank X Ki Technique</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ki Cost:</strong>  30 Ki</li>\n<li><strong>Range:</strong>  60 Feet</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 Minute (concentration)</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong>  Omni</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Target one object or creature in your range, they must make a <em>Constitution Saving Throw</em>, turning the object or target (and all of their equipment) into a choice of food of your choice on a failure. Creatures affected by this have their <em>Base Walk Speed</em> set to 5 feet and their <em>Unarmed Strike Damage Die</em> turned into 1d4 if not already lower. Candy Creatures also can’t use <strong>Techniques/Spells</strong>. A Candy Creature may attempt the <em>Saving Throw</em> again as an Action on their turn to end this effect.</p>\n<p>If a creature grapples the candy creature, they may attempt to eat them as an Action. Deal <em>Damage</em> equal to your <em>Unarmed Damage Die</em> + your <em>Constitution Modifier</em>, if you reduce the target to zero in this manner you eat them. If you eat the candy creature you restore your own <strong>Ki</strong> and <strong>Stamina</strong> by the amount the Candy Creature had remaining, if you are a <em>Majin</em> then you may CHOOSE to assimilate the target gaining the following effects:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You learn all <strong>Techniques</strong> and <em>Languages</em> of the assimilated,. If the assimilated has more <em>Mastery Ranks</em> in a <strong>Technique</strong> that you know, you gain those <em>Mastery Ranks</em>.</li>\n<li>If they have any <strong>Ability Scores</strong> higher than yours you may add +1 to those <strong>Ability Scores</strong>, this may increase it above your <em>Ability Score Maximum</em>.<ul>\n<li>If none of their <strong>Ability Scores</strong> surpass yours you gain +1 to whichever <strong>Ability Score</strong> was their highest.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>You gain visual quirks resembling the entities that you assimilated.</li>\n<li>You may only gain this benefit a number of times equal to your <em>Constitution Modifier</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"majin-majin-absorption","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1882,"endLine":1910},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Majin"}}}
{"_id":"d646e0a2636cb43a","name":"S-cell Awakening","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have felt the rush of battle, your blood boils at the thought. You dig down into a depth of power unlike anything you’ve felt before and you explode in a golden light.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Pure Super Saiyan</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"s-cell-awakening","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5680,"endLine":5685},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"d71b4300999e44c7","name":"Trained By A Master","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>“Yes, We’ll spend this hour on good old napping. Work hard, Study well and eat and sleep plenty… that’s the turtle hermit way to learn!”</em>\nTraining under a master is the most effective way to learn. A master must be above your current level by 3 levels. While training under a master you gain the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain 6 <strong>Training Boons</strong>.<ul>\n<li>You may spend 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong> to gain a <em>Mortal</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> that your <em>Master</em> knows</li>\n<li>You may spend 3 <strong>Training Boons</strong> to gain a <em>Alien/Divine</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> that your <em>Master</em> knows</li>\n<li>You may spend 2 <strong>Training Boons</strong> to gain a <strong>Technique</strong> that is a single <strong>Ki Rank</strong> higher than you are, so long as you fit any other <strong>Requirements</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"trained-by-a-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"arc","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":26,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Training under a master is the most effective way to learn. A master must be above your current level by 3 levels. While training under a master you gain the following","tags":"training arc"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3245,"endLine":3258}}}}
{"_id":"d7906be856ab2945","name":"Limit Breaker","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>18th Level</strong> you have pushed your body to unimaginable heights. Increase your Strength and Constitution <strong>Ability Scores</strong> and <em>Ability Score Maximums</em> by 2.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-limit-breaker","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3032,"endLine":3033},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"d82dc084f7c14d3b","name":"Animal Nature","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to comprehend and verbally communicate with beasts for the duration. The knowledge and awareness of many beasts is limited by their intelligence, but at minimum, beasts can give you information about nearby locations and monsters, including whatever they can perceive or have perceived within the past day. You might be able to persuade a beast to perform a small favor for you, at the GM's discretion.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beastmen-animal-nature","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":764,"endLine":765},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Beastmen"}}}
{"_id":"d847d2d6984fbea2","name":"Dark Pride","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Dark Energy Power-up</em> and <em>An Age Old Prophecy</em> Feat</strong>\nYour Dark Energy has mutated your Super Saiyan state, accessing a level beyond regular Super Saiyan.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Super Saiyan 3 Full Power</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dark-pride","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Dark Energy Power-up* and *An Age Old Prophecy* Feat","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5700,"endLine":5723},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"d86037ab57d061ba","name":"Grey’s","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Strength or +1 Constitution</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The stoic Grey’s DNA has given you their overflowing strength. All your Ability Score maximums increase by 2. Once per long rest you may initiate a clash using half ki. You also learn how to use meditation to regain ki, as an action on your turn you may enter a special meditation stance, floating just over the ground. You regain (5 times your Ki rank) Ki.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-greys","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1556,"endLine":1560},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"d8fe0887886bb384","name":"Limit Breaker","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires &quot;Realm of the Gods&quot; and Super Saiyan 4</strong>\nYou have became so used to your transformation combonations that you can even mix the peaks of mortal and gods. You can use Super Saiyan God as a <strong>Power-Up</strong> while <em>Super Saiyan 4</em> is active.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"limit-breaker","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires \"Realm of the Gods\" and Super Saiyan 4","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5599,"endLine":5605},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"d9cb7733be8a31cf","name":"Ogre","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<ul>\n<li>+1 Constitution</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your Ogre durability has surfaced allowing you to fight with the tenacity of the Otherworld.</p>\n<p>As an action on your turn you may spend stamina to gain Xd12, where X is equal to the stamina spent, and gain Temporary HP equal to the total. This health disappears after 1 hour or whenever you gain additional Temporary HP.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bio-android-ogre","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1592,"endLine":1598},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Bio-Android"}}}
{"_id":"daa8cb8e976df160","name":"Unlock Latent Energy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You passively pull forth more energy from your spirit than normal. Increase your <strong>Ki</strong> by 2 times your level, you also gain +2 <strong>Ki</strong> every <em>level-up</em> onward.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"unlock-latent-energy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6376,"endLine":6378},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"dcf19aeb6a8eb8c1","name":"Legendary Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Wrestling Control</em> and <em>Berserker Super Saiyan 2***\nAs you draw out more power in your controlled state your hair spikes up straight and lighting arcs around you occasionally. You gain the *Controlled Super Saiyan 2</em> **Transformation</strong>.</p>\n<p>**This Feat must be obtained through <em>Training Boons</em> or by completing an *Ordeal***</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"legendary-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Wrestling Control* and *Berserker Super Saiyan 2; This Feat must be obtained through *Training Boons* or by completing an *Ordeal","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5733,"endLine":5739},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"dd453b256cf2a19a","name":"Superiority: Unarmed","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are naturally adept at hand-to-hand combat. You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> added to all <em>Unarmed Strikes</em> and <strong>Melee Techniques</strong> . This increases to +2 at <strong>Level 7</strong>, +3 at <strong>Level 13</strong>, and +4 at <strong>Level 19</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ogre-superiority-unarmed","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1022,"endLine":1025},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Ogre"}}}
{"_id":"ddffca3f88513470","name":"Deadly absorption:","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Prerequisite: Incomplete Creation</p>\n<p>Your <strong>Life Drain</strong> now deals your Unarmed Damage and you may now use Weapon Techniques with your <strong>Life Drain</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"deadly-absorption","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Prerequisite: Incomplete Creation","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5914,"endLine":5918},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"deeba20781629fe8","name":"Signature Move","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>11th Level</strong> you may take a Long Rest to familiarize yourself with a specific <strong>Technique</strong> for constant use. Choose a <strong>Ki Technique</strong> that has a <em>Saving Throw</em> or an <em>Attack Roll</em>, you gain a <em>Static Bonus</em> to that <strong>Technique</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank</strong>.</p>\n<p>You may take a Long Rest and change your <em>Signature Move</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-signature-move","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2688,"endLine":2691},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"deeee023b9523f09","name":"Thick skinned","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You immediately gain <strong>Maximum HP</strong> equal to the maximum amount of your latest <strong>Hit Die</strong> + your Constitution Modifier. You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> more than once to a maximum of half of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"thick-skinned","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6367,"endLine":6369},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"df9e1fc1b56e1c24","name":"Heroic Strength","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your strength of spirit pushes past normal limitations. When you attack with an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or a <em>Weapon Attack Roll</em> using <strong>Strength</strong> that you are proficient with, you may replace the <em>Damage Die</em> with the <em>Damage Die</em> shown in the <strong>Heroic Strength Table</strong> above.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hero-heroic-strength","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3123,"endLine":3126},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Hero"}}}
{"_id":"dfa03ba2b5671086","name":"An age-old prophecy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>**Requires: *S-Cell Awakening***\nDrawing from the golden light inside always seemed like a small fraction of its potential, you dig deep inside you and break through that wall, flooding yourself in power. You are the legend reborn. You are the Super Saiyan of Legend.</p>\n<p>You gain the <em>Legendary Super Saiyan</em> <strong>Transformation</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"an-age-old-prophecy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *S-Cell Awakening","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5686,"endLine":5692},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"e10625d96093adf0","name":"Metamagic","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Requires the ability to cast at least 1 leveled spell</em></p>\n<p>Your practice of the magical arts has granted you the ability to twist your spells to suit your needs. You gain two of the following <em>Metamagic Options</em> of your choice. You gain another one each time you take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> after the first.</p>\n<p>You can use only one <em>Metamagic Option</em> on a <strong>Spell</strong> when you cast it, unless otherwise noted.</p>\n<h4>Metamagic Options</h4>\n<h5>Careful Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that forces other creatures to make a <em>Saving Throw</em>, you can protect some of those creatures from the spell’s full force. To do so, you spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> and choose a number of those creatures up to your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> (minimum of one creature). A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its <em>Saving Throw</em> against the <strong>Spell</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Distant Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that has a range of 5 feet or greater, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to double the range of the spell.</p>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that has a range of touch, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to make the range of that <strong>Spell</strong> 30 feet.</p>\n<h5>Empowered Spell</h5>\n<p>When you roll damage for a <strong>Spell</strong>, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to reroll a number of the <em>Damage Dice</em> up to your <em>Charisma Modifier</em> (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p>\n<p>You can use <strong>Empowered Spell</strong> even if you have already used a different <em>Metamagic Option</em> during the casting of the <strong>Spell</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Extended Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to double its duration, to a maximum duration of 24 hours.</p>\n<h5>Heightened Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that forces a creature to make a saving throw to resist its effects, you can spend 3 <strong>Stamina</strong> to give one target of the <strong>Spell</strong> Disadvantage on its first <em>Saving Throw</em> made against the <strong>Spell</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Quickened Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that has a casting time of 1 Action, you can spend 2 <strong>Stamina</strong> to change the casting time to 1 Bonus Action for this casting.</p>\n<h5>Subtle Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong>, you can spend 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> to cast it without any somatic or verbal components.</p>\n<h5>Twinned Spell</h5>\n<p>When you cast a <strong>Spell</strong> that targets only one creature and doesn’t have a range of self, you can spend a number of <strong>Stamina</strong> equal to the spell’s level to target a second creature in range with the same <strong>Spell</strong> (1 <strong>Stamina</strong> if the spell is a cantrip).</p>\n<p>To be eligible, a <strong>Spell</strong> must be incapable of targeting more than one creature at the <strong>Spell’s</strong> current level. For example, magic missile and scorching ray aren’t eligible, but ray of frost is.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"metamagic","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires the ability to cast at least 1 leveled spell","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6233,"endLine":6276},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e19eac7ab12b32b2","name":"Explosive Temper","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your DNA is strong but slightly unstable. Your anger can get ahead of you sometimes but it certainly can come in useful on the battlefield. Once per long rest you may enter the <em>Enraged Condition</em> as a Bonus Action.</p>\n<p>&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"hybrids-explosive-temper","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2365,"endLine":2375},"contentCategory":"subraceFeature","grantedBy":"Hybrids"}}}
{"_id":"e1b362588553a445","name":"Martial Arts Superiority","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master of the battle field and gain special benefits while in combat.</p>\n<h4>Tactics</h4>\n<p>You learn 2 <em>Martial Arts Maneuvers</em> of your choice. When you use the Attack Action to make a <em>Weapon Attack</em> or <em>Unarmed Strike</em> you may choose to use a <em>Martial Arts Maneuvers</em> with it. Many <em>Martial Arts Maneuvers</em> enhance an attack in some way. You can use only one <em>Martial Arts Maneuvers</em> per attack.</p>\n<h4>Superiority Dice</h4>\n<p>You have 2 <em>Superiority Dice</em>, which are d4s. A <em>Superiority Die</em> is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended <em>Superiority Dice</em> when you finish a Short or Long Rest. You may roll additional <em>Superiority Dice</em> by spending 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> per Die.\nTaking this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> again gives you either 2 new <em>Martial Arts Manuevers</em>, 2 more <em>Superiority Dice</em> or to increase the size of your <em>Superiority Diee</em> by 1 step to a max of d12.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-arts-superiority","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6221,"endLine":6232},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e2008dfd04f59322","name":"Superiority Improvement","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>10th Level</strong>, your <em>Superiority Dice</em> turn into d10s. At <strong>18th Level</strong>, they turn into d12s.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"martial-artist-superiority-improvement","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2685,"endLine":2687},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Martial Artist"}}}
{"_id":"e2e02b8154113f2b","name":"Ki Sense Amplification","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on <em>Sense Ki Checks</em> and can <em>Sense Ki</em> 1 range step higher then usual.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Continent &gt; Planet &gt; Solar System &gt; Galaxy &gt; Universe</em></li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"ki-sense-amplification","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3430,"endLine":3434}}}}
{"_id":"e36ccd671b549145","name":"Speed Force","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're quick, some may even call you &quot;The Fastest Thing Alive&quot;. At <strong>1st Level</strong> you gain the <em>Mach 1</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong> and you gain access to each subsequent <em>Speed Force</em> <strong>Power-Up</strong> each time you <strong>Rank Up</strong>.</p>\n<h5>Speed Force Power-Ups</h5>\n<p>You move faster than anyone else and nothing can get in your way. You gain <em>Mach 1</em> at <strong>Level 3</strong> and it <strong>Ranks Up</strong> each time your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> increases. You do not lose access to previous Power-Ups.</p>\n<p>When you use these <strong>Power-Ups</strong> outside of <strong>Combat</strong>, you pay the <strong>Stamina</strong> cost every minute. While this <strong>Power-Up</strong> is active you may travel vertically or horizontally across any surface, such as up walls or across water so long as you do not end your turn there, falling if you do.</p>\n<h6>Mach 1</h6>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Melee/Melee Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <em>Melee/Melee Weapon</em> <strong>Techniques</strong>.</li>\n<li>Double your <em>Walk</em> and <em>Fly Speed</em>.</li>\n<li>1 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h6>Mach 10</h6>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain +1 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Melee/Melee Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <em>Melee/Melee Weapon</em> <strong>Techniques</strong>.</li>\n<li>Triple your <em>Walk</em> and <em>Fly Speed</em>.</li>\n<li>You gain an additional attack as part of the <em>Attack Action</em> or when making <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> as an Action.</li>\n<li>You do not provoke <em>Attacks of Opprotunity.</em></li>\n<li>2 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h6>Mach 100</h6>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain +2 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Melee/Melee Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <em>Melee/Melee Weapon</em> <strong>Techniques</strong>.</li>\n<li>Quadruple your <em>Walk</em> and <em>Fly Speed</em>.</li>\n<li>You gain an additional attack as part of the <em>Attack Action</em> or when making <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> as an Action.</li>\n<li>You gain an additional Reaction each round.</li>\n<li>You do not provoke <em>Attacks of Opprotunity.</em></li>\n<li>4 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h6>Light Speed</h6>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain +2 <em>Static Bonus</em> to <em>Melee/Melee Weapon Attack Rolls</em> and <em>Melee/Melee Weapon</em> <strong>Techniques</strong>.</li>\n<li>Quintuple (5x) your <em>Walk</em> and <em>Fly Speed</em>.</li>\n<li>You gain an additional 2 attacks as part of the <em>Attack Action</em> or when making <em>Basic Ki Blasts</em> as an Action.</li>\n<li>You gain an additional Reaction each round.</li>\n<li>You do not provoke <em>Attacks of Opprotunity.</em></li>\n<li>6 <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"speedster-speed-force","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2233,"endLine":2285},"contentCategory":"subraceFeature","grantedBy":"Speedster"}}}
{"_id":"e42fdc9381ae56ac","name":"Pressure Points","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have figured out a way to stop the enemy’s ki from flowing. You may choose to deal any <em>Damage</em> from an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or <strong>Melee Technique</strong> to the enemy’s <strong>Ki</strong> instead of their <strong>HP</strong>, this must be declared before damage is rolled.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"pressure-points","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6302,"endLine":6307},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e4f76fa8aeb8bc13","name":"Flexible Weapon Technique","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are using a <em>Finesse</em> or <em>Ranged Weapon</em>, you may instead use <em>Dexterity</em> as your <strong>Weapon Technique</strong> <em>Ability Score</em> instead of <em>Strength</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"flexible-weapon-technique","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6148,"endLine":6149},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e57b49c17ce2db47","name":"Turtle Style Disciple","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The <em>Static Bonus</em> from the <em>Turtle Style</em> <strong>Stance</strong> is increased by 1.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"turtle-style-disciple","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Turtle School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3406,"endLine":3409}}}}
{"_id":"e6169e4a04410f53","name":"Consecutive ki blasts","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may attack an additional time as part of the <em>Ki Blast Action</em>. You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> more than once to a maximum of half of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"consecutive-ki-blasts","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6110,"endLine":6112},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e6cfeb57cf5aad8d","name":"Defensive Tactics","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Each time you take this Heroic Feature, reduce the Stamina Cost for <em>Block, Clash, Deflection, Interception,</em> and <em>Wild Sense</em> by 1 (minimum 1).</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"defensive-tactics","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6117,"endLine":6119},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"e7616fb0bd3bb688","name":"Quicker then the rest","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your <em>Base Walk Speed</em> is 2x your race’s <em>Base Walk Speed</em> and you can <em>Dash</em> as a Bonus Action on your turn. While you are under the effects of the <em>Dash Actin</em>, you may travel vertically or horizontally across any surface, such as up walls or across water so long as you do not end your turn there, falling if you do.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"speedster-quicker-then-the-rest","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2231,"endLine":2232},"contentCategory":"subraceFeature","grantedBy":"Speedster"}}}
{"_id":"e88cd56fdb795dac","name":"Predatory Rage","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action on your turn you can enter the <em>Enraged Condition</em>, this condition lasts for a number of rounds equal to your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>.</p>\n<p>You may use this feature once per Long Rest, each additional time you choose to use this feature you gain 2 <em>Ranks of Exhaustion</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"sekhmen-jin-predatory-rage","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2149,"endLine":2153},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Sekhmen-jin"}}}
{"_id":"e899110410dc2726","name":"Dragon Ball Creation","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Must be a Dragon Clan Namekian</strong>\nYou have learned the ancient ways and can create a <em>Set of Dragon Balls</em>. A <em>Set of Dragon Balls</em> can be created by taking anywhere from 2 to 7 equal sized stone spheres that are unblemished and a small statute of the <em>Wishing Dragon</em> you wish to create and preforming an 8 hour ritual praying to Zalama to bestow his blessing on the orbs. These orbs return to stone if you die.</p>\n<p>You may create a set of <em>Red Star Star Dragon Balls</em> of your choice, regardless of your choice it grants a single wish and recharges after 1 year by <em>Earth Standards.</em> Whenever you obtain <strong>God Ki</strong> you may increase the <em>Wish Count</em> by 1 or halve the <em>Recharge Time</em> of your <em>Set of Dragon Balls.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"dragon-ball-creation","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Must be a Dragon Clan Namekian","tags":"trained feature; Guardian of the Dragon Balls"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3588,"endLine":3593}}}}
{"_id":"e9275ddb9e05f251","name":"Embodinent of Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>20th Level</strong> you push your <em>Dragon Soul</em> to the absolute limit. When you activate your <em>Dragon Soul</em> you may choose to empower it, doubling your <em>Static Bonus</em> for the duration.\nYou may use this ability once per Long Rest.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"bruiser-embodinent-of-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3034,"endLine":3045},"contentCategory":"classFeature","grantedBy":"Bruiser"}}}
{"_id":"e94d47cdb3077db9","name":"Time Blink","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>2 Time Points</em>\nWhenever you would use your Movement for your turn you may spend your Reaction to vanish from the timestream momentarily.  You do not provoke <em>Attacks of Opprotunity</em> until the end of your turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-blink","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3497,"endLine":3501}}}}
{"_id":"ec447abf6a8582d1","name":"Telepathic","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You awaken the ability to mentally connect with others, granting you the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You can speak telepathically to any creature you can see within 60 feet of you. Your telepathic utterances are in a language you know, and the creature understands you only if it knows that language. Your communication doesn't give the creature the ability to respond to you telepathically.</li>\n<li>You can cast the <em>Detect Thoughts</em> spell, requiring no stamina or components, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it this way again. Your spellcasting ability for the spell is the ability increased by this feat. If you have spell slots of 2nd level or higher, you can cast this spell with them.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"telepathic","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5472,"endLine":5478},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"ed40f5e1c2671516","name":"The Warm-Up Is Over","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Upon removing <em>Weighted Gear</em>, you gain an extra +1 to all <strong>Ability Scores</strong> for the duration of the benefit. This can be taken up to 3 times, increasing the bonus by +1 each time.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"the-warm-up-is-over","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6358,"endLine":6361},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"ed6bafd5358980d7","name":"Demonic Ability","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You possess an ability of your choice based on your hellish nature.</p>\n<h5>Dark Magic</h5>\n<p>You gain access to 1 branch of magic of your choice as if through the <em>Mysticism</em> <em><strong>Class Feature</strong></em>, additionally you may use <em>Constitution</em> as your <em>Spell Casting Modifier</em> for the <em>Mysticism</em> <em><strong>Class Feature</strong></em>.</p>\n<h5>Demonic Wings</h5>\n<p>You possess a pair of bat-like wings that protrude from your back granting you a <em>Fly Speed</em> of 15x your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n<h5>Elementalist</h5>\n<p>Choose one <em>Damage Type</em> from the list below, this can not be changed later, anytime you cast a <strong>Technique</strong> you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> equal to it's <strong>Rank</strong> to change it's <em>Damage Type</em> to your chosen <em>Damage Type</em>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fire</li>\n<li>Cold</li>\n<li>Lightning</li>\n<li>Thunder</li>\n<li>Force</li>\n<li>Psychic</li>\n<li>Poison</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>Esoteric Gift</h5>\n<p>You gain 1 <em>Esoteric Art</em> from the <em>Esoteric Arts</em> <strong>Class Feature.</strong></p>\n<h5>Fiendish Power</h5>\n<p>Whenever you make an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or <strong>Melee Technique</strong> you may spend <strong>Stamina</strong> to give yourself a <strong>Static Boost</strong> equal to the amount spent for that casting. You may not spend more than half of your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em>, rounded up, in <strong>Stamina</strong> in this manner for a single attack roll.</p>\n<h5>Hardened Body</h5>\n<p>You are naturally tougher than others, you gain a bonus to <strong>AC</strong> equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n<h5>Unstable Biology</h5>\n<p>You have the ability to break down your physical structure on a whim to avoid harm. Your <strong>Wild Sense Manuever</strong> can now be used on <em>Strength</em> and <em>Constitution Saving Throws</em> as well to completly ignore effects on a success, if there would still be an effect.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"demon-demonic-ability","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1746,"endLine":1783},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Demon"}}}
{"_id":"f01f3e5624c489ba","name":"Solo Training","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>&quot;There is no better master of me than myself&quot;</em>\nTraining alone allows you to develop your own style more effectively. When training alone you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You (A) gain 3 <em>Ranks of Mastery</em> to put into <em><strong>Techniques</strong></em> you know or (B) gain 1 additional <strong>Training Boon</strong></li>\n<li>You gain one <strong>Training Boon</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Alternatively you may replace both of those options to gain 1 <strong>Technique</strong> of one <strong>Ki Rank</strong> higher than you currently are.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"solo-training","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"arc","boonCost":0,"durationWeeks":26,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"training arc"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3214,"endLine":3230}}}}
{"_id":"f0f0461d9c5fb41c","name":"Transformation Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one <strong>Form</strong> you know, reduce the <strong>Stamina Upkeep</strong> by 1 (minimum 1) while it is active in your <em>Transformation Slot</em>.</p>\n<p>You may take this <strong>Heroic Feature</strong> no more than 3 times per <strong>Form</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"transformation-mastery","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6370,"endLine":6375},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"f1527c1792c8595e","name":"Time Cage","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>3 Time Points</em>\nChoose 1 creature or object within 60 feet. They must make a <em>Charisma Saving Throw</em> against your <strong>Omni Save DC</strong> or gain the <em>Frozen in Time</em> <strong>Condition</strong> until the start of your next turn.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"time-cage","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Time Skip"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3509,"endLine":3514}}}}
{"_id":"f2245c5f21741ab0","name":"Skulker","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are an expert at slinking through shadows. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can try to hide when you are lightly obscured from the creature from which you are hiding.</li>\n<li>When you are hidden from a creature and miss it with a ranged weapon attack, making the attack doesn't reveal your position.</li>\n<li>Dim light doesn't impose disadvantage on your Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"skulker","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5432,"endLine":5438},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f2e28b6b41855ae6","name":"Firearm Expert","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Thanks to extensive practice with Firearms, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You ignore the loading quality of firearms with which you are proficient.</li>\n<li>Being within 5 feet of a hostile creature doesn’t impose disadvantage on your ranged attack rolls.</li>\n<li>When you use the Attack action and attack with a one handed weapon, you can use a bonus action to attack with a pistol you are holding.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"firearm-expert","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5238,"endLine":5244},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f35c1c4876bf5a16","name":"Z-Soul","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest, you may give yourself Advantage on an Attack Roll or impose Disadvantage on a <em>Saving Throw</em> that you force.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"z-soul","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6382,"endLine":6389},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"f3835b78fbd5a1ca","name":"Millenial Learning Curve","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Chronins have unique brain chemistry to support their extremely long lifespans of thousands of years, due to this they are able to compartmentalize specific knowledge so that it can be remembered and improved on easily.</p>\n<p>At <strong>1st Level</strong> you gain 3 <em>Skill, Tool, or Item Proficiencies</em> of your choice. Each time your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> increases you gain an additional proficiency of your choice. You may instead gain <em>Expertise</em> in a <em>Skill</em> you already have proficiency in.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"chronin-millenial-learning-curve","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1681,"endLine":1694},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Chronin"}}}
{"_id":"f4989ac43bcea2e5","name":"Divine Combination","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6/Ancient/Mutant</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Realm of the Gods</strong>\nYou may use your <strong>Forms</strong> from the <strong>Realm of the Gods Feat</strong> as a <strong>Combination Transformation</strong> known as <em>Super Saiyan God Super Saiyan</em> or shortened as <em>Super Saiyan Blue.</em></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"divine-combination","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Realm of the Gods","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5527,"endLine":5533},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f4c23ce153d06073","name":"Powerful Ki","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may gain a <em>Rank of Exhaustion</em> to gain the <em>Super-Charged Condtion</em> for a number of rounds equal to your <strong>Ki Rank.</strong></p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"powerful-ki","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"class","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6289,"endLine":6290},"contentCategory":"heroicFeature"}}}
{"_id":"f4d746053e60ee7b","name":"Divine Resilience","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires God Ki</strong></p>\n<p>You have toughened your body through extensive use of God Ki. <em>Destruction Damage</em> is no longer unreducable when it hits you. You may never reduce <em>Destruction Damage</em> to zero.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"divine-resilience","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires God Ki","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5097,"endLine":5101},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f5b238daf0f69b94","name":"Egotistical Vigor","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: Egostitical Strength</strong>\nYour destruction burns with even more vigor and adds it to the power of your <em>Destruction</em>. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you would use <strong>Fighting Spirit</strong>, you gain an additional amount of <strong>Temporary HP</strong> or <strong>Temporary Ki</strong> points equal to half your <strong>Character Level</strong>, rounded up.</li>\n<li>When you would use <strong>Destroy</strong>, you deal an additional damage equal to half your <strong>Character Level</strong>, rounded up.</li>\n<li>When you would use <strong>Neverending Destruction</strong>, you gain additional <strong>Temporary Stamina</strong> equal to 1/4 of your <strong>Character Level</strong>, rounded up.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You may pick this <strong>Feat</strong> multiple times, when you do, you choose one of these benefits to double the benefit's amount. You may not choose a benefit more than once.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"egotistical-vigor","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Egostitical Strength","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":6029,"endLine":6039},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f6236d13e41d9e70","name":"Spirit Control","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At <strong>Level 1</strong> you gain 1 <em>Spirit Control</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> of your choice. You also gain an additional <em>Spirit Control</em> <strong>Trained Feature</strong> each time your <strong>Ki Rank</strong> increases.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"yardratian-spirit-control","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2194,"endLine":2195},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Yardratian"}}}
{"_id":"f6913534b71b7e7b","name":"Mystical Mimicry","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're ability to shape shift is so incredible that it allows you to mimic another's very DNA.</p>\n<p>As a Reaction to seeing a creature activate a <strong>Form</strong> you may memorize that <strong>Form</strong> for your own use, even if it is a <strong>Racial Form</strong>. You must have <strong>God Ki</strong> to copy a <strong>Godly Form.</strong>\nYou keep this specific <strong>Form</strong> and may activate it at a later form, if you were to use this <strong>Feature</strong> again you may replace your current memorized <strong>Form</strong>, ending the <strong>Form</strong> if it was active.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"neko-majin-mystical-mimicry","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2035,"endLine":2041},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Neko Majin"}}}
{"_id":"f71853419033db24","name":"Resilient","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one ability score. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increase the chosen ability score by 1, to a maximum of your current Ability Score Maximum.</li>\n<li>You gain proficiency in saving throws using the chosen ability.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"resilient","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5389,"endLine":5394},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f79401f1db54234e","name":"Golden Great Ape","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Requires: <em>Super Saiyan 4</em> and <em>Saiyan Elite</em> Feat.</strong>\nYou no longer need to make control checks for using Super Saiyan while using Great Ape.  While using <em>Great Ape</em> you may now use <em>Super Saiyan 2</em> but make <em>Berserk Checks</em> at disadvantage while it is active.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"golden-great-ape","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: *Super Saiyan 4* and *Saiyan Elite* Feat.","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5637,"endLine":5641},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"f7d5643d60424c54","name":"Angelic Energy","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Due to the strange energy flowing through you, creatures without <strong>God Ki</strong> treat your <em>Passive Ki Stealth</em> and <em>Ki Stealth Checks</em> as 5 higher than it would actually be.</p>\n<p>You gain the <strong>Celestial Tag</strong> and count as a <em>Kai</em> for the purpose of features such as the <em>Potara Earrings</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"shinling-angelic-energy","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1256,"endLine":1260},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Shinling"}}}
{"_id":"f9515e5d110c0c3d","name":"Evolutionary Tactics","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are driven by your instincts to improve and adapt to survive. You gain a <strong>Technique</strong> every time you <strong>Level-Up</strong> to 20 and 2 <strong>Techniques</strong> every level beyond. You also gain 1 additional <em>Training Boon</em> each time you have a <strong>Training Arc</strong>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"beastmen-evolutionary-tactics","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":759,"endLine":763},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Beastmen"}}}
{"_id":"fa831098a8ffc75f","name":"Gates of Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Arcosions have a strange life span, being born into their final form before descending into a weakened state until they can handle the full force of their own power. You gain access to <em>Arcosion</em> <strong>Feats</strong> and Arcosion <strong>Forms</strong> as laid out in the <em><strong>Forms</strong></em> chapter.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"arcosian-gates-of-power","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1437,"endLine":1449},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Arcosian"}}}
{"_id":"faca916f2982aabf","name":"Alien resilience","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have no need to breathe and can safely travel through the vacuum of space. You have <em>Resistance</em> to <em>Cold Damage</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"arcosian-alien-resilience","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1423,"endLine":1426},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Arcosian"}}}
{"_id":"fda2b4998c977bd3","name":"Polearm Master","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you take the Attack action and attack with only a glaive, halberd, quarterstaff, or spear, you can use a bonus action to make a melee attack with the opposite end of the weapon. This attack uses the same ability modifier as the primary attack. The weapon's damage die for this attack is a d4, and it deals bludgeoning damage.</li>\n<li>While you are wielding a glaive, halberd, pike, quarterstaff, or spear, other creatures provoke an opportunity attack from you when they enter the reach you have with that weapon.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"polearm-master","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5383,"endLine":5388},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"fda416742c199d04","name":"Blinding Divinity","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>U7/U6</em></p>\n<p><strong>Requires: Perfected Divinity</strong>\nYou have reached the penultimate level for <em>Super Saiyan Blue</em>. You may now apply <em>Super Saiyan Grade 4</em> to the <em>Super Saiyan Blue</em> <strong>Combination Transformation</strong>.</p>\n<p>When you would end this <strong>Power-Up</strong>, your aura bursts out in a moment of uncontrolled power. You gain +6 <strong>Power Bonus</strong> until the end of your next turn. Afterwards gaining 3 <em>Ranks of Exhaustion</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"blinding-divinity","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"Requires: Perfected Divinity","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":5558,"endLine":5567},"contentCategory":"feat"}}}
{"_id":"fdc8a959412f3fde","name":"Cybernetic Features","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<h5>Battery Powered</h5>\n<p>You do not suffer negative effects from not eating. You are incapable of regaining <strong>Ki</strong> from a <strong>Technique</strong> or <strong>Item</strong>, instead have a 4 <strong>Ki</strong> per round regen, this increases by 4 again at <strong>Levels 4, 7, 10, 13, 16,</strong> and <strong>19.</strong></p>\n<h5>Infinite Stamina Engine</h5>\n<p>You regain 1 <strong>Stamina</strong> at the start of each of your turns as your internal core gives you energy constantly. This can not be improved in any way.</p>\n<h5>Artificial Limitation Remover</h5>\n<p>Increase 2 <em>Ability Score Maximums</em> of your choice by 2.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"cyborg-cybernetic-features","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":2292,"endLine":2309},"contentCategory":"subraceVariant","grantedBy":"Cyborg"}}}
{"_id":"ff54cbfc7112f43d","name":"Saiyan instincts","type":"feat","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your <em>Proficiency Bonus</em> to <em>Initiative</em> and can act normally on the first round of combat even when <em>Suprised</em>.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"saiyans-saiyan-instincts","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"requirements":"","type":{"value":"feat","subtype":""},"prerequisites":{"items":[],"level":0,"repeatable":false},"properties":[]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":1083,"endLine":1084},"contentCategory":"racialFeature","grantedBy":"Saiyans"}}}
{"_id":"ff62df381359345d","name":"Minor Spirit Control","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p><em>Guardians</em> tend to be spiritually gifted and have up to 3 random <em>Spirit Control</em> <strong>Trained Features</strong> available to teach.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"minor-spirit-control","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Guardian of the Dragon Balls"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3611,"endLine":3612}}}}
{"_id":"ff72627a239e9a9e","name":"Forced Spirit Fission","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to revert energy back to it's original form. In practice this is usually used to seperate fusions and release stolen energy.</p>\n<p>As a Reation you when land an <em>Unarmed Strike</em> or <strong>Melee Technique</strong> or as an Action when you can touch someone, You may spend <strong>Stamina</strong>  to do one of the following additional effects at the end of your attack:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Targets with the <strong>Fusion Tag</strong> are sperated into their base components for 5 <strong>Stamina</strong>.</li>\n<li>You may reduce the <strong>Ki</strong>, <strong>Temporary Ki</strong>, and any other forms of <strong>Ki</strong> the target may have by 10x the amount of <strong>Stamina</strong> that you spend when you use this <strong>Trained Feature.</strong></li>\n<li>If a target has taken any <strong>Ki</strong>, <strong>HP</strong>, or <strong>Stamina</strong> from a creature in the last minute and the target still has them, you return them to their original owner.</li>\n</ul>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"forced-spirit-fission","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"","tags":"trained feature; Spirit Control"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3416,"endLine":3423}}}}
{"_id":"ffc57a7837ba4da9","name":"Evil Containment Wave","type":"training","img":"systems/dragons-and-ballz/icons/svg/items/feature.svg","system":{"description":{"value":"<h2><em>Special Rank Technique</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Casting Cost:</strong>  5 <strong>Hit Die</strong>, this can reduce you below zero <strong>Hit Die</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Casting Time:</strong>  1 Action</li>\n<li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> 1 Jar (or any other sealable container) and 1 Sealing Tag that cost 10,000 Zeni each</li>\n<li><strong>Casting Time:</strong> 1 Action</li>\n<li><strong>Range:</strong>  30 Feet</li>\n<li><strong>Chargeable?:</strong>          No</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong>          Instantaneous</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong>  Omni</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You use an empty bottle and seal a creature within range that you can see. The target of this <strong>Technique</strong> must make a <em>Constitution Saving Throw</em>, with advantage during <strong>Combat</strong>. Creatures who fail are immediately sealed within the jar and can only be let free if a creature spends an Action to unseal them.</p>\n<p>While in the <em>Jar</em>, a creature gains the <em>Paralyzed Condition</em>, even if they would be immune to it. They do not age, do need to eat, breathe, or sleep. The <em>Jar</em> has 1 <strong>Hit Point</strong> and has an <strong>AC</strong> of 5. If the <em>Jar</em> is within a creature's inventory, the <em>Jar</em> cannot be targeted.\n<strong>Hit Die</strong> expended to cast this <strong>Technique</strong> can never be recovered. You die at the completion of this <strong>Technique</strong> if your <strong>Hit Die</strong> would hit Zero or below.</p>\n","chat":""},"identifier":"evil-containment-wave","source":{"custom":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook"},"category":"trainedFeature","boonCost":1,"durationWeeks":0,"kiRank":null,"requirements":"Prerequisites:** 1 Jar (or any other sealable container) and 1 Sealing Tag that cost 10,000 Zeni each","tags":"trained feature; Turtle School"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"flags":{"dragons-and-ballz":{"handbook":{"chapter":"Dragons and BallZ Handbook","startLine":3385,"endLine":3402}}}}
